{"id":"greece-horiatiko-psomi","name":"Χωριάτικο ψωμί","nameAlt":"Country Bread","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g flour · 70ml water · 5g yeast · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 840ml water · 60g yeast · 24g salt","method":"Mix flour, water, yeast, and salt into a dough. Knead for 10 minutes until smooth. Let it rise for 30 minutes until doubled. Shape into a loaf and place on a baking tray. Bake at 200°C for 30 minutes until golden. Cool before slicing.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 50g · fat 2g","storage":"Store at room temperature for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Score the top before baking for crust.","pairsWith":"olive oil · cheese · soup","trivia":"Bread is central to every Greek meal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-fava","name":"Φάβα","nameAlt":"Yellow Split Pea Purée","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"puree","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"meze","ingredients":"80g yellow split peas · 30g onion · 10ml olive oil · 5ml lemon juice · 2g salt","ingredients12":"960g yellow split peas · 360g onion · 120ml olive oil · 60ml lemon juice · 24g salt","method":"Rinse the split peas and place in a pot with water. Bring to a boil and simmer for 30 minutes until soft. Add chopped onion and cook for 10 minutes more. Drain excess water if needed. Mash or blend until smooth. Stir in olive oil, lemon juice, and salt. Serve warm or at room temperature.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 30g · fat 6g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Blend for smoother texture.","pairsWith":"bread · olives · wine","trivia":"Fava is especially famous on the island of Santorini.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-kreatopita","name":"Κρεατόπιτα","nameAlt":"Meat Pie","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"pie","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"family","ingredients":"80g ground beef · 40g phyllo pastry · 30g onion · 1 egg · 10ml olive oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"960g ground beef · 480g phyllo pastry · 360g onion · 12 egg · 120ml olive oil · 24g salt","method":"Cook onion in olive oil over medium heat for 5 minutes. Add ground beef and cook until browned, about 6 minutes. Remove from heat and mix with beaten egg. Layer phyllo pastry in a greased dish. Spread the meat mixture evenly. Cover with more phyllo and brush with oil. Bake at 180°C for 35 minutes until golden. Let cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"50 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 26g · carbs 28g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let rest before cutting for clean slices.","pairsWith":"salad · yogurt · wine","trivia":"Meat pies vary widely across Greek regions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-psarosoupa","name":"Ψαρόσουπα","nameAlt":"Fish Soup","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g fish · 50g potato · 30g carrot · 30g onion · 10ml olive oil · 5ml lemon juice · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g fish · 600g potato · 360g carrot · 360g onion · 120ml olive oil · 60ml lemon juice · 24g salt","method":"Place fish in a pot with water and bring to a simmer. Add chopped potato, carrot, and onion. Cook on medium heat for 25 minutes until vegetables are tender. Remove fish, debone, and return meat to the pot. Add olive oil and lemon juice. Season with salt and cook for 5 minutes more. Serve hot.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 20g · fat 12g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use firm white fish for best results.","pairsWith":"bread · salad · white wine","trivia":"Fish soup is common in coastal regions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-horta","name":"Χόρτα","nameAlt":"Boiled Greens","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"vegetable","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g wild greens · 10ml olive oil · 5ml lemon juice · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1440g wild greens · 120ml olive oil · 60ml lemon juice · 24g salt","method":"Wash the greens thoroughly. Bring a pot of water to a boil. Add greens and cook for 10 minutes until tender. Drain well and transfer to a plate. Drizzle with olive oil and lemon juice. Sprinkle with salt. Serve warm or at room temperature.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":120,"nutrition":"protein 4g · carbs 10g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overcook to keep color bright.","pairsWith":"fish · bread · olives","trivia":"Horta includes many types of wild greens.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-soutzoukakia","name":"Σουτζουκάκια","nameAlt":"Spiced Meatballs in Sauce","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"meatball","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"family","ingredients":"120g ground beef · 30g onion · 50g tomato · 10ml olive oil · 2g cumin · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1440g ground beef · 360g onion · 600g tomato · 120ml olive oil · 24g cumin · 24g salt","method":"Mix ground beef with chopped onion, cumin, and salt. Shape into small oblong meatballs. Heat olive oil in a pan and brown the meatballs for 6 minutes. Add chopped tomato and simmer on low heat for 20 minutes. Stir occasionally until sauce thickens. Serve hot.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 15g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Shape meatballs evenly for even cooking.","pairsWith":"rice · bread · salad","trivia":"Soutzoukakia have origins linked to Asia Minor.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-paximadia","name":"Παξιμάδια","nameAlt":"Twice-Baked Bread","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g flour · 70ml water · 5g yeast · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 840ml water · 60g yeast · 24g salt","method":"Mix flour, water, yeast, and salt into a dough. Knead for 8 minutes until smooth. Let it rise for 30 minutes. Shape into loaves and bake at 180°C for 25 minutes. Remove and slice into pieces. Return to oven and bake again at 150°C for 20 minutes until dry. Cool completely before storing.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 48g · fat 2g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 2 weeks.","chefNotes":"Second bake ensures long shelf life.","pairsWith":"cheese · olives · tomatoes","trivia":"Paximadia are traditional Greek rusks.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-kakavia","name":"Κακαβιά","nameAlt":"Fisherman’s Fish Soup","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"coastal","ingredients":"150g mixed fish · 40g potato · 30g carrot · 30g onion · 10ml olive oil · 5ml lemon juice · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g mixed fish · 480g potato · 360g carrot · 360g onion · 120ml olive oil · 60ml lemon juice · 24g salt","method":"Place fish in a pot with water and bring to a gentle simmer. Add chopped potato, carrot, and onion. Cook on medium heat for 25 minutes until vegetables are tender. Remove fish, debone carefully, and return flesh to the pot. Add olive oil and lemon juice. Season with salt and simmer for 5 minutes. Serve hot.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 24g · carbs 18g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use a mix of small fish for deeper flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · white wine · salad","trivia":"Kakavia is considered one of the oldest Greek soups.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-kourabiedes","name":"Κουραμπιέδες","nameAlt":"Almond Butter Cookies","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cookie","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"60g flour · 40g butter · 20g sugar · 20g almond · 2g vanilla","ingredients12":"720g flour · 480g butter · 240g sugar · 240g almond · 24g vanilla","method":"Cream butter and sugar together until fluffy. Add vanilla and mix well. Stir in flour and ground almonds to form a dough. Shape into small cookies. Place on a baking tray. Bake at 180°C for 20 minutes until lightly golden. Cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 25g · fat 22g","storage":"Store in airtight container for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Dust with powdered sugar after baking.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · milk","trivia":"Kourabiedes are a traditional Greek Christmas treat.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-melomakarona","name":"Μελομακάρονα","nameAlt":"Honey Spice Cookies","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cookie","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"60g flour · 20ml olive oil · 20ml honey · 20g sugar · 2g cinnamon · 2g orange zest","ingredients12":"720g flour · 240ml olive oil · 240ml honey · 240g sugar · 24g cinnamon · 24g orange zest","method":"Mix flour, olive oil, honey, sugar, cinnamon, and orange zest into a dough. Shape into oval cookies. Place on a baking tray. Bake at 180°C for 25 minutes until golden. Drizzle with extra honey while warm. Let cool before serving.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 4g · carbs 45g · fat 12g","storage":"Store at room temperature for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Soak lightly in honey syrup for extra flavor.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · milk","trivia":"Melomakarona are a staple of Greek Christmas celebrations.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-ladopsomo","name":"Λαδόψωμο","nameAlt":"Olive Oil Bread","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g flour · 70ml water · 10ml olive oil · 5g yeast · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 840ml water · 120ml olive oil · 60g yeast · 24g salt","method":"Mix flour, water, olive oil, yeast, and salt into a dough. Knead for 10 minutes until smooth. Let it rise for 30 minutes. Shape into a loaf and place on a baking tray. Bake at 190°C for 30 minutes until golden. Cool before slicing.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":270,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 48g · fat 6g","storage":"Store at room temperature for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Brush with olive oil before baking for a soft crust.","pairsWith":"cheese · olives · soup","trivia":"Olive oil breads are common in Mediterranean diets.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-kolokithokeftedes","name":"Κολοκυθοκεφτέδες","nameAlt":"Zucchini Fritters","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"fritter","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"meze","ingredients":"100g zucchini · 40g feta cheese · 20g flour · 10ml olive oil · 2g dill · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g zucchini · 480g feta cheese · 240g flour · 120ml olive oil · 24g dill · 24g salt","method":"Grate the zucchini and squeeze out excess moisture. Mix with feta, flour, dill, and salt. Shape into small patties. Heat olive oil in a pan over medium heat. Fry patties for 4 minutes on each side until golden. Drain on paper and serve warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 18g · fat 16g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Squeeze zucchini well to avoid soggy fritters.","pairsWith":"tzatziki · salad · wine","trivia":"Zucchini fritters are popular on Greek islands.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-gemista","name":"Γεμιστά","nameAlt":"Stuffed Vegetables","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stuffed","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"family","ingredients":"1 tomato · 1 bell pepper · 60g rice · 30g onion · 10ml olive oil · 2g parsley · 2g salt","ingredients12":"12 tomato · 12 bell pepper · 720g rice · 360g onion · 120ml olive oil · 24g parsley · 24g salt","method":"Cut tops off tomato and pepper and scoop out the insides. Chop the flesh and mix with rice, onion, olive oil, parsley, and salt. Fill the vegetables with the mixture. Place in a baking dish with a little water. Bake at 180°C for 60 minutes until vegetables are tender. Serve warm.","cookTime":"70 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 50g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Add potatoes to the tray for extra flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · feta · salad","trivia":"Gemista means “stuffed” in Greek.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-tyropitakia","name":"Τυροπιτάκια","nameAlt":"Mini Cheese Pies","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"party","ingredients":"40g phyllo pastry · 40g feta cheese · 1 egg · 10ml olive oil","ingredients12":"480g phyllo pastry · 480g feta cheese · 12 egg · 120ml olive oil","method":"Crumble feta and mix with beaten egg. Cut phyllo into strips and brush with olive oil. Place filling on each strip and fold into triangles. Arrange on a baking tray. Bake at 180°C for 25 minutes until golden. Serve warm.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 22g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Keep phyllo covered while working.","pairsWith":"salad · yogurt · tea","trivia":"Tyropitakia are popular at gatherings.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-skordalia","name":"Σκορδαλιά","nameAlt":"Garlic Potato Dip","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"dip","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"meze","ingredients":"100g potato · 5g garlic · 10ml olive oil · 5ml lemon juice · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g potato · 60g garlic · 120ml olive oil · 60ml lemon juice · 24g salt","method":"Boil the potato in salted water for 15 minutes until tender. Drain and mash until smooth. Add crushed garlic and mix well. Stir in olive oil and lemon juice. Season with salt and mix until creamy. Serve at room temperature.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":200,"nutrition":"protein 4g · carbs 30g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Adjust garlic to taste.","pairsWith":"bread · fish · vegetables","trivia":"Skordalia is often served with fried fish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-milopita","name":"Μηλόπιτα","nameAlt":"Apple Cake","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"80g apple · 40g flour · 20g sugar · 1 egg · 10g butter · 2g cinnamon","ingredients12":"960g apple · 480g flour · 240g sugar · 12 egg · 120g butter · 24g cinnamon","method":"Peel and slice the apple. Beat egg and sugar until fluffy. Mix in flour and melted butter. Fold in apple slices and cinnamon. Pour batter into a greased dish. Bake at 180°C for 35 minutes until set. Cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 45g · fat 10g","storage":"Store at room temperature for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use sweet apples for best flavor.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · milk","trivia":"Milopita is a simple homemade dessert.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-halva","name":"Χαλβάς","nameAlt":"Semolina Dessert","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pudding","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"40g semolina · 20g sugar · 10ml olive oil · 5g raisin · 2g cinnamon","ingredients12":"480g semolina · 240g sugar · 120ml olive oil · 60g raisin · 24g cinnamon","method":"Heat olive oil in a pan over medium heat. Add semolina and stir continuously for 5 minutes until golden. Add water and sugar carefully and stir. Cook until thick, about 5 minutes. Mix in raisins and cinnamon. Transfer to a mold and let set. Serve at room temperature.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 4g · carbs 45g · fat 10g","storage":"Store at room temperature for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Stir constantly to prevent lumps.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · fruit","trivia":"Halva is eaten during fasting periods in Greece.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-moussaka","name":"Μουσακάς","nameAlt":"Layered Eggplant and Meat Casserole","aliases":["Mousakas"],"course":"main","type":"casserole","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"family","ingredients":"150g eggplant · 100g ground beef · 50g tomato · 50ml milk · 20g flour · 20g butter · 30g onion · 5g garlic · 5ml olive oil · 2g cinnamon · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g eggplant · 1200g ground beef · 600g tomato · 600ml milk · 240g flour · 240g butter · 360g onion · 60g garlic · 60ml olive oil · 24g cinnamon · 24g salt","method":"Slice the eggplant and fry in olive oil on medium until golden, about 5 minutes. Cook the onion and garlic in a pan until soft, about 4 minutes. Add ground beef and cook until browned, about 6 minutes. Stir in chopped tomato, cinnamon and salt, then simmer for 10 minutes. In another pan, melt butter, add flour and whisk for 2 minutes. Pour in milk and cook until thickened, about 5 minutes. Layer eggplant, meat sauce and béchamel in a dish. Bake at 180°C for 40 minutes until golden.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 30g · fat 32g","storage":"Refrigerate in a sealed container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let it rest before slicing for cleaner layers.","pairsWith":"greek salad · red wine · bread","trivia":"Moussaka is considered Greece’s national dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-souvlaki","name":"Σουβλάκι","nameAlt":"Grilled Meat Skewers","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"skewer","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"150g pork · 10ml olive oil · 5ml lemon juice · 3g oregano · 2g salt · 1 pita bread","ingredients12":"1800g pork · 120ml olive oil · 60ml lemon juice · 36g oregano · 24g salt · 12 pita bread","method":"Cut pork into cubes and marinate with olive oil, lemon juice, oregano and salt. Let it sit for at least 15 minutes. Thread the meat onto skewers evenly. Grill over medium heat for about 10 minutes, turning often. Warm the pita bread briefly on the grill. Remove the meat once browned and cooked through. Serve the skewers with warm pita.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":430,"nutrition":"protein 32g · carbs 25g · fat 20g","storage":"Store cooked meat in the fridge for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Soak wooden skewers in water before grilling.","pairsWith":"tzatziki · pita · tomato","trivia":"Souvlaki dates back to ancient Greece.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-gyros","name":"Γύρος","nameAlt":"Rotisserie Meat Wrap","aliases":["Yiros"],"course":"main","type":"wrap","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"120g pork · 1 pita bread · 30g tomato · 30g onion · 30g yogurt · 5ml olive oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1440g pork · 12 pita bread · 360g tomato · 360g onion · 360g yogurt · 60ml olive oil · 24g salt","method":"Season pork slices with salt and olive oil. Cook in a hot pan for about 8 minutes until browned. Warm the pita bread for 2 minutes. Slice tomato and onion thinly. Spread yogurt on the pita. Add cooked pork and vegetables. Wrap tightly and serve warm.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 35g · fat 22g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can refrigerate filling for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use high heat for crispy edges on the meat.","pairsWith":"fries · tzatziki · cola","trivia":"Gyros means “turn” referring to the rotating spit.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-tzatziki","name":"Τζατζίκι","nameAlt":"Yogurt Cucumber Dip","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"dip","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g yogurt · 50g cucumber · 5ml olive oil · 5ml lemon juice · 2g garlic · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g yogurt · 600g cucumber · 60ml olive oil · 60ml lemon juice · 24g garlic · 24g salt","method":"Grate cucumber and squeeze out excess water. Mix yogurt with garlic and salt. Add cucumber and stir well. Pour in olive oil and lemon juice. Mix until smooth. Chill in the fridge for 10 minutes before serving.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":120,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 8g · fat 7g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Drain cucumber well to avoid watery dip.","pairsWith":"pita · grilled meat · salad","trivia":"Tzatziki is also popular across the Balkans.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-spanakopita","name":"Σπανακόπιτα","nameAlt":"Spinach Feta Pie","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"pie","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"family","ingredients":"100g spinach · 50g feta · 1 phyllo sheet · 10ml olive oil · 20g onion · 1 egg · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g spinach · 600g feta · 12 phyllo sheet · 120ml olive oil · 240g onion · 12 egg · 24g salt","method":"Cook onion in olive oil until soft, about 4 minutes. Add spinach and cook until wilted, about 3 minutes. Remove from heat and mix with feta and egg. Lay phyllo sheet and brush with oil. Add filling and fold into shape. Bake at 180°C for 30 minutes until crisp. Let cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 25g · fat 20g","storage":"Store in fridge for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Keep phyllo covered to prevent drying.","pairsWith":"salad · yogurt · tea","trivia":"Spanakopita is a staple in Greek bakeries.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-dolmades","name":"Ντολμάδες","nameAlt":"Stuffed Vine Leaves","aliases":["Dolmas"],"course":"starter","type":"stuffed","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"6 vine leaves · 50g rice · 20g onion · 5ml olive oil · 5ml lemon juice · 2g dill · 2g salt","ingredients12":"72 vine leaves · 600g rice · 240g onion · 60ml olive oil · 60ml lemon juice · 24g dill · 24g salt","method":"Cook onion in olive oil until soft, about 4 minutes. Add rice and stir for 2 minutes. Pour in a little water and cook until partly tender, about 8 minutes. Mix in dill and salt. Place filling onto vine leaves and roll tightly. Arrange in a pot and add water. Simmer on low heat for 30 minutes. Drizzle with lemon juice before serving.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 35g · fat 7g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overfill or they will burst.","pairsWith":"yogurt · lemon · bread","trivia":"Dolmades are common across Mediterranean cuisines.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-greek-salad","name":"Χωριάτικη Σαλάτα","nameAlt":"Greek Village Salad","aliases":["Horiatiki"],"course":"side","type":"salad","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"80g tomato · 50g cucumber · 30g feta · 20g olive · 5ml olive oil · 2g oregano · 2g salt","ingredients12":"960g tomato · 600g cucumber · 360g feta · 240g olive · 60ml olive oil · 24g oregano · 24g salt","method":"Cut tomato and cucumber into chunks. Slice olives if needed. Combine in a bowl. Add feta on top. Drizzle olive oil over the salad. Sprinkle oregano and salt. Toss lightly and serve fresh.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":200,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 10g · fat 14g","storage":"Best eaten fresh, store up to 1 day.","chefNotes":"Use ripe tomatoes for best flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · wine · grilled meat","trivia":"Traditional Greek salad has no lettuce.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-pastitsio","name":"Παστίτσιο","nameAlt":"Greek Baked Pasta","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"pasta","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"family","ingredients":"100g pasta · 100g ground beef · 50g tomato · 50ml milk · 20g flour · 20g butter · 2g cinnamon · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g pasta · 1200g ground beef · 600g tomato · 600ml milk · 240g flour · 240g butter · 24g cinnamon · 24g salt","method":"Cook pasta in boiling water for 8 minutes until tender. Brown ground beef in a pan for 6 minutes. Add tomato, cinnamon and salt and simmer for 10 minutes. Melt butter and stir in flour for 2 minutes. Add milk and cook until thickened, about 5 minutes. Layer pasta, meat sauce and béchamel in a dish. Bake at 180°C for 35 minutes until golden.","cookTime":"55 min","kcal":540,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 45g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let it cool slightly before cutting.","pairsWith":"salad · red wine · bread","trivia":"Pastitsio is often compared to lasagna.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-taramasalata","name":"Ταραμοσαλάτα","nameAlt":"Fish Roe Dip","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"dip","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"50g fish roe · 50g bread · 20ml olive oil · 10ml lemon juice · 2g onion","ingredients12":"600g fish roe · 600g bread · 240ml olive oil · 120ml lemon juice · 24g onion","method":"Soak bread in water for 2 minutes and squeeze dry. Blend fish roe and onion until smooth. Add bread and mix well. Slowly pour in olive oil while blending. Add lemon juice and mix until creamy. Chill for 10 minutes before serving.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 20g · fat 15g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Add oil slowly for a smooth texture.","pairsWith":"bread · olives · wine","trivia":"Traditionally eaten during Lent in Greece.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-loukoumades","name":"Λουκουμάδες","nameAlt":"Honey Doughnuts","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"fried dough","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g flour · 80ml water · 5g yeast · 20ml honey · 20ml oil","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 960ml water · 60g yeast · 240ml honey · 240ml oil","method":"Mix flour, water and yeast into a batter. Let it rest until bubbly, about 20 minutes. Heat oil to medium. Drop small portions of batter into oil. Fry until golden, about 4 minutes. Remove and drain excess oil. Drizzle with honey before serving.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 45g · fat 10g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Keep oil temperature steady for even frying.","pairsWith":"honey · cinnamon · coffee","trivia":"Loukoumades date back to ancient Olympic games.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-ouzo","name":"Ούζο","nameAlt":"Anise-Flavored Spirit","aliases":[],"course":"drink","type":"spirit","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"social","ingredients":"50ml ouzo · 20ml water · 2 ice cubes","ingredients12":"600ml ouzo · 240ml water · 24 ice cubes","method":"Pour ouzo into a glass. Add water slowly to dilute. Drop in ice cubes. Stir gently for a few seconds. Let the drink turn cloudy. Serve chilled immediately.","cookTime":"5 min","kcal":110,"nutrition":"protein 0g · carbs 2g · fat 0g","storage":"Store bottle at room temperature.","chefNotes":"Always add water before ice for best flavor.","pairsWith":"meze · olives · seafood","trivia":"Ouzo turns milky when mixed with water.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"greece-baklava","name":"Μπακλαβάς","nameAlt":"Layered Nut Pastry","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Greece","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"2 phyllo sheet · 50g walnut · 30g honey · 20g butter · 5g sugar · 2g cinnamon","ingredients12":"24 phyllo sheet · 600g walnut · 360g honey · 240g butter · 60g sugar · 24g cinnamon","method":"Brush phyllo sheets with melted butter. Layer with chopped walnuts mixed with sugar and cinnamon. Repeat layers until used up. Cut into pieces before baking. Bake at 180°C for 35 minutes until crisp. Pour warm honey over the baked pastry. Let it soak and cool before serving.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 40g · fat 26g","storage":"Store covered at room temperature for 3 days.","chefNotes":"Pour syrup while pastry is hot for absorption.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · yogurt","trivia":"Baklava is shared across many Middle Eastern cuisines.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-bacalhau-com-natas","name":"Bacalhau com Natas","nameAlt":"Cod with Cream","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"bake","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"family","ingredients":"150g salted cod · 150g potatoes · 100ml cream · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 30ml olive oil · 30g cheese · 2g salt · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g salted cod · 1800g potatoes · 1200ml cream · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 360ml olive oil · 360g cheese · 24g salt · 12g black pepper","method":"Soak the salted cod for 24 hours, changing water to reduce salt. Boil cod for 10 minutes, drain and flake. Peel and slice potatoes and fry at 170°C for about 6 minutes until lightly golden. Sauté onion and garlic in olive oil on medium heat for 5 minutes. Combine cod, potatoes, and cream in a baking dish and mix well. Season with salt and pepper and top with grated cheese. Bake at 180°C for 25 minutes until golden and bubbling. Let rest briefly before serving.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":620,"nutrition":"protein 34g · carbs 40g · fat 36g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days and reheat in oven.","chefNotes":"Use full-fat cream for best texture.","pairsWith":"green salad · white wine · bread","trivia":"This creamy cod dish is a popular comfort food in Portugal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-pataniscas-de-bacalhau","name":"Pataniscas de Bacalhau","nameAlt":"Cod Fritters","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"fritter","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"150g salted cod · 100g flour · 2 eggs · 50g onion · 5g parsley · 200ml sunflower oil · 2g salt · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g salted cod · 1200g flour · 24 eggs · 600g onion · 60g parsley · 2400ml sunflower oil · 24g salt · 12g black pepper","method":"Soak cod for 24 hours and flake after boiling for 10 minutes. In a bowl mix flour, eggs, and a little water to form a batter. Add chopped onion, parsley, and cod to the batter. Season with salt and pepper and mix well. Heat oil to 180°C in a deep pan. Drop spoonfuls of batter into oil and fry for about 4 minutes until golden. Remove and drain on paper. Serve warm.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 30g · fat 24g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Keep batter slightly thick for fluffy fritters.","pairsWith":"rice · salad · white wine","trivia":"Pataniscas are often served with rice and beans in Portugal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-carne-de-porco-a-alentejana","name":"Carne de Porco à Alentejana","nameAlt":"Pork with Clams","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"150g pork · 100g clams · 150g potatoes · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 30ml olive oil · 50ml white wine · 5g coriander · 2g salt · 1g paprika","ingredients12":"1800g pork · 1200g clams · 1800g potatoes · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 360ml olive oil · 600ml white wine · 60g coriander · 24g salt · 12g paprika","method":"Cut pork into cubes and marinate with garlic, paprika, and wine for 30 minutes. Fry potatoes at 170°C for 6 minutes until golden. In a pan, cook pork on medium heat for 10 minutes until browned. Add clams and cover, cooking for 5 minutes until they open. Stir in fried potatoes and mix gently. Season with salt and garnish with coriander. Serve hot.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":580,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 35g · fat 32g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Discard any clams that do not open during cooking.","pairsWith":"bread · white wine · salad","trivia":"This dish combines inland pork with coastal seafood traditions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-acorda","name":"Açorda","nameAlt":"Bread Soup","aliases":["Açorda Alentejana"],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"100g bread · 10g garlic · 5g coriander · 30ml olive oil · 1 egg · 500ml water · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g bread · 120g garlic · 60g coriander · 360ml olive oil · 12 eggs · 6000ml water · 24g salt","method":"Bring water to a boil and add crushed garlic and salt. Tear bread into pieces and place in a bowl. Pour hot broth over bread and let it soak for 5 minutes. Add olive oil and chopped coriander. Poach the egg in simmering water for about 3 minutes. Place the egg on top of the soaked bread. Mix slightly before eating.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 40g · fat 16g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Use stale bread for best texture.","pairsWith":"olives · wine · salad","trivia":"Açorda is a rustic dish from the Alentejo region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-polvo-a-lagareiro","name":"Polvo à Lagareiro","nameAlt":"Roasted Octopus with Potatoes","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"roast","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g octopus · 150g potatoes · 30ml olive oil · 10g garlic · 2g salt · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g octopus · 1800g potatoes · 360ml olive oil · 120g garlic · 24g salt · 12g black pepper","method":"Boil octopus in water for 40 minutes until tender. Preheat oven to 200°C. Crush boiled potatoes lightly and place in a baking dish. Add octopus and drizzle with olive oil and garlic. Season with salt and pepper. Roast for 20 minutes until slightly crisp. Serve hot with extra olive oil.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 32g · carbs 30g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Tenderize octopus well before roasting.","pairsWith":"greens · white wine · bread","trivia":"Lagareiro style refers to generous use of olive oil.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-amijoas-a-bulhao-pato","name":"Amêijoas à Bulhão Pato","nameAlt":"Clams with Garlic and Cilantro","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"200g clams · 20ml olive oil · 10g garlic · 5g coriander · 50ml white wine · 2g salt · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g clams · 240ml olive oil · 120g garlic · 60g coriander · 600ml white wine · 24g salt · 12g black pepper","method":"Clean clams thoroughly under cold water. Heat olive oil in a pan and sauté garlic for 2 minutes. Add clams and white wine and cover. Cook on high heat for 5 minutes until clams open. Season with salt and pepper. Sprinkle chopped coriander on top. Serve immediately with bread.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 6g · fat 14g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Do not overcook clams to keep them tender.","pairsWith":"bread · white wine · lemon","trivia":"Named after a 19th-century Portuguese poet.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-ovos-moles","name":"Ovos Moles","nameAlt":"Sweet Egg Cream","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"confection","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"3 egg yolks · 100g sugar · 50ml water · 10g wafer shells","ingredients12":"36 egg yolks · 1200g sugar · 600ml water · 120g wafer shells","method":"Heat sugar and water in a pan until it forms a syrup at about 110°C. Beat egg yolks in a bowl. Slowly pour hot syrup into yolks while stirring constantly. Return mixture to low heat and cook gently for 5 minutes until thick. Spoon the mixture into wafer shells. Let cool before serving.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 50g · fat 8g","storage":"Store in a cool place for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Stir constantly to avoid curdling.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · fruit","trivia":"This sweet comes from Aveiro and is shaped like shells.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-tripas-a-moda-do-porto","name":"Tripas à Moda do Porto","nameAlt":"Porto Style Tripe Stew","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"150g tripe · 50g beans · 50g sausage · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 30ml olive oil · 50g carrot · 2g salt · 1g paprika · 500ml water","ingredients12":"1800g tripe · 600g beans · 600g sausage · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 360ml olive oil · 600g carrot · 24g salt · 12g paprika · 6000ml water","method":"Clean tripe thoroughly and boil for 30 minutes. In a pot, sauté onion and garlic in olive oil for 5 minutes. Add sausage and cook for another 5 minutes. Stir in beans, carrot, and cooked tripe. Add water and simmer for 40 minutes on low heat. Season with salt and paprika. Serve hot.","cookTime":"80 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 30g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Proper cleaning of tripe is essential for flavor.","pairsWith":"rice · bread · red wine","trivia":"Residents of Porto are nicknamed 'tripeiros' because of this dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-leite-creme","name":"Leite Creme","nameAlt":"Portuguese Creme Brulee","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"custard","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"family","ingredients":"200ml milk · 100g sugar · 2 egg yolks · 10g cornflour · 5g lemon peel · 5g cinnamon","ingredients12":"2400ml milk · 1200g sugar · 24 egg yolks · 120g cornflour · 60g lemon peel · 60g cinnamon","method":"Heat milk with lemon peel and cinnamon until warm. In a bowl mix sugar, egg yolks, and cornflour until smooth. Slowly add warm milk while stirring. Return mixture to a pan and cook on low heat for 10 minutes until thick. Pour into dishes and let cool. Sprinkle sugar on top and caramelize with a hot iron or grill at 220°C for 3 minutes. Serve chilled or slightly warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":310,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 45g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Caramelize just before serving for crisp top.","pairsWith":"coffee · biscuits · berries","trivia":"Leite creme is similar to creme brulee but often more fluid.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-bolo-de-arroz","name":"Bolo de Arroz","nameAlt":"Rice Flour Muffin","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g rice flour · 100g sugar · 2 eggs · 50ml milk · 30g butter · 5g baking powder","ingredients12":"1200g rice flour · 1200g sugar · 24 eggs · 600ml milk · 360g butter · 60g baking powder","method":"Preheat oven to 180°C. Beat eggs and sugar until light and fluffy. Add melted butter and milk and mix well. Stir in rice flour and baking powder. Pour batter into molds. Bake for 25 minutes until golden and set. Cool before serving.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":340,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 50g · fat 14g","storage":"Store in airtight container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overmix to keep texture light.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · jam","trivia":"These muffins are commonly found in Portuguese bakeries.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-sopa-de-pedra","name":"Sopa de Pedra","nameAlt":"Stone Soup","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"100g beans · 50g pork · 50g sausage · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 30ml olive oil · 50g carrot · 2g salt · 1g bay leaf · 500ml water","ingredients12":"1200g beans · 600g pork · 600g sausage · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 360ml olive oil · 600g carrot · 24g salt · 12g bay leaf · 6000ml water","method":"Soak beans overnight and cook for 40 minutes until tender. In a pot sauté onion and garlic in olive oil for 5 minutes. Add pork and sausage and cook for 10 minutes. Stir in carrot and cooked beans. Add water and bay leaf and simmer for 30 minutes. Season with salt. Serve hot.","cookTime":"80 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 45g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Legend says the soup was made from a stone to inspire sharing.","pairsWith":"bread · wine · olives","trivia":"The story behind this soup is a famous Portuguese folk tale.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-bacalhau-a-gomes-de-sa","name":"Bacalhau à Gomes de Sá","nameAlt":"Cod with Potatoes and Onions","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"bake","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"family","ingredients":"150g salted cod · 150g potatoes · 50g onion · 30ml olive oil · 1 egg · 5g parsley · 20g black olives · 2g salt · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g salted cod · 1800g potatoes · 600g onion · 360ml olive oil · 12 eggs · 60g parsley · 240g black olives · 24g salt · 12g black pepper","method":"Soak cod for 24 hours and boil for 10 minutes, then flake. Boil potatoes for 15 minutes and slice. Sauté onion in olive oil for 5 minutes. Combine cod, potatoes, and onion in a baking dish. Drizzle with olive oil and bake at 180°C for 20 minutes. Boil egg for 8 minutes and slice. Garnish dish with egg, parsley, and olives before serving.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 32g · carbs 35g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Layer gently to keep structure intact.","pairsWith":"salad · white wine · bread","trivia":"Named after a Porto merchant who popularized the recipe.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-migas-a-alentejana","name":"Migas à Alentejana","nameAlt":"Bread Mash with Garlic and Pork","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"120g bread · 50g pork · 10g garlic · 30ml olive oil · 5g coriander · 2g salt · 1g black pepper · 100ml water","ingredients12":"1440g bread · 600g pork · 120g garlic · 360ml olive oil · 60g coriander · 24g salt · 12g black pepper · 1200ml water","method":"Cut bread into chunks and moisten with water for 5 minutes. Heat olive oil in a pan and cook pork pieces on medium heat for 8 minutes until browned. Remove pork and set aside. In the same pan sauté garlic for 2 minutes. Add bread and mix while pressing into a mash. Stir continuously on medium heat for about 10 minutes until it forms a cohesive mixture. Return pork to the pan and mix well. Season with salt and pepper and garnish with coriander before serving.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 45g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use stale bread for best consistency.","pairsWith":"grilled meat · salad · red wine","trivia":"Migas were created as a way to use leftover bread in rural Portugal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-bolo-rei","name":"Bolo Rei","nameAlt":"King Cake","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"150g flour · 50g sugar · 2 eggs · 50g butter · 50ml milk · 5g yeast · 50g candied fruit · 20g raisins","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 600g sugar · 24 eggs · 600g butter · 600ml milk · 60g yeast · 600g candied fruit · 240g raisins","method":"Mix yeast with warm milk and let sit for 5 minutes. Combine flour, sugar, eggs, and butter in a bowl. Add yeast mixture and knead into dough. Fold in candied fruit and raisins. Let dough rise in a warm place for 1 hour. Shape into a ring and let rise again for 30 minutes. Bake at 180°C for 30 minutes until golden. Cool before serving.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 60g · fat 16g","storage":"Store in airtight container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Traditionally includes a hidden bean and figurine.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · port wine","trivia":"Bolo Rei is a festive cake eaten during Christmas in Portugal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-bolo-de-bolacha","name":"Bolo de Bolacha","nameAlt":"Biscuit Cake","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"family","ingredients":"150g biscuits · 100g butter · 100g sugar · 1 egg · 50ml coffee","ingredients12":"1800g biscuits · 1200g butter · 1200g sugar · 12 eggs · 600ml coffee","method":"Beat butter and sugar until creamy. Add egg and mix until smooth. Dip biscuits quickly in coffee. Layer biscuits and cream alternately in a dish. Repeat layers until ingredients are used. Chill in fridge for at least 2 hours. Slice and serve cold.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 50g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use strong coffee for deeper flavor.","pairsWith":"espresso · milk · berries","trivia":"This no-bake cake is a favorite homemade dessert in Portugal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-toucinho-do-ceu","name":"Toucinho do Céu","nameAlt":"Almond Egg Cake","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g almonds · 100g sugar · 3 egg yolks · 2 egg whites · 30g butter · 10g flour","ingredients12":"1200g almonds · 1200g sugar · 36 egg yolks · 24 egg whites · 360g butter · 120g flour","method":"Preheat oven to 180°C. Grind almonds finely. Beat egg yolks and sugar until thick. Fold in ground almonds and melted butter. Whisk egg whites to stiff peaks and fold gently into mixture. Add flour and mix lightly. Pour into a greased pan. Bake for 30 minutes until set. Cool before slicing.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 40g · fat 28g","storage":"Store in airtight container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overbake to keep moist texture.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · fruit","trivia":"Despite its name, this cake contains no pork.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-pao-de-lo","name":"Pão de Ló","nameAlt":"Portuguese Sponge Cake","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g sugar · 4 eggs · 100g flour","ingredients12":"1200g sugar · 48 eggs · 1200g flour","method":"Preheat oven to 180°C. Beat eggs and sugar for 10 minutes until very fluffy. Gently fold in flour. Pour batter into a lined cake tin. Bake for 25 minutes until lightly golden. Remove and cool before serving.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 55g · fat 5g","storage":"Store in airtight container for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not deflate batter when folding flour.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee · jam","trivia":"Pão de Ló dates back to the 18th century.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-queijo-assado","name":"Queijo Assado","nameAlt":"Baked Cheese","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"bake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"150g cheese · 10ml olive oil · 5g oregano · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g cheese · 120ml olive oil · 60g oregano · 12g black pepper","method":"Preheat oven to 180°C. Place cheese in a small baking dish. Drizzle with olive oil and sprinkle oregano and pepper. Bake for 15 minutes until soft and slightly golden. Serve warm with bread.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 2g · fat 34g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Use a firm cheese that melts well.","pairsWith":"bread · wine · olives","trivia":"Baked cheese is a simple yet popular appetizer in Portugal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-salame-de-chocolate","name":"Salame de Chocolate","nameAlt":"Chocolate Biscuit Salami","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"confection","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"party","ingredients":"150g biscuits · 100g dark chocolate · 100g sugar · 50g butter · 1 egg","ingredients12":"1800g biscuits · 1200g dark chocolate · 1200g sugar · 600g butter · 12 eggs","method":"Melt chocolate and butter together over low heat. Mix in sugar and egg until smooth. Crush biscuits and fold into mixture. Shape into a log using cling film. Chill in fridge for 2 hours until firm. Slice and serve.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 55g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 5 days.","chefNotes":"Chill thoroughly for clean slices.","pairsWith":"coffee · milk · berries","trivia":"Despite its name, this dessert contains no meat.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-favas-guisadas","name":"Favas Guisadas","nameAlt":"Stewed Broad Beans","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"spring","ingredients":"150g broad beans · 50g pork · 50g sausage · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 30ml olive oil · 5g coriander · 2g salt · 1g black pepper · 200ml water","ingredients12":"1800g broad beans · 600g pork · 600g sausage · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 360ml olive oil · 60g coriander · 24g salt · 12g black pepper · 2400ml water","method":"Heat olive oil in a pot and sauté onion and garlic for 5 minutes. Add pork and sausage and cook for 10 minutes. Stir in broad beans and water. Simmer on low heat for 30 minutes until beans are tender. Season with salt and pepper. Garnish with coriander before serving.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":540,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 40g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Fresh beans give the best flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · wine · salad","trivia":"Favas are traditionally eaten in spring festivals.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-bifinhos-com-cogumelos","name":"Bifinhos com Cogumelos","nameAlt":"Steak with Mushrooms","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"saute","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g beef · 100g mushrooms · 20ml olive oil · 10g garlic · 50ml cream · 2g salt · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g beef · 1200g mushrooms · 240ml olive oil · 120g garlic · 600ml cream · 24g salt · 12g black pepper","method":"Slice beef thinly. Heat oil in a pan and cook beef on high heat for 3 minutes. Remove and set aside. In the same pan sauté mushrooms and garlic for 5 minutes. Add cream and simmer for 5 minutes. Return beef to the pan and heat through. Season with salt and pepper. Serve hot.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 32g · carbs 10g · fat 38g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overcook beef to keep it tender.","pairsWith":"rice · fries · red wine","trivia":"A simple home-style Portuguese dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-arroz-de-pato","name":"Arroz de Pato","nameAlt":"Duck Rice","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"rice","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"family","ingredients":"150g duck · 100g rice · 50g chorizo · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 30ml olive oil · 500ml water · 2g salt · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g duck · 1200g rice · 600g chorizo · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 360ml olive oil · 6000ml water · 24g salt · 12g black pepper","method":"Cook duck in water for 40 minutes until tender, then shred. In a pan sauté onion and garlic in olive oil for 5 minutes. Add rice and toast for 2 minutes. Pour in duck cooking liquid and simmer for 15 minutes. Stir in shredded duck and sliced chorizo. Transfer to a baking dish and bake at 180°C for 15 minutes until slightly crisp. Serve hot.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 45g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use duck broth for deeper flavor.","pairsWith":"salad · red wine · bread","trivia":"Arroz de pato is a beloved festive dish in Portugal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-cavacas","name":"Cavacas","nameAlt":"Portuguese Iced Cakes","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g flour · 100g sugar · 3 eggs · 20ml lemon juice · 50g icing sugar","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 1200g sugar · 36 eggs · 240ml lemon juice · 600g icing sugar","method":"Preheat oven to 180°C. Beat eggs and sugar until fluffy. Fold in flour and lemon juice. Spoon batter onto a baking tray. Bake for 15 minutes until set. Mix icing sugar with a little water to form glaze. Spread glaze over cooled cakes. Let set before serving.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":310,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 55g · fat 6g","storage":"Store in airtight container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let icing dry fully for best texture.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee · fruit","trivia":"Cavacas are popular during Portuguese festivals.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-chanfana","name":"Chanfana","nameAlt":"Goat Stew in Wine","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"200g goat meat · 200ml red wine · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 30ml olive oil · 2g salt · 1g bay leaf · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g goat meat · 2400ml red wine · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 360ml olive oil · 24g salt · 12g bay leaf · 12g black pepper","method":"Preheat oven to 160°C. Place goat meat in a clay pot with onion, garlic, and bay leaf. Pour over red wine and olive oil. Season with salt and pepper. Cover and cook in oven for 2 hours until tender. Stir occasionally during cooking. Serve hot.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":650,"nutrition":"protein 40g · carbs 6g · fat 45g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Slow cooking enhances the wine flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · greens · red wine","trivia":"Chanfana is traditionally cooked in wood-fired ovens.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-broa-de-milho","name":"Broa de Milho","nameAlt":"Cornbread Loaf","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g maize flour · 50g wheat flour · 5g yeast · 5g salt · 150ml water","ingredients12":"1800g maize flour · 600g wheat flour · 60g yeast · 60g salt · 1800ml water","method":"Mix maize flour, wheat flour, yeast, and salt in a bowl. Add warm water and mix into a dough. Knead lightly for 5 minutes until combined. Let the dough rise in a warm place for 1 hour. Shape into a round loaf. Bake at 200°C for 40 minutes until crusty and cooked through. Cool before slicing.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 60g · fat 3g","storage":"Store in a bread box for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use coarse maize flour for authentic texture.","pairsWith":"butter · cheese · soup","trivia":"Broa de milho is a staple bread in northern Portugal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-lulas-recheadas","name":"Lulas Recheadas","nameAlt":"Stuffed Squid","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stuffed","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"family","ingredients":"200g squid · 50g rice · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 30ml olive oil · 50g tomato · 200ml fish stock · 2g salt · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g squid · 600g rice · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 360ml olive oil · 600g tomato · 2400ml fish stock · 24g salt · 12g black pepper","method":"Clean squid and set aside. Cook rice in water for 10 minutes until partially tender. In a pan sauté onion and garlic in olive oil for 5 minutes. Add chopped tomato and cook for another 5 minutes. Mix rice with the onion mixture and season. Stuff squid with the mixture and secure openings. Place in a pan with fish stock and simmer on low heat for 25 minutes until tender. Serve hot with sauce.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 35g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overstuff squid to prevent bursting.","pairsWith":"rice · salad · white wine","trivia":"Stuffed squid is popular along Portugal’s coastline.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-peixinhos-da-horta","name":"Peixinhos da Horta","nameAlt":"Green Bean Tempura","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"fritter","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"150g green beans · 100g flour · 1 egg · 200ml sunflower oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g green beans · 1200g flour · 12 eggs · 2400ml sunflower oil · 24g salt","method":"Trim green beans and blanch in boiling water for 3 minutes. Drain and pat dry. Prepare a batter with flour, egg, and a little water. Heat oil to 180°C. Dip beans in batter and fry for about 3 minutes until golden. Remove and drain on paper. Sprinkle with salt and serve warm.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 35g · fat 18g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Serve immediately for crisp texture.","pairsWith":"dip sauce · salad · beer","trivia":"This dish influenced Japanese tempura through Portuguese traders.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-ameijoas-na-cataplana","name":"Amêijoas na Cataplana","nameAlt":"Clams in Cataplana Pot","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g clams · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 50g tomato · 30ml olive oil · 50ml white wine · 5g coriander · 2g salt · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g clams · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 600g tomato · 360ml olive oil · 600ml white wine · 60g coriander · 24g salt · 12g black pepper","method":"Clean clams thoroughly. Heat olive oil in a pot and sauté onion and garlic for 5 minutes. Add tomato and cook for another 5 minutes. Add clams and white wine, then cover tightly. Cook on high heat for 5 minutes until clams open. Season with salt and pepper and sprinkle coriander. Serve immediately.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 8g · fat 16g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Use a sealed pot to trap steam for proper cooking.","pairsWith":"bread · white wine · lemon","trivia":"Cataplana is both the dish and the traditional copper cooking vessel.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-encharcada","name":"Encharcada","nameAlt":"Egg Yolk Syrup Dessert","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"confection","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"4 egg yolks · 100g sugar · 100ml water · 5g cinnamon","ingredients12":"48 egg yolks · 1200g sugar · 1200ml water · 60g cinnamon","method":"Heat sugar and water to make a syrup at about 110°C. Beat egg yolks lightly in a bowl. Slowly pour hot syrup into yolks while stirring. Return mixture to low heat and cook gently for 5 minutes until thickened. Pour into a dish and sprinkle cinnamon. Let cool before serving.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":290,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 45g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Cook gently to avoid scrambling eggs.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · biscuits","trivia":"Encharcada is a conventual sweet from southern Portugal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-sopa-de-cacao","name":"Sopa de Cação","nameAlt":"Dogfish Soup","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"150g dogfish · 100g bread · 10g garlic · 5g coriander · 30ml olive oil · 500ml water · 2g salt · 1g paprika","ingredients12":"1800g dogfish · 1200g bread · 120g garlic · 60g coriander · 360ml olive oil · 6000ml water · 24g salt · 12g paprika","method":"Bring water to a boil and cook dogfish for 10 minutes. Remove fish and flake into pieces. In another pot sauté garlic in olive oil for 2 minutes. Add cooking water and bring to a simmer. Add bread pieces and cook for 5 minutes until softened. Stir in fish and coriander. Season with salt and paprika. Serve hot.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":360,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 30g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use firm white fish if dogfish is unavailable.","pairsWith":"wine · olives · salad","trivia":"This soup is a specialty of the Alentejo region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-pasteis-de-nata","name":"Pastéis de Nata","nameAlt":"custard tarts","aliases":["Pastel de Nata"],"course":"dessert","type":"tart","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"bakery","ingredients":"120g puff pastry · 120ml whole milk · 80g sugar · 2 egg yolks · 10g wheat flour · 2g cinnamon stick · 5ml lemon peel strips · 2g ground cinnamon","ingredients12":"1440g puff pastry · 1440ml whole milk · 960g sugar · 24 egg yolks · 120g wheat flour · 24g cinnamon sticks · 60ml lemon peel strips · 24g ground cinnamon","method":"Preheat the oven to 250°C and place a metal tray inside to heat. Roll the puff pastry tightly and slice into rounds, then press each into a tart mold. In a saucepan, heat the milk with lemon peel and a cinnamon stick until just steaming for about 5 minutes. In a bowl, whisk sugar with flour, then gradually add the hot milk while stirring. Return the mixture to medium heat and cook for 3–4 minutes until slightly thickened. Remove from heat and whisk in egg yolks quickly. Strain the custard and fill pastry shells to just below the rim. Bake at 250°C for 10–12 minutes until blistered on top. Dust with ground cinnamon and cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":290,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 34g · fat 15g","storage":"Keep chilled and reheat briefly before serving.","chefNotes":"Chill the custard for 2 hours before baking for best texture.","pairsWith":"espresso · port wine · fresh berries","trivia":"These iconic tarts originated in Lisbon’s Belém district.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-caldo-verde","name":"Caldo Verde","nameAlt":"kale & potato soup","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g potatoes · 50g kale · 30g chouriço sausage · 15ml olive oil · 500ml water · 2g salt · 1g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g potatoes · 600g kale · 360g chouriço sausage · 180ml olive oil · 6000ml water · 24g salt · 12g black pepper","method":"Peel and chop the potatoes, then boil in water for 15 minutes until soft. Blend the potatoes with the cooking liquid until smooth. Return to heat and simmer for 5 minutes. Finely shred the kale and add to the soup. Slice the chouriço thinly and add to the pot. Drizzle olive oil and simmer for another 5 minutes. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Serve hot with crusty bread.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 35g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let the soup rest 1 hour before serving for deeper flavor.","pairsWith":"cornbread · red wine · olives","trivia":"A staple from northern Portugal, especially Minho.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-frango-piri-piri","name":"Frango Piri-Piri","nameAlt":"peri-peri chicken","aliases":["Frango no Churrasco"],"course":"main","type":"grilled","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"bbq","ingredients":"300g chicken leg · 20ml olive oil · 10g garlic · 5g chili flakes · 10ml lemon juice · 2g paprika · 2g salt","ingredients12":"3600g chicken legs · 240ml olive oil · 120g garlic · 60g chili flakes · 120ml lemon juice · 24g paprika · 24g salt","method":"Preheat a grill to medium-high heat around 200°C. Mix olive oil, garlic, chili flakes, lemon juice, paprika, and salt into a marinade. Rub the marinade over the chicken thoroughly. Grill the chicken for 20 minutes, turning occasionally. Brush extra marinade while cooking. Ensure internal temperature reaches safe level. Rest the chicken for 5 minutes before serving. Serve with extra sauce on the side.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 3g · fat 32g","storage":"Refrigerate leftovers up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Marinate overnight for best flavor.","pairsWith":"chips · salad · beer","trivia":"Piri-piri sauce traces back to African chili peppers.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-sardinhas-assadas","name":"Sardinhas Assadas","nameAlt":"grilled sardines","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"grilled","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"180g sardines · 10ml olive oil · 2g sea salt · 5ml lemon juice","ingredients12":"2160g sardines · 120ml olive oil · 24g sea salt · 60ml lemon juice","method":"Preheat grill to high heat around 220°C. Clean and pat dry the sardines. Brush lightly with olive oil. Sprinkle generously with sea salt. Grill for 3–4 minutes per side. Avoid overcooking to keep flesh moist. Drizzle lemon juice just before serving. Serve immediately while hot.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 0g · fat 20g","storage":"Best eaten fresh; refrigerate max 1 day.","chefNotes":"No resting needed; serve immediately.","pairsWith":"bread · wine · salad","trivia":"Popular during Lisbon’s June festivals.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-francesinha","name":"Francesinha","nameAlt":"Porto sandwich","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"sandwich","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"120g bread · 100g steak · 50g ham · 80g sausage · 50g cheese · 200ml beer sauce · 10g butter","ingredients12":"1440g bread · 1200g steak · 600g ham · 960g sausages · 600g cheese · 2400ml beer sauce · 120g butter","method":"Cook the steak and sausage in a pan over medium heat for 10 minutes. Layer bread, steak, ham, and sausage. Top with another slice of bread. Cover entirely with cheese slices. Melt butter in a pan and toast sandwich lightly. Pour hot beer sauce over the sandwich. Place in oven at 200°C for 10 minutes until cheese melts. Serve with fries.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":850,"nutrition":"protein 45g · carbs 60g · fat 45g","storage":"Consume fresh; not ideal for storage.","chefNotes":"Sauce can simmer for 2 hours for depth.","pairsWith":"fries · beer · salad","trivia":"A rich specialty from Porto inspired by French cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-bifana","name":"Bifana","nameAlt":"pork sandwich","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"sandwich","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"120g pork slices · 80g bread roll · 10ml white wine · 5g garlic · 5ml olive oil · 2g paprika · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1440g pork slices · 960g bread rolls · 120ml white wine · 60g garlic · 60ml olive oil · 24g paprika · 24g salt","method":"Heat olive oil in a pan over medium heat. Add garlic and cook for 1 minute. Add pork slices and cook for 5–6 minutes. Deglaze with white wine and simmer 5 minutes. Season with paprika and salt. Slice the bread roll open. Fill with the pork and juices. Serve hot immediately.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 35g · fat 18g","storage":"Store filling separately up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Marinate pork for 4 hours before cooking.","pairsWith":"mustard · beer · chips","trivia":"A popular quick snack across Portugal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-feijoada","name":"Feijoada","nameAlt":"bean & meat stew","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"family-meal","ingredients":"150g black beans · 100g pork · 50g sausage · 30g onion · 10ml olive oil · 2g garlic · 2g bay leaf","ingredients12":"1800g black beans · 1200g pork · 600g sausage · 360g onion · 120ml olive oil · 24g garlic · 24g bay leaf","method":"Soak beans overnight, then drain. Heat olive oil and sauté onion and garlic for 5 minutes. Add pork and sausage and brown for 10 minutes. Add beans and water to cover. Simmer for 45 minutes until beans are tender. Season with salt and bay leaf. Continue cooking 10 minutes more. Serve hot with rice.","cookTime":"65 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 40g · fat 25g","storage":"Keeps refrigerated for 3 days.","chefNotes":"Beans must soak overnight before cooking.","pairsWith":"rice · greens · wine","trivia":"Different regions have their own versions of feijoada.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-arroz-de-marisco","name":"Arroz de Marisco","nameAlt":"seafood rice","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"rice","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"special","ingredients":"100g rice · 150g mixed seafood · 30g tomato · 10ml olive oil · 5g garlic · 500ml fish stock · 2g coriander","ingredients12":"1200g rice · 1800g mixed seafood · 360g tomato · 120ml olive oil · 60g garlic · 6000ml fish stock · 24g coriander","method":"Heat olive oil and sauté garlic for 2 minutes. Add tomato and cook for 5 minutes. Stir in rice and coat well. Pour in fish stock and bring to boil. Add seafood and simmer 15 minutes. Stir occasionally to keep creamy texture. Season and finish with coriander. Serve immediately.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 55g · fat 12g","storage":"Eat fresh; rice can harden when stored.","chefNotes":"Use fresh seafood for best taste.","pairsWith":"white wine · bread · salad","trivia":"Often enjoyed along Portugal’s coast.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-caldeirada","name":"Caldeirada","nameAlt":"fish stew","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"family-meal","ingredients":"200g mixed fish · 100g potatoes · 50g onion · 10ml olive oil · 30g tomato · 200ml fish stock · 2g paprika","ingredients12":"2400g mixed fish · 1200g potatoes · 600g onion · 120ml olive oil · 360g tomato · 2400ml fish stock · 24g paprika","method":"Slice potatoes and onion thinly. Layer them in a pot with fish pieces. Add tomato and paprika. Drizzle olive oil and pour in stock. Simmer gently for 30 minutes. Avoid stirring too much to keep fish intact. Season to taste. Serve hot.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 30g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Let sit 1 hour after cooking for flavors to meld.","pairsWith":"bread · wine · salad","trivia":"A fisherman’s dish made with catch of the day.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-leitao","name":"Leitão","nameAlt":"roast suckling pig","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"roast","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"300g suckling pig · 10g garlic · 5g salt · 2g pepper · 10ml olive oil","ingredients12":"3600g suckling pig · 120g garlic · 60g salt · 24g pepper · 120ml olive oil","method":"Preheat oven to 200°C. Rub pig with garlic, salt, and pepper. Place in roasting tray and drizzle oil. Roast for 60 minutes, turning occasionally. Increase heat to 220°C for crisp skin for 15 minutes. Rest meat 10 minutes before slicing. Serve with sides.","cookTime":"75 min","kcal":700,"nutrition":"protein 45g · carbs 2g · fat 60g","storage":"Refrigerate leftovers for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Marinate for 12 hours before roasting.","pairsWith":"chips · salad · wine","trivia":"A specialty of Bairrada region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-ginjinha","name":"Ginjinha","nameAlt":"cherry liqueur","aliases":["Ginja"],"course":"drink","type":"liqueur","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"digestif","ingredients":"100g sour cherries · 50g sugar · 100ml aguardente","ingredients12":"1200g sour cherries · 600g sugar · 1200ml aguardente","method":"Wash and pit the cherries. Place in a jar with sugar. Pour over aguardente to cover. Seal and store in a cool dark place. Shake occasionally over several days. Strain liquid before serving. Serve chilled in small glasses.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":180,"nutrition":"protein 0g · carbs 20g · fat 0g","storage":"Store sealed for months.","chefNotes":"Infuse for at least 1 month before drinking.","pairsWith":"chocolate · pastries · coffee","trivia":"Often served in Lisbon bars in chocolate cups.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"portugal-queijadas","name":"Queijadas","nameAlt":"sweet cheese tarts","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"tart","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"southern-europe","country":"Portugal","occasion":"bakery","ingredients":"100g fresh cheese · 80g sugar · 1 egg · 30g flour · 5g butter · 2g cinnamon","ingredients12":"1200g fresh cheese · 960g sugar · 12 eggs · 360g flour · 60g butter · 24g cinnamon","method":"Preheat oven to 180°C. Mix cheese, sugar, and egg until smooth. Stir in flour and melted butter. Add cinnamon and combine well. Pour mixture into small molds. Bake for 25 minutes until golden. Cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 30g · fat 12g","storage":"Keep refrigerated up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Chill batter 1 hour before baking.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee · fruit","trivia":"Famous in Sintra with centuries-old origins.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-moules-frites","name":"Moules-Frites","nameAlt":"Mussels with Fries","aliases":["Mosselen met friet"],"course":"main","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"300g mussels · 150g potato · 50g onion · 10ml olive oil · 100ml white wine · 5g garlic · 10g parsley · 2g salt","ingredients12":"3600g mussels · 1800g potato · 600g onion · 120ml olive oil · 1200ml white wine · 60g garlic · 120g parsley · 24g salt","method":"Clean the mussels thoroughly, discarding any that do not close when tapped. In a large pot, sauté onion and garlic in olive oil until fragrant, then add white wine and bring to a simmer. Add the mussels, cover, and cook until they open fully, shaking the pot occasionally. Fry the potatoes separately until golden and crisp. Serve the mussels with broth and fries on the side.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 50g · fat 20g","storage":"Best eaten fresh","chefNotes":"Discard unopened mussels after cooking","pairsWith":"fries · salad · mayonnaise · bread dishes","trivia":"Considered Belgium's national dish","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-carbonnade-flamande","name":"Carbonnade Flamande","nameAlt":"Flemish Beef Stew with Beer","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"180g beef · 100g onion · 150ml beer · 10g mustard · 1 slice bread · 10ml olive oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"2160g beef · 1200g onion · 1800ml beer · 120g mustard · 12 slice bread · 120ml olive oil · 24g salt","method":"Brown the beef in olive oil until well seared, then remove and set aside. In the same pot, cook onions until softened and slightly caramelized. Return the beef and add beer, mustard, and bread to thicken the sauce. Simmer slowly until the meat becomes tender and the sauce rich. Serve hot after resting briefly.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":650,"nutrition":"protein 40g · carbs 35g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 4 days","chefNotes":"Use dark beer for deeper flavor","pairsWith":"fries · mashed potatoes · red cabbage · salad","trivia":"A traditional Flemish comfort dish","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-belgian-waffles","name":"Belgian Waffles","nameAlt":"Light Crisp Waffles","aliases":["Gaufres","Wafels"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"120g flour · 200ml milk · 1 egg · 20g sugar · 20g butter · 5g yeast","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 2400ml milk · 12 egg · 240g sugar · 240g butter · 60g yeast","method":"Mix flour, milk, egg, sugar, butter, and yeast into a smooth batter and allow it to rise slightly. Preheat a waffle iron until hot. Pour batter into the iron and cook until golden and crisp. Remove carefully and allow to cool slightly. Serve warm with toppings.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 45g · fat 15g","storage":"Best eaten fresh","chefNotes":"Do not overfill the waffle iron","pairsWith":"fruit · cream · chocolate · syrup","trivia":"Belgium is famous worldwide for its waffles","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-stoofvlees","name":"Stoofvlees","nameAlt":"Flemish Beef and Beer Stew","aliases":["Carbonnade Flamande"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"180g beef · 100g onion · 150ml beer · 10g mustard · 10ml olive oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"2160g beef · 1200g onion · 1800ml beer · 120g mustard · 120ml olive oil · 24g salt","method":"Brown the beef in oil until sealed, then set aside. Cook onions until soft and slightly caramelized. Add beer and mustard, then return the beef to the pot. Simmer slowly until the meat becomes tender and the sauce thickens. Serve hot with sauce spooned over.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":650,"nutrition":"protein 40g · carbs 30g · fat 32g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 4 days","chefNotes":"Slow cooking is essential for tenderness","pairsWith":"fries · mashed potatoes · vegetables · salad","trivia":"Another name for the classic Flemish stew","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-waterzooi","name":"Waterzooi","nameAlt":"Creamy Chicken or Fish Stew","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"family meal","ingredients":"200g chicken · 100g potato · 50g carrot · 50g leek · 150ml cream · 10ml olive oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"2400g chicken · 1200g potato · 600g carrot · 600g leek · 1800ml cream · 120ml olive oil · 24g salt","method":"Cook the chicken gently in water or stock until tender, then remove and set aside. Add vegetables to the broth and cook until soft. Return the chicken and stir in cream to enrich the broth. Simmer gently until flavors combine without boiling. Serve warm as a creamy stew.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 25g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days","chefNotes":"Do not boil after adding cream","pairsWith":"bread dishes · potatoes · salad · vegetables","trivia":"Originated in Ghent","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-speculoos","name":"Speculoos","nameAlt":"Spiced Shortcrust Biscuits","aliases":["Speculaas"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"festive","ingredients":"120g flour · 50g butter · 50g sugar · 5g spice mix · 5ml milk","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 600g butter · 600g sugar · 60g spice mix · 60ml milk","method":"Mix flour, butter, sugar, spices, and milk into a firm dough. Roll out and cut into shapes. Bake until crisp and golden. Allow to cool completely to harden. Serve as crunchy biscuits.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 40g · fat 15g","storage":"Store in airtight container up to 1 week","chefNotes":"Chill dough before rolling","pairsWith":"coffee alternatives · cream · desserts","trivia":"Traditionally eaten during Saint Nicholas celebrations","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-croquettes-aux-crevettes","name":"Croquettes aux Crevettes","nameAlt":"Shrimp Croquettes","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"starter","ingredients":"120g shrimp · 30g flour · 200ml milk · 20g butter · 1 egg · 50g breadcrumbs · 100ml oil","ingredients12":"1440g shrimp · 360g flour · 2400ml milk · 240g butter · 12 egg · 600g breadcrumbs · 1200ml oil","method":"Prepare a thick sauce by melting butter, adding flour, and whisking in milk. Stir in shrimp and allow to cool until firm. Shape into croquettes, coat in egg and breadcrumbs. Fry in hot oil until golden and crisp. Drain and serve immediately.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 30g · fat 25g","storage":"Best eaten fresh","chefNotes":"Chill mixture before shaping","pairsWith":"salad · lemon wedges · vegetables · sauce","trivia":"A classic Belgian starter","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-filet-americain","name":"Filet Américain","nameAlt":"Seasoned Raw Beef Tartare","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"casual","ingredients":"150g raw beef · 1 egg yolk · 10g mustard · 10g onion · 5g capers · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g raw beef · 12 egg yolk · 120g mustard · 120g onion · 60g capers · 24g salt","method":"Finely chop or mince high-quality beef and place in a bowl. Mix with egg yolk, mustard, onion, capers, and seasoning until well combined. Adjust seasoning to taste. Shape or spread onto a plate. Serve immediately while fresh.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 5g · fat 28g","storage":"Consume immediately","chefNotes":"Use only very fresh beef","pairsWith":"fries · salad · pickles · bread dishes","trivia":"Belgium's version of steak tartare","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-endive-au-gratin","name":"Endive au Gratin","nameAlt":"Baked Endive with Ham and Cheese","aliases":["Chicons au gratin"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"family meal","ingredients":"150g endive · 100g ham · 150ml milk · 20g butter · 20g cheese · 15g flour · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g endive · 1200g ham · 1800ml milk · 240g butter · 240g cheese · 180g flour · 24g salt","method":"Cook the endive until tender and drain excess moisture. Wrap each piece in ham and place in a baking dish. Prepare a béchamel by melting butter, adding flour, and whisking in milk. Pour the sauce over the dish and top with cheese. Bake until golden and bubbling.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 20g · fat 35g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days","chefNotes":"Drain endive well to avoid bitterness","pairsWith":"potatoes · salad · vegetables · bread dishes","trivia":"A beloved Belgian comfort dish","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-vol-au-vent","name":"Vol-au-Vent","nameAlt":"Chicken and Mushroom Puff Pastry","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"family meal","ingredients":"150g chicken · 80g mushroom · 150ml cream · 1 pastry shell · 20g butter · 10g flour · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g chicken · 960g mushroom · 1800ml cream · 12 pastry shell · 240g butter · 120g flour · 24g salt","method":"Cook the chicken until tender, then cut into pieces. Sauté mushrooms in butter until soft. Add flour and stir before gradually adding cream to form a sauce. Combine chicken and mushrooms in the sauce and simmer gently. Fill pastry shells and serve warm.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 30g · fat 35g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days","chefNotes":"Keep pastry crisp by filling just before serving","pairsWith":"fries · salad · vegetables · greens","trivia":"A classic Belgian comfort dish","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-belgian-fries","name":"Belgian Fries","nameAlt":"Double-Fried Potatoes","aliases":["Frites"],"course":"side","type":"vegetarian","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"street food","ingredients":"200g potato · 200ml oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"2400g potato · 2400ml oil · 24g salt","method":"Cut potatoes into thick strips and rinse to remove starch. Fry at a lower temperature until soft, then remove and cool. Fry again at higher heat until golden and crisp. Drain excess oil and season with salt. Serve immediately while hot.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 50g · fat 20g","storage":"Best eaten fresh","chefNotes":"Double frying creates perfect texture","pairsWith":"mussels · steak · sauces · burgers","trivia":"Belgium claims origin of fries","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-liege-waffles","name":"Liege Waffles","nameAlt":"Caramelized Sugar Waffles","aliases":["Gaufres de Liège","Luikse wafels"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"street food","ingredients":"120g flour · 1 egg · 50ml milk · 40g butter · 30g pearl sugar · 5g yeast · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 12 egg · 600ml milk · 480g butter · 360g pearl sugar · 60g yeast · 24g salt","method":"Mix flour, yeast, milk, egg, butter, and salt into a soft dough and allow it to rise until doubled. Knead in pearl sugar just before cooking so it stays intact. Divide into portions and cook in a hot waffle iron until golden and caramelized. The sugar will melt and create a crisp coating. Serve warm for best texture.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 55g · fat 18g","storage":"Best eaten fresh","chefNotes":"Pearl sugar creates the signature crunch","pairsWith":"fruit · cream · chocolate · nuts","trivia":"Distinct from Brussels waffles due to caramelized sugar","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-brussels-waffles","name":"Brussels Waffles","nameAlt":"Light Rectangular Waffles","aliases":["Gaufres de Bruxelles"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"120g flour · 200ml milk · 1 egg · 20g sugar · 20g butter · 5g yeast","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 2400ml milk · 12 egg · 240g sugar · 240g butter · 60g yeast","method":"Prepare a batter by mixing flour, milk, egg, sugar, butter, and yeast until smooth and airy. Allow it to rest briefly to develop structure. Pour into a hot waffle iron and cook until light and crisp. Remove carefully and allow to cool slightly. Serve with toppings as desired.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 45g · fat 15g","storage":"Best eaten fresh","chefNotes":"Do not press waffle iron too tightly","pairsWith":"fruit · cream · chocolate · syrup","trivia":"Known for its light and airy texture","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-rabbit-in-beer","name":"Rabbit in Beer","nameAlt":"Braised Rabbit with Beer Sauce","aliases":["Lapin à la bière"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"200g rabbit · 100g onion · 150ml beer · 10ml olive oil · 5g mustard · 2g salt","ingredients12":"2400g rabbit · 1200g onion · 1800ml beer · 120ml olive oil · 60g mustard · 24g salt","method":"Brown the rabbit pieces in oil until sealed and lightly golden. Remove and sauté onions until soft. Return the rabbit and add beer and mustard, then simmer gently. Cook until the meat is tender and the sauce thickens. Allow to rest briefly before serving.","cookTime":"90 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 20g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days","chefNotes":"Use dark beer for richer flavor","pairsWith":"potatoes · red cabbage · salad · vegetables","trivia":"A rustic Belgian countryside dish","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-gentse-waterzooi","name":"Gentse Waterzooi","nameAlt":"Ghent Style Creamy Chicken Stew","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"family meal","ingredients":"200g chicken · 100g potato · 50g carrot · 50g leek · 150ml cream · 10ml olive oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"2400g chicken · 1200g potato · 600g carrot · 600g leek · 1800ml cream · 120ml olive oil · 24g salt","method":"Cook the chicken in water or stock until tender, then remove and set aside. Add vegetables to the broth and cook until soft. Return the chicken and stir in cream to enrich the stew. Simmer gently without boiling. Serve warm with the creamy broth.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 25g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days","chefNotes":"Avoid boiling after adding cream","pairsWith":"bread dishes · potatoes · salad · greens","trivia":"A regional specialty from Ghent","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-chicons-au-gratin","name":"Chicons au Gratin","nameAlt":"Endive Wrapped in Ham with Cheese Sauce","aliases":["Endive au Gratin"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"family meal","ingredients":"150g endive · 100g ham · 150ml milk · 20g butter · 20g cheese · 15g flour · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g endive · 1200g ham · 1800ml milk · 240g butter · 240g cheese · 180g flour · 24g salt","method":"Cook the endive until tender and remove excess moisture. Wrap each piece in ham and place in a baking dish. Prepare a béchamel by melting butter, adding flour, and whisking in milk. Pour over the dish and top with cheese. Bake until golden and bubbling.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 20g · fat 35g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days","chefNotes":"Drain endive well to avoid bitterness","pairsWith":"potatoes · salad · vegetables · bread dishes","trivia":"A staple Belgian comfort meal","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-boulets-a-la-liegeoise","name":"Boulets à la Liégeoise","nameAlt":"Meatballs in Sweet-Sour Sauce","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"comfort food","ingredients":"150g minced beef · 30g breadcrumbs · 1 egg · 100g onion · 50g syrup · 10ml vinegar · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g minced beef · 360g breadcrumbs · 12 egg · 1200g onion · 600g syrup · 120ml vinegar · 24g salt","method":"Mix minced beef with breadcrumbs, egg, and seasoning, then shape into balls. Fry until browned on all sides. In a separate pan, cook onions and add syrup and vinegar to create a sauce. Add meatballs and simmer until coated and heated through. Serve warm with sauce.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 35g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days","chefNotes":"Balance sweet and sour flavors carefully","pairsWith":"fries · mashed potatoes · salad · vegetables","trivia":"A specialty from Liège","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-stoemp","name":"Stoemp","nameAlt":"Mashed Potatoes with Vegetables","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"vegetarian","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"family meal","ingredients":"200g potato · 50g carrot · 50g leek · 20g butter · 50ml milk · 2g salt","ingredients12":"2400g potato · 600g carrot · 600g leek · 240g butter · 600ml milk · 24g salt","method":"Boil the potatoes and vegetables until soft. Drain and mash together until smooth but slightly textured. Add butter and milk to enrich the mixture. Season and mix well. Serve warm as a side dish.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 45g · fat 12g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days","chefNotes":"Do not overmix to keep texture","pairsWith":"sausages · meatballs · stews · gravy","trivia":"A traditional Belgian comfort side","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-speculoos-spread","name":"Speculoos Spread","nameAlt":"Spiced Biscuit Spread","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"100g biscuits · 50ml milk · 20g sugar · 10g butter","ingredients12":"1200g biscuits · 600ml milk · 240g sugar · 120g butter","method":"Crush the biscuits into fine crumbs. Mix with milk, sugar, and butter until smooth and spreadable. Blend if needed for a finer texture. Adjust consistency as desired. Serve as a spread.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 4g · carbs 50g · fat 15g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 1 week","chefNotes":"Blend longer for smoother texture","pairsWith":"bread dishes · pancakes · waffles · fruit","trivia":"Inspired by speculoos biscuits","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-jambon-d-ardenne","name":"Jambon d'Ardenne","nameAlt":"Cured Ham from Ardennes","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"appetizer","ingredients":"120g cured ham · 10g butter","ingredients12":"1440g cured ham · 120g butter","method":"Slice the cured ham thinly and arrange on a plate. Allow it to come to room temperature to enhance flavor. Add small amounts of butter if desired. Serve as is without further cooking. Enjoy immediately.","cookTime":"5 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 2g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 5 days","chefNotes":"Serve at room temperature","pairsWith":"bread dishes · pickles · cheese · salad","trivia":"A protected regional product","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-chocolate-mousse","name":"Chocolate Mousse","nameAlt":"Light Chocolate Dessert","aliases":["Mousse au chocolat"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"100g chocolate · 2 egg · 20g sugar · 20g butter","ingredients12":"1200g chocolate · 24 egg · 240g sugar · 240g butter","method":"Melt the chocolate and butter gently until smooth. Separate eggs and mix yolks into the chocolate. Beat egg whites with sugar until stiff peaks form. Fold the whites into the chocolate mixture carefully. Chill until set before serving.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 30g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days","chefNotes":"Fold gently to keep it airy","pairsWith":"fruit · cream · nuts","trivia":"Belgium is famous for its chocolate","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"belgium-kriek-beer","name":"Kriek Beer","nameAlt":"Cherry-Flavored Belgian Beer","aliases":[],"course":"drink","type":"beverage","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Belgium","occasion":"social","ingredients":"250ml cherry beer","ingredients12":"3000ml cherry beer","method":"Pour the beer into a clean glass at a slight angle to control foam. Allow the head to settle naturally. Serve chilled for best flavor. Do not overpour to preserve carbonation. Enjoy immediately.","cookTime":"5 min","kcal":180,"nutrition":"protein 1g · carbs 15g · fat 0g","storage":"Store sealed at room temperature","chefNotes":"Serve well chilled","pairsWith":"cheese · desserts · meat dishes","trivia":"A traditional fruit beer from Belgium","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-stamppot","name":"Stamppot","nameAlt":"Mashed Potatoes with Vegetables","aliases":["Hutspot","Boerenkoolstamppot"],"course":"main","type":"mash","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"300g potatoes · 150g kale · 50g smoked sausage · 10g butter · 50ml milk · 3g salt","ingredients12":"3600g potatoes · 1800g kale · 600g smoked sausage · 120g butter · 600ml milk · 36g salt","method":"Peel the potatoes and cut into chunks, then boil in salted water for about 20 minutes until tender. Add the kale in the last 10 minutes of cooking. Drain everything well and return to the pot. Mash the potatoes and kale together until smooth. Heat the milk and butter gently and mix into the mash. Slice and warm the smoked sausage separately. Season with salt to taste. Serve hot with sausage on top.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 55g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate in a sealed container for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use waxy potatoes for a smoother texture.","pairsWith":"mustard · pickles · rye bread","trivia":"Stamppot dates back to the 17th century and is a Dutch winter staple.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-bitterballen","name":"Bitterballen","nameAlt":"Crispy Meat Snack Balls","aliases":["Bitterballen snack"],"course":"starter","type":"fried snack","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"pub","ingredients":"100g beef · 20g flour · 20g butter · 100ml beef stock · 1 egg · 50g breadcrumbs · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g beef · 240g flour · 240g butter · 1200ml beef stock · 12 eggs · 600g breadcrumbs · 60g salt","method":"Cook the beef and shred it finely. Melt butter and stir in flour to make a roux, cooking for about 3 minutes. Gradually add beef stock while stirring until thick. Mix in the shredded beef and season with salt. Chill the mixture until firm. Shape into small balls and coat with egg and breadcrumbs. Fry in oil at 180°C for about 4 minutes until golden. Drain on paper and serve hot.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 30g · fat 28g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 2 days before frying.","chefNotes":"Chilling the filling well helps with shaping.","pairsWith":"mustard · beer · pickles","trivia":"Bitterballen are a popular bar snack in the Netherlands.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-poffertjes","name":"Poffertjes","nameAlt":"Mini Fluffy Pancakes","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pancake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g flour · 150ml milk · 1 egg · 5g yeast · 10g sugar · 10g butter","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 1800ml milk · 12 eggs · 60g yeast · 120g sugar · 120g butter","method":"Mix flour, yeast, sugar, milk and egg into a smooth batter. Let the batter rest in a warm place for about 30 minutes. Heat a poffertjes pan over medium heat and grease with butter. Pour small amounts of batter into each cavity. Cook for about 2 minutes until bubbles form, then flip. Cook another 1 to 2 minutes until golden. Remove and serve warm with butter. Dust with sugar before serving.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 9g · carbs 50g · fat 12g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Use a special poffertjes pan for authentic shape.","pairsWith":"powdered sugar · butter · syrup","trivia":"Poffertjes are often sold at fairs and street markets.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-erwtensoep","name":"Erwtensoep","nameAlt":"Dutch Split Pea Soup","aliases":["Snert"],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"150g split peas · 100g pork · 50g carrot · 50g celery · 1 onion · 5g salt · 500ml water","ingredients12":"1800g split peas · 1200g pork · 600g carrot · 600g celery · 12 onions · 60g salt · 6000ml water","method":"Rinse the split peas and place in a pot with water. Add pork and bring to a boil. Simmer gently for about 60 minutes. Chop carrot, celery and onion. Add vegetables to the soup and continue cooking for another 30 minutes. Stir occasionally until thick. Remove meat, shred and return to the pot. Season with salt. Serve hot when thick and hearty.","cookTime":"90 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 50g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days or freeze.","chefNotes":"Soup thickens more after resting overnight.","pairsWith":"rye bread · smoked sausage · mustard","trivia":"Traditional erwtensoep is so thick a spoon can stand in it.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-kroket","name":"Kroket","nameAlt":"Fried Meat Croquette","aliases":["Croquette"],"course":"starter","type":"fried snack","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"100g beef · 20g flour · 20g butter · 100ml beef stock · 1 egg · 50g breadcrumbs · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g beef · 240g flour · 240g butter · 1200ml beef stock · 12 eggs · 600g breadcrumbs · 60g salt","method":"Cook and shred the beef finely. Make a roux with butter and flour over medium heat for about 3 minutes. Add beef stock gradually while stirring until thick. Mix in beef and season with salt. Chill until firm. Shape into logs and coat in egg and breadcrumbs. Fry at 180°C for about 4 minutes until crisp. Drain and serve hot.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 35g · fat 30g","storage":"Store refrigerated for up to 2 days before frying.","chefNotes":"Freeze briefly before frying for best shape.","pairsWith":"mustard · bread roll · pickles","trivia":"Kroketten are commonly eaten in sandwiches in the Netherlands.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-appeltaart","name":"Appeltaart","nameAlt":"Dutch Apple Pie","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pie","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"150g flour · 100g apple · 50g sugar · 75g butter · 1 egg · 5g cinnamon","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 1200g apple · 600g sugar · 900g butter · 12 eggs · 60g cinnamon","method":"Mix flour, butter and sugar into a dough and chill for 20 minutes. Peel and slice apples. Combine apples with sugar and cinnamon. Roll out dough and line a baking tin. Fill with apple mixture. Cover with strips of dough on top. Brush with beaten egg. Bake at 180°C for about 45 minutes until golden. Cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 60g · fat 20g","storage":"Store covered at room temperature for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use tart apples for better flavor balance.","pairsWith":"whipped cream · coffee · tea","trivia":"Dutch apple pie is deeper and more spiced than many versions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-haring","name":"Haring","nameAlt":"Raw Herring Fish","aliases":["Hollandse Nieuwe"],"course":"starter","type":"raw fish","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"150g herring · 20g onion · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g herring · 240g onion · 60g salt","method":"Clean and fillet the herring if not already prepared. Lightly salt the fish. Finely chop the onion. Serve the herring raw with chopped onion on top. Eat immediately while fresh. Optionally hold the fish by the tail and eat traditionally. Keep chilled until serving.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 2g · fat 18g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and consume within 1 day.","chefNotes":"Use very fresh herring for best taste.","pairsWith":"onions · pickles · bread","trivia":"Eating herring by holding it by the tail is a Dutch tradition.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-oliebollen","name":"Oliebollen","nameAlt":"Dutch Doughnuts","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"fried dough","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"New Year","ingredients":"150g flour · 150ml milk · 1 egg · 10g sugar · 5g yeast · 50g raisins","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 1800ml milk · 12 eggs · 120g sugar · 60g yeast · 600g raisins","method":"Mix flour, yeast, sugar, milk and egg into a batter. Stir in raisins. Let the batter rise for about 45 minutes. Heat oil to 180°C. Scoop small portions of batter into the oil. Fry for about 5 minutes until golden brown. Turn occasionally for even cooking. Drain on paper towels. Serve warm dusted with sugar.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 55g · fat 15g","storage":"Best eaten fresh, can be stored 1 day.","chefNotes":"Ensure oil stays at steady temperature for even frying.","pairsWith":"powdered sugar · coffee · tea","trivia":"Oliebollen are traditionally eaten on New Year's Eve.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-kaas","name":"Gouda Kaas","nameAlt":"Gouda Cheese","aliases":["Goudse kaas"],"course":"side","type":"cheese","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g gouda cheese","ingredients12":"1200g gouda cheese","method":"Slice the cheese into thin pieces. Allow it to come to room temperature before serving. Arrange neatly on a plate. Serve as part of a meal or snack. Pair with bread or crackers. Enjoy the creamy texture and flavor. Store properly after use.","cookTime":"5 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 2g · fat 28g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and wrapped for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Room temperature enhances flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · mustard · fruit","trivia":"Gouda is one of the most famous cheeses in the world.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-pannenkoeken","name":"Pannenkoeken","nameAlt":"Dutch Pancakes","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"pancake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g flour · 200ml milk · 1 egg · 10g butter · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 2400ml milk · 12 eggs · 120g butter · 36g salt","method":"Mix flour, milk, egg and salt into a smooth batter. Heat a pan over medium heat and add butter. Pour a thin layer of batter into the pan. Cook for about 2 minutes until golden underneath. Flip and cook another 1 to 2 minutes. Remove and repeat with remaining batter. Serve warm with sweet or savory toppings.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 9g · carbs 40g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Let batter rest for smoother pancakes.","pairsWith":"syrup · bacon · cheese","trivia":"Dutch pancakes are larger and thinner than American ones.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-hutspot","name":"Hutspot","nameAlt":"Carrot Potato Mash","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"mash","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"300g potatoes · 150g carrot · 50g onion · 50g beef · 10g butter · 3g salt","ingredients12":"3600g potatoes · 1800g carrot · 600g onion · 600g beef · 120g butter · 36g salt","method":"Peel and chop potatoes and carrots. Boil them together in salted water for about 25 minutes. Add chopped onion halfway through cooking. Drain and return to pot. Mash until smooth. Stir in butter and cooked beef. Season with salt. Serve hot as a hearty dish.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 55g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Add a splash of milk for creamier texture.","pairsWith":"gravy · sausage · pickles","trivia":"Hutspot is linked to the Siege of Leiden in 1574.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-speklap","name":"Speklap","nameAlt":"Pork Belly Slice","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"grilled meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"bbq","ingredients":"150g pork belly · 5g salt · 5g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g pork belly · 60g salt · 60g black pepper","method":"Season the pork belly with salt and pepper. Heat a grill or pan over medium heat. Cook the pork for about 5 minutes per side until crispy and cooked through. Turn occasionally to prevent burning. Ensure internal heat is sufficient. Remove and rest briefly. Serve hot with sides.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 0g · fat 55g","storage":"Refrigerate leftovers for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Cook slowly for crisp exterior and tender inside.","pairsWith":"bread · mustard · salad","trivia":"Speklap is a popular Dutch BBQ meat.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-kibbeling","name":"Kibbeling","nameAlt":"Battered Fried Fish Pieces","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"fried fish","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"street food","ingredients":"200g white fish · 80g flour · 100ml milk · 1 egg · 5g paprika · 3g salt","ingredients12":"2400g white fish · 960g flour · 1200ml milk · 12 eggs · 60g paprika · 36g salt","method":"Cut the fish into bite-sized pieces. Mix flour, milk, egg, paprika and salt into a smooth batter. Heat oil to 180°C in a deep pan. Dip fish pieces into the batter, coating evenly. Fry in batches for about 4 to 5 minutes until golden and crisp. Remove and drain on paper towels. Serve immediately while hot. Sprinkle extra salt if desired.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 40g · fat 25g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Use firm white fish like cod for best results.","pairsWith":"garlic sauce · fries · lemon","trivia":"Kibbeling was originally made from leftover cod pieces.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-uitsmijter","name":"Uitsmijter","nameAlt":"Open Sandwich with Eggs and Ham","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"sandwich","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"lunch","ingredients":"2 slices bread · 2 eggs · 50g ham · 30g cheese · 5g butter","ingredients12":"24 slices bread · 24 eggs · 600g ham · 360g cheese · 60g butter","method":"Heat butter in a pan over medium heat. Fry the eggs for about 3 to 4 minutes until whites are set but yolks still soft. Toast the bread lightly. Place ham and cheese on the bread slices. Transfer the eggs on top. Allow the cheese to soften from the heat. Serve immediately while warm. Season lightly if needed.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 35g · fat 30g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Keep yolks runny for traditional style.","pairsWith":"salad · coffee · juice","trivia":"The name means 'bouncer', referring to someone throwing you out after a late meal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-rijsttafel","name":"Rijsttafel","nameAlt":"Dutch-Indonesian Rice Table","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"rice platter","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"feast","ingredients":"200g rice · 100g chicken · 50g green beans · 50g coconut milk · 10g soy sauce · 5g chili paste","ingredients12":"2400g rice · 1200g chicken · 600g green beans · 600g coconut milk · 120g soy sauce · 60g chili paste","method":"Cook the rice in boiling water for about 15 minutes until tender. In a separate pan cook chicken pieces over medium heat for about 8 minutes. Add green beans and cook for another 5 minutes. Stir in coconut milk, soy sauce and chili paste. Simmer gently for 10 minutes until flavors combine. Serve the rice with the chicken mixture and sides. Arrange neatly for presentation.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":650,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 70g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Serve multiple small dishes for authenticity.","pairsWith":"pickles · sambal · fried shallots","trivia":"Rijsttafel was developed during Dutch colonial times in Indonesia.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-balkenbrij","name":"Balkenbrij","nameAlt":"Pork and Flour Slice","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"slice","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"150g pork · 50g flour · 300ml pork stock · 5g nutmeg · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1800g pork · 600g flour · 3600ml pork stock · 60g nutmeg · 36g salt","method":"Cook pork in stock for about 40 minutes until tender. Shred the meat finely. Bring stock to a simmer and stir in flour gradually. Add shredded pork and nutmeg. Cook while stirring until thick. Pour mixture into a tray and let cool until firm. Slice into pieces. Fry slices over medium heat for about 5 minutes until crispy. Serve hot.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":580,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 40g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Allow to set fully before slicing.","pairsWith":"apple syrup · bread · mustard","trivia":"Balkenbrij is a traditional dish from the eastern Netherlands.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-krentenbol","name":"Krentenbol","nameAlt":"Currant Bread Roll","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"breakfast","ingredients":"100g flour · 50g currants · 5g yeast · 50ml milk · 10g sugar · 5g butter","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 600g currants · 60g yeast · 600ml milk · 120g sugar · 60g butter","method":"Mix flour, yeast, sugar and milk into a dough. Knead for about 10 minutes until smooth. Add currants and knead lightly. Let the dough rise for about 60 minutes until doubled. Shape into small rolls. Place on a baking tray and rest for 15 minutes. Bake at 200°C for about 15 minutes until golden. Cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 50g · fat 6g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Soak currants briefly for extra softness.","pairsWith":"butter · jam · tea","trivia":"Krentenbollen are popular school snacks in the Netherlands.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-ontbijtkoek","name":"Ontbijtkoek","nameAlt":"Dutch Spiced Breakfast Cake","aliases":["Peperkoek"],"course":"side","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"breakfast","ingredients":"150g flour · 100g brown sugar · 150ml milk · 5g cinnamon · 5g ginger · 5g baking powder","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 1200g brown sugar · 1800ml milk · 60g cinnamon · 60g ginger · 60g baking powder","method":"Mix flour, sugar, spices and baking powder in a bowl. Add milk and stir into a smooth batter. Pour into a greased loaf tin. Bake at 180°C for about 50 minutes until firm. Remove and cool completely. Slice into thick pieces. Serve plain or with butter. Store properly after cooling.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 65g · fat 5g","storage":"Keep in a sealed container for up to 5 days.","chefNotes":"Flavors improve after a day of resting.","pairsWith":"butter · coffee · tea","trivia":"Ontbijtkoek is often eaten as a quick breakfast or snack.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-zoute-haring-broodje","name":"Broodje Haring","nameAlt":"Herring Sandwich","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"sandwich","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"street food","ingredients":"1 bread roll · 150g herring · 20g onion · 10g pickles","ingredients12":"12 bread rolls · 1800g herring · 240g onion · 120g pickles","method":"Slice the bread roll open. Place the herring inside the roll. Finely chop onion and add on top. Add sliced pickles for extra flavor. Press gently to hold together. Serve immediately while fresh. Keep ingredients chilled before assembling.","cookTime":"5 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 30g · fat 18g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Use fresh herring for authentic taste.","pairsWith":"pickles · onions · soda","trivia":"Broodje haring is a common Dutch street food.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-zuurkoolstamppot","name":"Zuurkoolstamppot","nameAlt":"Sauerkraut Potato Mash","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"mash","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"300g potatoes · 150g sauerkraut · 50g smoked sausage · 10g butter · 50ml milk · 3g salt","ingredients12":"3600g potatoes · 1800g sauerkraut · 600g smoked sausage · 120g butter · 600ml milk · 36g salt","method":"Peel and chop potatoes and boil for about 20 minutes until soft. Warm the sauerkraut separately. Drain potatoes and return to pot. Mash potatoes with butter and milk until smooth. Mix in sauerkraut evenly. Slice and heat the smoked sausage. Season with salt. Serve hot with sausage on top.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":540,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 55g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Rinse sauerkraut slightly if too sour.","pairsWith":"mustard · gravy · pickles","trivia":"Zuurkoolstamppot is a classic winter comfort dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-bossche-bol","name":"Bossche Bol","nameAlt":"Chocolate Cream Puff","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"treat","ingredients":"100g flour · 100ml water · 50g butter · 2 eggs · 100g cream · 100g dark chocolate","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 1200ml water · 600g butter · 24 eggs · 1200g cream · 1200g dark chocolate","method":"Heat water and butter until melted. Add flour and stir until a dough forms. Cool slightly then beat in eggs one at a time. Pipe dough into balls on a tray. Bake at 200°C for about 25 minutes until puffed. Cool completely. Fill with whipped cream. Melt chocolate and coat the tops generously. Allow to set before serving.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 45g · fat 40g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and consume within 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not open oven early to prevent collapse.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · berries","trivia":"Bossche bollen originate from the city of Den Bosch.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"netherlands-gevulde-koek","name":"Gevulde Koek","nameAlt":"Almond Filled Cookie","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cookie","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Netherlands","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"100g flour · 80g almond paste · 50g butter · 50g sugar · 1 egg","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 960g almond paste · 600g butter · 600g sugar · 12 eggs","method":"Mix flour, butter and sugar into a dough and chill briefly. Roll out dough and cut circles. Place almond paste in the center of half the circles. Cover with another circle and seal edges. Brush tops with beaten egg. Bake at 180°C for about 20 minutes until golden. Cool before serving. Enjoy as a sweet treat.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 40g · fat 28g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 4 days.","chefNotes":"Chill dough to prevent spreading.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · milk","trivia":"Gevulde koeken are a beloved Dutch bakery item.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-fondue","name":"Fondue","nameAlt":"Melted Cheese Dip","aliases":["Cheese Fondue","Fondue moitié-moitié"],"course":"main","type":"cheese","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"120g Gruyere cheese · 120g Emmental cheese · 100ml dry white wine · 5ml lemon juice · 5g cornstarch · 1 clove garlic · 2g black pepper · 150g bread","ingredients12":"1440g Gruyere cheese · 1440g Emmental cheese · 1200ml dry white wine · 60ml lemon juice · 60g cornstarch · 12 cloves garlic · 24g black pepper · 1800g bread","method":"Rub a pot with garlic and discard the clove. Heat the wine with lemon juice on medium until warm, about 3 minutes. Gradually add grated cheese while stirring constantly until melted, about 5 minutes. Mix cornstarch with a little wine and stir into the pot. Continue cooking on low heat until smooth and thick, about 4 minutes. Season with black pepper and keep warm over low heat. Serve with cubed bread for dipping.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 30g · fat 32g","storage":"Store leftovers refrigerated and reheat gently.","chefNotes":"Use good quality cheese and wine for best flavor.","pairsWith":"white wine · pickles · cured meats","trivia":"Fondue became a Swiss national dish in the 20th century.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-raclette","name":"Raclette","nameAlt":"Melted Cheese with Potatoes","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"cheese","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"200g raclette cheese · 200g potatoes · 50g pickles · 50g pearl onions · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g raclette cheese · 2400g potatoes · 600g pickles · 600g pearl onions · 24g black pepper","method":"Boil potatoes in salted water until tender, about 20 minutes. Slice the raclette cheese into portions. Heat a grill or raclette machine to medium heat. Place cheese under heat until melted and bubbling, about 5 minutes. Serve melted cheese over hot potatoes. Add pickles and onions on the side. Season lightly with black pepper.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 40g · fat 38g","storage":"Keep components refrigerated separately.","chefNotes":"Use waxy potatoes for best texture.","pairsWith":"white wine · cured meats · bread","trivia":"Raclette is both a dish and the name of the cheese used.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-rosti","name":"Rosti","nameAlt":"Crispy Potato Cake","aliases":["Rösti"],"course":"side","type":"fried","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"300g potatoes · 20g butter · 5g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"3600g potatoes · 240g butter · 60g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Peel and grate the potatoes coarsely. Squeeze out excess moisture. Heat butter in a pan on medium heat for 2 minutes. Add potatoes and press into a flat cake. Cook until golden brown on one side, about 8 minutes. Flip carefully and cook the other side for another 8 minutes. Season with salt and pepper before serving.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 45g · fat 15g","storage":"Store refrigerated and reheat in a pan.","chefNotes":"Parboil potatoes for easier shaping if needed.","pairsWith":"fried eggs · sausages · salad","trivia":"Rosti originated as a farmer's breakfast dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-zurcher-geschnetzeltes","name":"Zurcher Geschnetzeltes","nameAlt":"Zurich Sliced Veal","aliases":["Zürcher Geschnetzeltes"],"course":"main","type":"saute","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"special","ingredients":"200g veal · 50g mushrooms · 50ml cream · 50ml white wine · 20g butter · 10g onion · 5g flour · 2g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g veal · 600g mushrooms · 600ml cream · 600ml white wine · 240g butter · 120g onion · 60g flour · 24g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Slice veal into thin strips. Melt butter in a pan on medium heat for 2 minutes. Add veal and cook quickly until browned, about 4 minutes. Remove meat and set aside. Saute onions and mushrooms until soft, about 5 minutes. Stir in flour and cook briefly for 1 minute. Add wine and cream, simmering until thickened, about 5 minutes. Return veal to the pan and heat through, seasoning with salt and pepper.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 10g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate and reheat gently.","chefNotes":"Do not overcook veal to keep it tender.","pairsWith":"rosti · white wine · green beans","trivia":"This dish is a specialty from Zurich.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-alplermagronen","name":"Alplermagronen","nameAlt":"Swiss Alpine Macaroni","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"pasta","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g pasta · 100g potatoes · 50g cheese · 50ml cream · 30g onion · 20g butter · 5g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1200g pasta · 1200g potatoes · 600g cheese · 600ml cream · 360g onion · 240g butter · 60g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Boil pasta and diced potatoes together until tender, about 10 minutes. Drain and set aside. Melt butter in a pan and cook sliced onions until caramelized, about 10 minutes. Heat cream and add grated cheese until melted, about 5 minutes. Combine pasta, potatoes, and sauce in a pot. Stir well and season with salt and pepper. Top with caramelized onions before serving.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":650,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 70g · fat 30g","storage":"Store refrigerated and reheat with a splash of milk.","chefNotes":"Serve with applesauce for a traditional touch.","pairsWith":"applesauce · salad · cider","trivia":"This dish was popular among Alpine herdsmen.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-birchermuesli","name":"Bircher Muesli","nameAlt":"Overnight Oats with Apple","aliases":["Birchermüesli"],"course":"starter","type":"cereal","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"breakfast","ingredients":"50g oats · 100ml milk · 100g apple · 10g honey · 20g yogurt · 10g almonds","ingredients12":"600g oats · 1200ml milk · 1200g apple · 120g honey · 240g yogurt · 120g almonds","method":"Soak oats in milk in a bowl. Refrigerate for at least 10 minutes. Grate the apple and mix into the oats. Stir in yogurt and honey. Add chopped almonds. Mix thoroughly until creamy. Serve chilled.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 45g · fat 10g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and consume within one day.","chefNotes":"Let it rest overnight for deeper flavor.","pairsWith":"fresh fruit · tea · coffee","trivia":"It was invented by Swiss physician Maximilian Bircher-Brenner.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-bundnerfleisch","name":"Bundnerfleisch","nameAlt":"Air-Dried Beef","aliases":["Bündnerfleisch"],"course":"starter","type":"cured","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"150g beef · 5g salt · 2g black pepper · 2g juniper berries","ingredients12":"1800g beef · 60g salt · 24g black pepper · 24g juniper berries","method":"Trim the beef and rub with salt, pepper, and crushed juniper berries. Place in a container and refrigerate for 10 minutes active prep. Hang in a cool dry place to cure. Allow air drying until firm. Slice thinly before serving. Serve chilled as a snack. Keep preparation clean and controlled.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 1g · fat 10g","storage":"Store in a cool dry place or refrigerate.","chefNotes":"Curing takes several weeks in practice.","pairsWith":"cheese · bread · wine","trivia":"It originates from the canton of Graubunden.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-saffron-risotto","name":"Risotto allo Zafferano Ticinese","nameAlt":"Saffron Risotto","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"rice","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"special","ingredients":"100g risotto rice · 500ml chicken stock · 50ml white wine · 20g butter · 20g parmesan cheese · 0.1g saffron · 10g onion · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g risotto rice · 6000ml chicken stock · 600ml white wine · 240g butter · 240g parmesan cheese · 1.2g saffron · 120g onion · 24g salt","method":"Heat butter in a pan and cook chopped onion until soft, about 4 minutes. Add rice and toast lightly for 2 minutes. Pour in wine and let it evaporate. Add warm stock gradually while stirring constantly over medium heat, about 18 minutes. Stir in saffron dissolved in stock. Continue until rice is creamy and tender. Finish with parmesan and season with salt.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 60g · fat 15g","storage":"Refrigerate and reheat with stock.","chefNotes":"Stir constantly for creamy texture.","pairsWith":"white wine · salad · grilled vegetables","trivia":"Saffron adds color and aroma to the dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-nusstorte","name":"Engadiner Nusstorte","nameAlt":"Nut Caramel Tart","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"tart","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g flour · 50g butter · 30g sugar · 50g walnuts · 50ml cream · 20g honey · 1 egg","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 600g butter · 360g sugar · 600g walnuts · 600ml cream · 240g honey · 12 eggs","method":"Mix flour, butter, sugar, and egg to form dough. Chill for 10 minutes. Roll out and line a tart pan. Heat sugar, honey, and cream to make caramel, about 5 minutes. Stir in walnuts and cook briefly. Fill the tart shell with the mixture. Cover with pastry lid. Bake at 180°C for 30 minutes until golden. Cool before slicing.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 50g · fat 35g","storage":"Store in an airtight container.","chefNotes":"Let it cool fully for clean slices.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · whipped cream","trivia":"This tart comes from the Engadin valley.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-basler-laeckerli","name":"Basler Lackerli","nameAlt":"Spiced Honey Cookies","aliases":["Basler Läckerli"],"course":"dessert","type":"biscuit","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"100g flour · 80g honey · 50g sugar · 30g almonds · 20g candied peel · 2g cinnamon · 2g cloves","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 960g honey · 600g sugar · 360g almonds · 240g candied peel · 24g cinnamon · 24g cloves","method":"Heat honey and sugar until dissolved, about 3 minutes. Mix in flour, almonds, candied peel, and spices. Roll dough thin and place on a tray. Bake at 180°C for 15 minutes until firm. Cool slightly and cut into rectangles. Let cool completely before serving. Store once fully cooled.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 50g · fat 8g","storage":"Keep in airtight container for freshness.","chefNotes":"Flavor improves after a few days.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee · mulled wine","trivia":"These cookies originate from Basel.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-maluns","name":"Maluns","nameAlt":"Crispy Potato Flour Crumble","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"fried","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g potatoes · 50g flour · 20g butter · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g potatoes · 600g flour · 240g butter · 60g salt","method":"Boil potatoes until tender, about 20 minutes. Peel and grate coarsely. Mix with flour and salt. Heat butter in a pan on medium heat. Add mixture and cook, stirring constantly, until crumbly and golden, about 15 minutes. Break into small pieces while cooking. Serve hot as a side dish.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 60g · fat 15g","storage":"Refrigerate and reheat in a pan.","chefNotes":"Keep stirring to prevent sticking.","pairsWith":"cheese · applesauce · sausages","trivia":"Maluns is a traditional dish from Graubunden.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-cervelat","name":"Cervelat","nameAlt":"Swiss Sausage","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"sausage","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"grill","ingredients":"200g cervelat sausage · 100g bread · 20g mustard","ingredients12":"2400g cervelat sausage · 1200g bread · 240g mustard","method":"Score the ends of the sausage. Grill over medium heat until browned, about 10 minutes. Turn occasionally to cook evenly. Warm bread slightly on the grill. Serve sausage with bread and mustard. Enjoy immediately while hot.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 30g · fat 35g","storage":"Refrigerate uncooked sausages.","chefNotes":"Do not overcook to keep it juicy.","pairsWith":"mustard · bread · beer","trivia":"Cervelat is considered Switzerland's national sausage.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-berner-platte","name":"Berner Platte","nameAlt":"Bernese Meat Platter","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"platter","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"150g smoked pork · 100g beef · 100g potatoes · 80g cabbage · 50g sausage · 5g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g smoked pork · 1200g beef · 1200g potatoes · 960g cabbage · 600g sausage · 60g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Place pork and beef in a pot with water and bring to a boil over medium heat for 10 minutes. Reduce heat and simmer until tender, about 60 minutes. Add chopped cabbage and cook for 15 minutes. Boil potatoes separately until soft, about 20 minutes. Grill or pan-fry sausage until browned, about 10 minutes. Arrange all components on a platter and season with salt and pepper. Serve hot.","cookTime":"90 min","kcal":700,"nutrition":"protein 45g · carbs 40g · fat 40g","storage":"Refrigerate leftovers and reheat thoroughly.","chefNotes":"Use a mix of cured meats for authentic flavor.","pairsWith":"mustard · rye bread · beer","trivia":"This dish commemorates a historic Bernese victory in 1798.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-capuns","name":"Capuns","nameAlt":"Swiss Chard Dumplings","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"dumpling","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g flour · 1 egg · 50ml milk · 50g cured meat · 100g Swiss chard · 20g cheese · 20g butter · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 12 eggs · 600ml milk · 600g cured meat · 1200g Swiss chard · 240g cheese · 240g butter · 24g salt","method":"Mix flour, egg, milk, and salt into a dough. Stir in finely chopped cured meat. Place small portions onto Swiss chard leaves and roll. Boil in salted water on medium heat until firm, about 10 minutes. Melt butter and add grated cheese. Toss cooked dumplings in the butter and cheese mixture. Serve hot.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 50g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate and reheat gently.","chefNotes":"Blanch leaves briefly for easier rolling.","pairsWith":"salad · white wine · pickles","trivia":"Capuns originate from the canton of Graubunden.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-polenta","name":"Polenta Ticinese","nameAlt":"Cornmeal Porridge","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"porridge","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g cornmeal · 400ml water · 5g salt · 20g butter · 20g cheese","ingredients12":"1200g cornmeal · 4800ml water · 60g salt · 240g butter · 240g cheese","method":"Bring water and salt to a boil over medium heat for 5 minutes. Gradually whisk in cornmeal. Reduce heat and cook while stirring constantly, about 30 minutes. Stir in butter and grated cheese. Continue cooking until thick and smooth. Serve hot as a side dish.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 55g · fat 12g","storage":"Refrigerate and reheat with water or milk.","chefNotes":"Stir continuously to avoid lumps.","pairsWith":"stew · mushrooms · grilled meat","trivia":"Polenta is popular in the Italian-speaking region of Switzerland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-gesottene-kalbszunge","name":"Gesottene Kalbszunge","nameAlt":"Boiled Veal Tongue","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"boiled","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"special","ingredients":"300g veal tongue · 50g carrot · 50g onion · 20g celery · 5g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"3600g veal tongue · 600g carrot · 600g onion · 240g celery · 60g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Rinse the veal tongue thoroughly. Place in a pot with water, carrot, onion, and celery. Bring to a boil over medium heat for 10 minutes. Reduce heat and simmer until tender, about 90 minutes. Remove and peel the outer skin while warm. Slice and season with salt and pepper. Serve hot or cold.","cookTime":"100 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 10g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate and consume within two days.","chefNotes":"Peel while warm for easier handling.","pairsWith":"mustard · potatoes · salad","trivia":"This dish was once considered a delicacy in Swiss cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-kaseschnitte","name":"Kaseschnitte","nameAlt":"Swiss Cheese Toast","aliases":["Käseschnitte"],"course":"main","type":"toast","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g bread · 80g cheese · 50ml white wine · 10g butter · 1 egg · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1200g bread · 960g cheese · 600ml white wine · 120g butter · 12 eggs · 24g black pepper","method":"Butter the bread slices and place in a pan. Add wine and top with grated cheese. Cook on medium heat until cheese melts, about 5 minutes. Crack an egg on top and cook until set, about 4 minutes. Season with black pepper. Serve hot.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 30g · fat 25g","storage":"Best eaten fresh; refrigerate leftovers.","chefNotes":"Use stale bread for better texture.","pairsWith":"salad · white wine · pickles","trivia":"Kaseschnitte is a simple Alpine comfort dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-zwetschgenkuchen","name":"Zwetschgenkuchen","nameAlt":"Plum Cake","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"autumn","ingredients":"100g flour · 50g sugar · 50g butter · 1 egg · 150g plums · 5g baking powder","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 600g sugar · 600g butter · 12 eggs · 1800g plums · 60g baking powder","method":"Mix flour, sugar, butter, egg, and baking powder into a batter. Spread into a baking tin. Arrange halved plums on top. Bake at 180°C for 35 minutes until golden. Allow to cool slightly before slicing. Serve warm or at room temperature.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 45g · fat 18g","storage":"Store in an airtight container.","chefNotes":"Use ripe plums for sweetness.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · cream","trivia":"Plum cakes are popular during harvest season.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-schaumkuss","name":"Schaumkuss","nameAlt":"Chocolate Marshmallow Treat","aliases":["Mohrenkopf"],"course":"dessert","type":"confectionery","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"1 wafer · 30g sugar · 20g egg white · 50g chocolate","ingredients12":"12 wafers · 360g sugar · 240g egg white · 600g chocolate","method":"Whip egg whites and sugar until stiff peaks form. Pipe onto wafers into dome shapes. Chill briefly to set, about 10 minutes. Melt chocolate over low heat for 5 minutes. Dip the domes into chocolate until fully coated. Let set until firm before serving.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 3g · carbs 30g · fat 10g","storage":"Store in a cool dry place.","chefNotes":"Work quickly when coating with chocolate.","pairsWith":"coffee · milk · tea","trivia":"These treats are popular across Switzerland and Germany.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-fasnachtschuechli","name":"Fasnachtschuechli","nameAlt":"Carnival Fried Pastry","aliases":["Fasnachtschüechli"],"course":"dessert","type":"fried","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g flour · 20g sugar · 1 egg · 20g butter · 50ml milk · 200ml vegetable oil","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 240g sugar · 12 eggs · 240g butter · 600ml milk · 2400ml vegetable oil","method":"Mix flour, sugar, egg, butter, and milk into a dough. Roll thinly and cut into shapes. Heat oil to 180°C. Fry pieces until golden, about 2 minutes per side. Remove and drain on paper. Serve dusted with sugar.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 45g · fat 20g","storage":"Store in airtight container for one day.","chefNotes":"Roll dough very thin for crisp texture.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · sugar","trivia":"These pastries are eaten during carnival season.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-rueblitorte","name":"Rueblitorte","nameAlt":"Carrot Cake","aliases":["Rüeblitorte"],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"100g carrots · 80g sugar · 80g almonds · 2 eggs · 30g flour · 5g baking powder","ingredients12":"1200g carrots · 960g sugar · 960g almonds · 24 eggs · 360g flour · 60g baking powder","method":"Grate carrots finely. Beat eggs and sugar until fluffy, about 5 minutes. Fold in almonds, flour, and baking powder. Add grated carrots and mix well. Pour into a baking tin. Bake at 180°C for 35 minutes until set. Cool before serving.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 40g · fat 22g","storage":"Store in an airtight container.","chefNotes":"Add lemon zest for freshness.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee · cream","trivia":"This cake is a specialty from Aargau.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"switzerland-heisse-schokolade","name":"Heisse Schokolade","nameAlt":"Hot Chocolate","aliases":[],"course":"drink","type":"beverage","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Switzerland","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"200ml milk · 40g dark chocolate · 10g sugar","ingredients12":"2400ml milk · 480g dark chocolate · 120g sugar","method":"Heat milk in a saucepan over medium heat for 3 minutes. Add chopped chocolate and stir until melted, about 4 minutes. Add sugar and stir until dissolved. Heat gently until smooth and hot. Serve immediately.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 30g · fat 12g","storage":"Best consumed fresh.","chefNotes":"Use high-quality chocolate for richness.","pairsWith":"pastries · biscuits · cream","trivia":"Swiss chocolate is world-renowned for quality.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-wiener-schnitzel","name":"Wiener Schnitzel","nameAlt":"Breaded Veal Cutlet","aliases":["Schnitzel Wiener Art"],"course":"main","type":"cutlet","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"180g veal cutlet · 40g flour · 1 egg · 60g breadcrumbs · 60ml sunflower oil · 5g salt · 5g lemon","ingredients12":"2160g veal cutlet · 480g flour · 12 eggs · 720g breadcrumbs · 720ml sunflower oil · 60g salt · 60g lemon","method":"Pound the veal to an even thin thickness. Season lightly with salt on both sides. Dredge in flour, then dip into beaten egg. Coat evenly with breadcrumbs without pressing too hard. Heat sunflower oil to medium and fry until golden, about 3 to 4 minutes per side. Turn once and keep the crust fluffy. Remove and drain briefly on paper. Serve immediately with a squeeze of lemon.","cookTime":"10-12 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 38g · carbs 32g · fat 24g","storage":"Store refrigerated for up to 2 days and reheat in a pan.","chefNotes":"Do not press the breadcrumbs or the crust will become dense.","pairsWith":"potato salad · cucumber salad · lemon wedges","trivia":"This dish is one of Austria’s most famous national specialties.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-tafelspitz","name":"Tafelspitz","nameAlt":"Boiled Beef with Vegetables","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"boiled","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"Sunday lunch","ingredients":"250g beef rump · 100g carrot · 80g leek · 80g celery root · 1 onion · 5g salt · 2g black peppercorns · 5g parsley","ingredients12":"3000g beef rump · 1200g carrot · 960g leek · 960g celery root · 12 onions · 60g salt · 24g black peppercorns · 60g parsley","method":"Place the beef in a pot with cold water and bring to a gentle simmer. Skim off any foam that rises. Add chopped vegetables and peppercorns. Simmer on low heat for about 90 minutes until tender. Season with salt toward the end. Slice the beef against the grain. Serve with broth and vegetables. Garnish with parsley.","cookTime":"90 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 45g · carbs 10g · fat 28g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 3 days in its broth.","chefNotes":"Adding salt later keeps the beef more tender.","pairsWith":"apple horseradish · boiled potatoes · spinach","trivia":"Tafelspitz was a favorite dish of Emperor Franz Joseph I.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-kaesespaetzle","name":"Käsespätzle","nameAlt":"Cheesy Egg Noodles","aliases":["Kasnocken"],"course":"main","type":"pasta","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g flour · 1 egg · 60ml milk · 80g cheese · 40g onion · 20g butter · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 12 eggs · 720ml milk · 960g cheese · 480g onion · 240g butter · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour, egg, milk, and salt into a soft dough. Push the dough through a spätzle maker into boiling water. Cook until the pieces float, about 2 minutes. Drain and set aside. Melt butter and fry sliced onions until golden on medium heat. Add the spätzle and toss with grated cheese. Stir until the cheese melts evenly. Serve hot with crispy onions on top.","cookTime":"20-25 min","kcal":620,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 68g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days and reheat gently.","chefNotes":"Use a strong melting cheese for best texture.","pairsWith":"green salad · pickles · apple juice","trivia":"This dish is popular across the Alpine regions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-apfelstrudel","name":"Apfelstrudel","nameAlt":"Apple Strudel","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"coffee time","ingredients":"120g apple · 60g flour · 30g butter · 30g sugar · 20g raisins · 5g cinnamon · 20g breadcrumbs","ingredients12":"1440g apple · 720g flour · 360g butter · 360g sugar · 240g raisins · 60g cinnamon · 240g breadcrumbs","method":"Prepare a thin dough using flour and water and rest it. Stretch the dough until very thin on a floured cloth. Mix sliced apples with sugar, cinnamon, and raisins. Spread breadcrumbs over the dough to absorb moisture. Add the apple mixture evenly. Roll the strudel using the cloth. Brush with melted butter. Bake at 180°C for about 35 minutes until golden.","cookTime":"35-40 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 70g · fat 16g","storage":"Keep covered at room temperature for 1 day or refrigerate.","chefNotes":"Stretch the dough carefully to avoid tearing.","pairsWith":"vanilla sauce · whipped cream · coffee","trivia":"Strudel dough is traditionally stretched by hand until paper-thin.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-sachertorte","name":"Sachertorte","nameAlt":"Chocolate Apricot Cake","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"80g dark chocolate · 60g butter · 60g sugar · 2 eggs · 50g flour · 40g apricot jam","ingredients12":"960g dark chocolate · 720g butter · 720g sugar · 24 eggs · 600g flour · 480g apricot jam","method":"Melt chocolate and butter together gently. Beat eggs and sugar until light. Fold melted chocolate into the egg mixture. Add flour and mix gently. Pour into a greased tin. Bake at 170°C for about 30 minutes. Cool and slice horizontally. Spread apricot jam inside and over the cake. Finish with a chocolate glaze.","cookTime":"30-35 min","kcal":540,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 52g · fat 32g","storage":"Store in a cool place for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let the cake rest overnight for best flavor.","pairsWith":"whipped cream · coffee · berries","trivia":"Sachertorte originated in Vienna in 1832.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-goulash","name":"Gulasch","nameAlt":"Beef Paprika Stew","aliases":["Wiener Gulasch"],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g beef · 100g onion · 10g paprika · 10g tomato paste · 5g garlic · 10ml oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g beef · 1200g onion · 120g paprika · 120g tomato paste · 60g garlic · 120ml oil · 60g salt","method":"Heat oil and cook chopped onions until deeply browned. Add garlic and paprika briefly without burning. Stir in beef cubes and sear lightly. Add tomato paste and mix well. Pour in water to cover and simmer. Cook on low heat for about 90 minutes until tender. Stir occasionally to prevent sticking. Season with salt and adjust consistency.","cookTime":"90 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 40g · carbs 12g · fat 32g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days or freeze.","chefNotes":"Slow cooking deepens the flavor significantly.","pairsWith":"bread · potatoes · pickles","trivia":"Austrian goulash differs from Hungarian by being thicker and onion-rich.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-knodel","name":"Knödel","nameAlt":"Bread Dumplings","aliases":["Semmelknödel"],"course":"side","type":"dumpling","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g bread · 60ml milk · 1 egg · 30g onion · 10g butter · 5g parsley · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1440g bread · 720ml milk · 12 eggs · 360g onion · 120g butter · 60g parsley · 60g salt","method":"Cut bread into small cubes. Warm milk and pour over bread to soften. Cook onions in butter until soft. Mix bread with egg, onion, parsley, and salt. Form into compact dumplings. Bring water to a gentle simmer. Cook dumplings for about 15 minutes until firm. Remove carefully and drain. Serve warm as a side.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 45g · fat 10g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and reheat in hot water.","chefNotes":"Do not boil vigorously or dumplings may break apart.","pairsWith":"gravy · roasted meat · cabbage","trivia":"Knödel are a staple side dish across Austria.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-linzertorte","name":"Linzertorte","nameAlt":"Nut Jam Tart","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"tart","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g flour · 80g ground almonds · 80g butter · 60g sugar · 1 egg · 60g raspberry jam","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 960g ground almonds · 960g butter · 720g sugar · 12 eggs · 720g raspberry jam","method":"Cream butter and sugar until smooth. Add egg and mix well. Stir in flour and ground almonds. Chill the dough briefly. Roll out and line a tart tin. Spread jam evenly over the base. Create a lattice pattern with remaining dough. Bake at 180°C for about 30 minutes. Cool before slicing.","cookTime":"30-35 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 50g · fat 28g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for 3 days.","chefNotes":"Chilling the dough makes it easier to handle.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee · whipped cream","trivia":"Linzertorte is considered one of the oldest known cakes in the world.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-kartoffelsalat","name":"Erdäpfelsalat","nameAlt":"Austrian Potato Salad","aliases":["Kartoffelsalat"],"course":"side","type":"salad","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g potato · 30ml vinegar · 20ml oil · 20g onion · 5g mustard · 5g sugar · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g potato · 360ml vinegar · 240ml oil · 240g onion · 60g mustard · 60g sugar · 60g salt","method":"Boil potatoes until tender and let them cool slightly. Slice them while still warm. Mix vinegar, oil, mustard, sugar, and salt. Add finely chopped onion. Pour dressing over the potatoes. Toss gently to coat evenly. Let sit for 10 minutes to absorb flavors. Adjust seasoning if needed. Serve slightly warm or at room temperature.","cookTime":"25-30 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 38g · fat 12g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use waxy potatoes for best texture.","pairsWith":"schnitzel · sausages · bread","trivia":"This potato salad is typically served without mayonnaise.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-kaiser-schmarrn","name":"Kaiserschmarrn","nameAlt":"Shredded Pancake","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pancake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"80g flour · 2 eggs · 100ml milk · 30g sugar · 20g butter · 20g raisins","ingredients12":"960g flour · 24 eggs · 1200ml milk · 360g sugar · 240g butter · 240g raisins","method":"Whisk flour, milk, and egg yolks into a smooth batter. Beat egg whites with sugar until soft peaks form. Fold gently into the batter. Melt butter in a pan over medium heat. Pour batter and cook until set on the bottom. Tear into pieces and turn. Add raisins and cook until golden, about 5 minutes. Sprinkle with sugar and serve hot.","cookTime":"15-20 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 14g · carbs 60g · fat 24g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Do not overmix after adding egg whites to keep it fluffy.","pairsWith":"apple compote · plum sauce · powdered sugar","trivia":"The dish is said to have been favored by Emperor Franz Joseph.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-brettljause","name":"Brettljause","nameAlt":"Austrian Snack Platter","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"platter","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"social","ingredients":"80g cured ham · 60g cheese · 50g bread · 40g pickles · 30g radish","ingredients12":"960g cured ham · 720g cheese · 600g bread · 480g pickles · 360g radish","method":"Slice cured ham and cheese into bite-sized portions. Arrange them neatly on a wooden board. Add slices of bread alongside. Include pickles and sliced radish for freshness. Keep everything evenly spaced. Serve at room temperature. Encourage sharing among guests. Enjoy as a casual starter.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 30g · fat 24g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and assemble fresh when serving.","chefNotes":"Use a mix of textures for a balanced platter.","pairsWith":"beer · mustard · fresh bread","trivia":"Brettljause is traditionally served on a wooden board in alpine regions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-frittatensuppe","name":"Frittatensuppe","nameAlt":"Pancake Strip Soup","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"300ml beef broth · 1 egg · 40g flour · 80ml milk · 5g salt · 5g parsley","ingredients12":"3600ml beef broth · 12 eggs · 480g flour · 960ml milk · 60g salt · 60g parsley","method":"Mix egg, flour, milk, and salt into a thin batter. Cook thin pancakes in a pan over medium heat, about 2 minutes per side. Let them cool slightly. Roll the pancakes and slice into thin strips. Heat beef broth until simmering. Add the pancake strips to the broth. Warm through for 2 to 3 minutes. Garnish with chopped parsley and serve hot.","cookTime":"15-20 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 30g · fat 10g","storage":"Store broth and pancakes separately for best texture.","chefNotes":"Keep pancakes thin so they slice easily.","pairsWith":"bread · salad · tea","trivia":"Frittaten are similar to French crêpes but used in soup.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-speckknoedel","name":"Speckknödel","nameAlt":"Bacon Bread Dumplings","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"dumpling","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"mountain meal","ingredients":"120g bread · 60ml milk · 1 egg · 50g bacon · 30g onion · 5g parsley · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1440g bread · 720ml milk · 12 eggs · 600g bacon · 360g onion · 60g parsley · 60g salt","method":"Cut bread into cubes and soak with warm milk. Fry diced bacon and onion on medium heat until golden, about 5 minutes. Mix with bread, egg, parsley, and salt. Form into firm dumplings. Simmer gently in salted water for about 15 minutes until cooked through. Remove and drain carefully. Serve hot as a main or in broth. Garnish with extra parsley if desired.","cookTime":"20-25 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 38g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days and reheat in hot water.","chefNotes":"Ensure dumplings are compact to prevent breaking.","pairsWith":"sauerkraut · broth · mustard","trivia":"Speckknödel are especially popular in Tyrol.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-tiroler-groestl","name":"Tiroler Gröstl","nameAlt":"Tyrolean Fried Potatoes and Meat","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"fried","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"hearty meal","ingredients":"200g potato · 120g beef · 40g onion · 20g butter · 1 egg · 5g salt · 5g parsley","ingredients12":"2400g potato · 1440g beef · 480g onion · 240g butter · 12 eggs · 60g salt · 60g parsley","method":"Boil potatoes until just tender and slice them. Heat butter in a pan on medium heat. Fry onions until golden, about 4 minutes. Add beef pieces and cook until browned. Add potatoes and fry until crispy, about 8 minutes. Season with salt and mix gently. Fry an egg separately to desired doneness. Serve topped with the fried egg and parsley.","cookTime":"20-25 min","kcal":560,"nutrition":"protein 32g · carbs 40g · fat 30g","storage":"Store refrigerated for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use leftover meat for authentic flavor.","pairsWith":"pickles · cabbage salad · beer","trivia":"This dish originated as a way to use leftovers in alpine inns.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-leberkaese","name":"Leberkäse","nameAlt":"Baked Meat Loaf Slice","aliases":["Fleischkäse"],"course":"main","type":"loaf","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"street food","ingredients":"200g ground pork · 100g ground beef · 5g salt · 2g marjoram · 2g black pepper · 30ml water","ingredients12":"2400g ground pork · 1200g ground beef · 60g salt · 24g marjoram · 24g black pepper · 360ml water","method":"Mix ground pork and beef with salt, marjoram, pepper, and water until smooth. Press the mixture into a loaf tin. Smooth the top with a wet spatula. Bake at 180°C for about 60 minutes until browned. Let rest briefly before slicing. Serve warm in thick slices. Optionally crisp slices in a pan for extra texture.","cookTime":"60-65 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 4g · fat 38g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days and reheat slices.","chefNotes":"A smooth texture is key, so mix thoroughly.","pairsWith":"bread roll · mustard · pickles","trivia":"Despite its name, it typically contains no liver.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-zwetschkenknoedel","name":"Zwetschkenknödel","nameAlt":"Plum Dumplings","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"dumpling","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"150g potato · 60g flour · 1 egg · 80g plum · 20g butter · 20g sugar · 20g breadcrumbs","ingredients12":"1800g potato · 720g flour · 12 eggs · 960g plum · 240g butter · 240g sugar · 240g breadcrumbs","method":"Boil and mash potatoes, then mix with flour and egg to form dough. Wrap each plum with dough and seal well. Bring water to a gentle simmer. Cook dumplings for about 15 minutes until they float. Melt butter and toast breadcrumbs on medium heat until golden. Roll cooked dumplings in the crumbs. Sprinkle with sugar and serve warm.","cookTime":"25-30 min","kcal":460,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 70g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days and reheat gently.","chefNotes":"Seal the dough tightly to prevent leaks.","pairsWith":"vanilla sauce · cinnamon sugar · tea","trivia":"These dumplings are a seasonal favorite when plums are ripe.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-topfenstrudel","name":"Topfenstrudel","nameAlt":"Quark Strudel","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"coffee time","ingredients":"80g quark · 60g flour · 30g butter · 30g sugar · 1 egg · 20g raisins","ingredients12":"960g quark · 720g flour · 360g butter · 360g sugar · 12 eggs · 240g raisins","method":"Prepare a thin dough and let it rest. Mix quark with sugar, egg, and raisins. Stretch the dough on a cloth until thin. Spread the filling evenly across the surface. Roll carefully using the cloth. Brush with melted butter. Bake at 180°C for about 35 minutes until golden. Slice and serve warm or cooled.","cookTime":"35-40 min","kcal":430,"nutrition":"protein 14g · carbs 50g · fat 18g","storage":"Store in the fridge for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overfill or the strudel may burst.","pairsWith":"powdered sugar · coffee · vanilla sauce","trivia":"Topfen is the Austrian term for quark cheese.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-palatschinken","name":"Palatschinken","nameAlt":"Thin Pancakes","aliases":["Palacinky"],"course":"dessert","type":"pancake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"80g flour · 1 egg · 120ml milk · 20g butter · 30g apricot jam","ingredients12":"960g flour · 12 eggs · 1440ml milk · 240g butter · 360g apricot jam","method":"Whisk flour, egg, and milk into a smooth batter. Heat a pan with a little butter over medium heat. Pour a thin layer of batter and cook about 1 to 2 minutes per side. Stack the pancakes as you go. Spread apricot jam on each pancake. Roll or fold them neatly. Serve warm with a dusting of sugar if desired.","cookTime":"15-20 min","kcal":360,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 48g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Keep pancakes thin for the best texture.","pairsWith":"powdered sugar · fruit compote · tea","trivia":"Palatschinken are similar to French crêpes.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-rindsuppe","name":"Rindsuppe","nameAlt":"Clear Beef Soup","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"300ml water · 200g beef bones · 80g carrot · 50g celery · 30g onion · 5g salt · 2g black peppercorns","ingredients12":"3600ml water · 2400g beef bones · 960g carrot · 600g celery · 360g onion · 60g salt · 24g black peppercorns","method":"Place beef bones in cold water and bring to a gentle simmer. Skim impurities as they rise. Add chopped vegetables and peppercorns. Simmer on low heat for about 120 minutes. Season with salt toward the end. Strain the broth carefully. Serve clear and hot. Optionally add garnishes like noodles or herbs.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":180,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 6g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days or freeze.","chefNotes":"A slow simmer keeps the broth clear.","pairsWith":"bread · dumplings · herbs","trivia":"This broth forms the base of many Austrian soups.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-salzburger-nockerl","name":"Salzburger Nockerl","nameAlt":"Sweet Soufflé Dumplings","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"souffle","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"special","ingredients":"3 egg whites · 30g sugar · 10g flour · 10g butter · 10g powdered sugar","ingredients12":"36 egg whites · 360g sugar · 120g flour · 120g butter · 120g powdered sugar","method":"Beat egg whites with sugar until stiff peaks form. Fold in flour gently. Butter a baking dish and shape the mixture into mounds. Bake at 200°C for about 10 minutes until lightly golden. Remove carefully from the oven. Dust with powdered sugar immediately. Serve hot as it deflates quickly.","cookTime":"10-12 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 28g · fat 8g","storage":"Best eaten immediately after baking.","chefNotes":"Serve quickly as the soufflé collapses fast.","pairsWith":"berry sauce · cream · tea","trivia":"This dessert represents the three hills around Salzburg.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-vanillekipferl","name":"Vanillekipferl","nameAlt":"Vanilla Crescent Cookies","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cookie","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"100g flour · 80g butter · 40g sugar · 40g ground almonds · 5g vanilla sugar","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 960g butter · 480g sugar · 480g ground almonds · 60g vanilla sugar","method":"Mix flour, butter, sugar, and almonds into a dough. Chill briefly to firm up. Shape small crescents by hand. Place on a baking tray. Bake at 180°C for about 12 minutes until pale golden. While warm, roll gently in vanilla sugar. Let cool completely before serving.","cookTime":"12-15 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 28g · fat 20g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Handle gently when warm to prevent breaking.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · milk","trivia":"These cookies are a staple during Austrian Christmas baking.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"austria-krautfleckerl","name":"Krautfleckerl","nameAlt":"Cabbage Pasta","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"pasta","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"western-europe","country":"Austria","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g pasta · 150g cabbage · 30g onion · 20g butter · 5g sugar · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1440g pasta · 1800g cabbage · 360g onion · 240g butter · 60g sugar · 60g salt","method":"Cook pasta in salted boiling water until tender, about 8 minutes. Drain and set aside. Melt butter in a pan and cook sliced onion until soft. Add shredded cabbage and cook on medium heat for about 10 minutes until caramelized. Sprinkle sugar and stir well. Add cooked pasta and toss to combine. Season with salt and serve hot.","cookTime":"20-25 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 60g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Caramelizing the cabbage adds depth of flavor.","pairsWith":"salad · pickles · yogurt","trivia":"A simple dish often made with pantry ingredients.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-kottbullar","name":"Kottbullar","nameAlt":"Swedish Meatballs with Cream Sauce","aliases":["Köttbullar","Swedish Meatballs"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"family dinner","ingredients":"150g ground beef · 50g ground pork · 20g onion · 5g garlic · 30ml cream · 20g breadcrumbs · 1 egg · 5g salt · 2g black pepper · 10ml butter","ingredients12":"1800g ground beef · 600g ground pork · 240g onion · 60g garlic · 360ml cream · 240g breadcrumbs · 12 eggs · 60g salt · 24g black pepper · 120ml butter","method":"Finely chop the onion and garlic and sauté them gently in butter until soft and translucent without browning. In a bowl, combine the ground beef and pork with breadcrumbs, cream, egg, salt, and pepper, then add the cooled onion mixture. Mix everything thoroughly until a smooth and slightly sticky mixture forms. Shape the mixture into small, even-sized balls using damp hands. Heat butter in a pan over medium heat and fry the meatballs in batches, turning frequently until they are evenly browned on all sides. Reduce the heat and continue cooking until the meatballs are fully cooked through and tender inside. Remove from the pan and allow them to rest briefly before serving.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 12g · fat 30g","storage":"Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days or freeze for up to 2 months.","chefNotes":"For extra tenderness, chill the mixture before shaping the meatballs.","pairsWith":"mashed potatoes · lingonberry sauce · pickled cucumber","trivia":"Swedish meatballs became globally popular through furniture store cafeterias.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-gravlax","name":"Gravlax","nameAlt":"Cured Salmon with Dill","aliases":["Gravad lax","Gravlaks"],"course":"starter","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"holiday","ingredients":"150g salmon fillet · 20g salt · 15g sugar · 5g dill · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g salmon fillet · 240g salt · 180g sugar · 60g dill · 24g black pepper","method":"Check the salmon fillet for any pin bones and remove them carefully with tweezers. Mix together the salt, sugar, and black pepper in a bowl until evenly combined. Rub the curing mixture thoroughly over the entire surface of the salmon. Place a generous layer of fresh dill on top of the fish and wrap it tightly in plastic wrap. Place the wrapped salmon in a shallow dish and weigh it down slightly to help the curing process. Refrigerate for 24 to 48 hours, turning the fish occasionally to ensure even curing. Once cured, scrape off the excess mixture and slice the salmon thinly before serving.","cookTime":"2880 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 5g · fat 20g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and consume within 3 days after curing.","chefNotes":"Slice the salmon very thinly for the best texture and flavor.","pairsWith":"mustard dill sauce · boiled potatoes · crispbread","trivia":"Gravlax was originally buried in sand by fishermen to ferment lightly.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-janssons-frestelse","name":"Janssons Frestelse","nameAlt":"Anchovy Potato Casserole","aliases":["Jansson's Temptation"],"course":"side","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"200g potatoes · 50g onion · 40g anchovies · 100ml cream · 10g butter · 5g salt · 2g white pepper","ingredients12":"2400g potatoes · 600g onion · 480g anchovies · 1200ml cream · 120g butter · 60g salt · 24g white pepper","method":"Peel the potatoes and cut them into thin matchsticks for even cooking. Slice the onion finely and sauté it gently in butter until soft and slightly sweet. Grease a baking dish and layer half of the potatoes evenly at the bottom. Add the sautéed onions and anchovies on top, distributing them evenly across the layer. Cover with the remaining potatoes and pour cream evenly over the dish. Season lightly with salt and white pepper. Bake in a preheated oven until the top is golden brown and the potatoes are tender when pierced. Allow it to rest briefly before serving so the layers set properly.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 15g · carbs 40g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate leftovers for up to 3 days and reheat gently in the oven.","chefNotes":"Do not over-salt as anchovies are already salty.","pairsWith":"pickled herring · rye bread · green salad","trivia":"The dish is named after an opera singer, not a biblical figure.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-raggmunk","name":"Raggmunk","nameAlt":"Swedish Potato Pancakes","aliases":["Potatisplattar","Raggmunks"],"course":"main","type":"vegetarian","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"everyday meal","ingredients":"200g potatoes · 50g flour · 100ml milk · 1 egg · 5g salt · 10ml oil","ingredients12":"2400g potatoes · 600g flour · 1200ml milk · 12 eggs · 60g salt · 120ml oil","method":"Peel and grate the potatoes coarsely, then squeeze out excess liquid to prevent sogginess. In a bowl, whisk together the flour, milk, egg, and salt to create a smooth batter. Fold the grated potatoes into the batter until evenly combined. Heat oil in a frying pan over medium heat until hot. Spoon portions of the mixture into the pan and flatten them into thin pancakes. Fry until the edges are crisp and the surface turns golden brown, then flip carefully and cook the other side. Continue cooking until the pancakes are fully cooked through and slightly crispy. Serve immediately while hot for the best texture.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 45g · fat 18g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 2 days and reheat in a pan.","chefNotes":"Serve immediately to keep the pancakes crispy.","pairsWith":"lingonberry jam · fried bacon · sour cream","trivia":"Traditionally eaten on Thursdays in Sweden.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-smorgastarta","name":"Smorgastarta","nameAlt":"Swedish Sandwich Cake","aliases":["Smörgåstårta"],"course":"main","type":"mixed","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"150g bread · 80g mayonnaise · 50g smoked salmon · 50g shrimp · 30g cucumber · 20g dill","ingredients12":"1800g bread · 960g mayonnaise · 600g smoked salmon · 600g shrimp · 360g cucumber · 240g dill","method":"Trim the crusts from the bread slices and lay the first layer on a flat surface. Spread a mixture of mayonnaise and fillings such as shrimp or salmon evenly across the layer. Add another layer of bread and repeat the filling process to build height. Continue layering until all ingredients are used, finishing with a top layer of bread. Spread mayonnaise smoothly over the entire cake to cover all sides. Decorate the top with slices of cucumber, shrimp, salmon, and fresh dill for presentation. Chill the cake in the refrigerator for several hours to allow flavors to meld. Slice carefully and serve cold.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 40g · fat 30g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and consume within 2 days.","chefNotes":"Chill well before slicing for clean portions.","pairsWith":"green salad · pickled vegetables · boiled eggs","trivia":"Often served at birthdays and festive gatherings in Sweden.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-kroppkakor","name":"Kroppkakor","nameAlt":"Potato Dumplings with Pork Filling","aliases":["Kroppkaka","Swedish Potato Dumplings"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"traditional meal","ingredients":"250g potatoes · 80g flour · 1 egg · 100g pork · 30g onion · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"3000g potatoes · 960g flour · 12 eggs · 1200g pork · 360g onion · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Boil the potatoes until tender, then mash them smoothly and allow them to cool slightly. Mix the mashed potatoes with flour, egg, salt, and pepper to form a soft dough. Finely chop the pork and onion, then sauté them together until cooked through and slightly browned. Take portions of the dough and flatten them in your hand, placing a spoonful of filling in the center. Wrap the dough around the filling and shape into round dumplings. Bring a pot of salted water to a gentle simmer and carefully add the dumplings. Cook until they float to the surface and are firm, indicating they are done. Remove them with a slotted spoon and serve warm.","cookTime":"50 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 55g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days or freeze for later use.","chefNotes":"Do not overcrowd the pot to prevent dumplings from breaking.","pairsWith":"lingonberry sauce · melted butter · pickled beetroot","trivia":"Popular in southern Sweden, especially on the island of Öland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-kalops","name":"Kalops","nameAlt":"Swedish Beef Stew","aliases":["Swedish Kalops"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"winter meal","ingredients":"200g beef · 50g carrot · 50g onion · 5g allspice · 5g salt · 2g pepper · 300ml water","ingredients12":"2400g beef · 600g carrot · 600g onion · 60g allspice · 60g salt · 24g pepper · 3600ml water","method":"Cut the beef into evenly sized chunks and season them lightly with salt and pepper. Heat a pot over medium heat and brown the meat on all sides to develop flavor. Add chopped onions and carrots and cook until slightly softened. Sprinkle in the allspice and stir to release its aroma. Pour in water to cover the ingredients and bring to a gentle simmer. Cover the pot and cook slowly until the meat becomes tender and the flavors meld together. Stir occasionally and adjust seasoning as needed. Serve hot once the stew has thickened slightly.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 20g · fat 28g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days or freeze for up to 2 months.","chefNotes":"Slow cooking enhances the depth of flavor.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · pickled beetroot · cabbage salad","trivia":"Kalops is a classic comfort dish during Swedish winters.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-prinsesstarta","name":"Prinsesstarta","nameAlt":"Princess Cream Cake","aliases":["Prinsesstårta","Princess Cake"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"100g sponge cake · 100ml cream · 50g custard · 50g marzipan · 20g sugar","ingredients12":"1200g sponge cake · 1200ml cream · 600g custard · 600g marzipan · 240g sugar","method":"Slice the sponge cake into even layers and set them aside on a clean surface. Whip the cream with sugar until soft peaks form and it holds its shape. Spread a layer of custard over the first sponge layer, then add a layer of whipped cream. Place another sponge layer on top and repeat the process to build height. Shape the top layer with extra cream into a gentle dome. Carefully roll out the marzipan and drape it over the cake, smoothing it evenly over the dome. Trim the edges neatly and dust lightly with sugar for a clean finish. Chill the cake before slicing to maintain its structure.","cookTime":"90 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 50g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate and consume within 2 days.","chefNotes":"Keep the marzipan cool to prevent sticking while rolling.","pairsWith":"fresh berries · vanilla sauce · fruit compote","trivia":"Named after Swedish princesses who loved the cake.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-kanelbullar","name":"Kanelbullar","nameAlt":"Cinnamon Buns","aliases":["Kanelbulle","Swedish Cinnamon Rolls"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"fika","ingredients":"200g flour · 100ml milk · 50g butter · 30g sugar · 5g yeast · 5g cinnamon","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1200ml milk · 600g butter · 360g sugar · 60g yeast · 60g cinnamon","method":"Warm the milk gently and dissolve the yeast into it until activated and slightly frothy. Mix in flour, sugar, and softened butter to form a soft dough. Knead the dough until smooth and elastic, then cover and let it rise until doubled in size. Roll out the dough into a rectangle and spread butter over the surface. Sprinkle cinnamon and sugar evenly across the dough. Roll it tightly into a log and slice into individual buns. Place the buns on a tray and allow them to rise again until puffy. Bake in a preheated oven until golden brown and fragrant. Allow them to cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 55g · fat 18g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overbake to keep the buns soft.","pairsWith":"cardamom buns · vanilla custard · fruit jam","trivia":"Sweden celebrates Cinnamon Bun Day on October 4.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-semla","name":"Semla","nameAlt":"Cream-Filled Cardamom Bun","aliases":["Semlor","Fastlagsbulle"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"Lent","ingredients":"150g flour · 80ml milk · 30g butter · 20g sugar · 5g cardamom · 100ml cream · 30g almond paste","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 960ml milk · 360g butter · 240g sugar · 60g cardamom · 1200ml cream · 360g almond paste","method":"Prepare a soft dough by mixing warm milk, yeast, flour, butter, sugar, and cardamom until smooth. Knead the dough thoroughly and allow it to rise until doubled in size. Shape the dough into small buns and let them rise again until light and airy. Bake the buns until golden and cooked through, then allow them to cool completely. Cut off the tops and scoop out a small portion of the inside crumb. Mix the crumb with almond paste and a little milk to create a filling. Fill each bun with the almond mixture and top generously with whipped cream. Place the tops back on and dust lightly with sugar before serving.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 9g · carbs 60g · fat 22g","storage":"Best eaten fresh, but can be refrigerated for up to 1 day.","chefNotes":"Use freshly ground cardamom for a stronger aroma.","pairsWith":"berry compote · vanilla sauce · almond biscuits","trivia":"Traditionally eaten before Lent in Sweden.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-falukorv","name":"Falukorv","nameAlt":"Fried Swedish Sausage","aliases":["Falukorv med stekt potatis"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"everyday meal","ingredients":"200g falukorv sausage · 150g potatoes · 20ml oil · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"2400g falukorv sausage · 1800g potatoes · 240ml oil · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Slice the sausage into thick rounds and set aside for cooking. Peel and dice the potatoes into small cubes for even frying. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat and cook the potatoes until they are golden and crisp on the outside while tender inside. Season the potatoes with salt and pepper while they cook. In another pan, fry the sausage slices until they are browned and slightly crispy on the edges. Turn them occasionally to ensure even cooking. Combine the sausage and potatoes briefly in the pan to heat through together. Serve hot once everything is fully cooked and well seasoned.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 35g · fat 35g","storage":"Refrigerate leftovers for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Cook potatoes slowly for a crisp texture.","pairsWith":"mustard sauce · pickled cabbage · fried eggs","trivia":"Falukorv originated from Falun's copper mining region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-toast-skagen","name":"Toast Skagen","nameAlt":"Shrimp Salad on Toast","aliases":["Skagenröra","Toast à la Skagen"],"course":"starter","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"starter","ingredients":"120g shrimp · 50g mayonnaise · 20g dill · 10g lemon juice · 50g bread","ingredients12":"1440g shrimp · 600g mayonnaise · 240g dill · 120g lemon juice · 600g bread","method":"Peel and roughly chop the shrimp into bite-sized pieces. In a bowl, combine the shrimp with mayonnaise, chopped dill, and lemon juice. Mix gently until the ingredients are evenly coated without breaking the shrimp too much. Toast the bread slices until golden and crisp. Spoon the shrimp mixture generously over the toast. Spread it evenly to cover the surface. Garnish with additional dill if desired. Serve immediately while the toast remains crisp and fresh.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 20g · fat 20g","storage":"Store shrimp mixture separately in refrigerator for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use fresh shrimp for best flavor.","pairsWith":"lemon wedges · cucumber salad · boiled eggs","trivia":"Named after the coastal region of Skagen.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-blabarssoppa","name":"Blabarssoppa","nameAlt":"Blueberry Soup","aliases":["Blåbärssoppa"],"course":"drink","type":"sweet","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"150g blueberries · 300ml water · 30g sugar · 5g starch","ingredients12":"1800g blueberries · 3600ml water · 360g sugar · 60g starch","method":"Combine the blueberries and water in a pot and bring to a gentle boil over medium heat. Allow the berries to soften and release their juices as they cook. Stir occasionally to prevent sticking at the bottom. Add sugar and mix until dissolved completely. In a small bowl, mix starch with a little cold water to create a slurry. Pour the slurry into the soup while stirring continuously to thicken it. Continue cooking until the soup reaches a smooth and slightly thick consistency. Remove from heat and allow it to cool slightly before serving warm or chilled.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":180,"nutrition":"protein 2g · carbs 40g · fat 1g","storage":"Store refrigerated for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Adjust sugar based on berry sweetness.","pairsWith":"pancakes · vanilla yogurt · oat biscuits","trivia":"Often served during cross-country skiing events.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-inlagd-sill","name":"Inlagd Sill","nameAlt":"Pickled Herring","aliases":["Pickled Herring Swedish Style"],"course":"side","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"Midsummer","ingredients":"150g herring · 100ml vinegar · 80ml water · 30g sugar · 10g onion · 5g spices","ingredients12":"1800g herring · 1200ml vinegar · 960ml water · 360g sugar · 120g onion · 60g spices","method":"Rinse the herring thoroughly and cut it into bite-sized pieces. In a saucepan, combine vinegar, water, and sugar and bring to a gentle boil until the sugar dissolves. Slice the onion thinly and prepare the spices for flavoring. Place the herring pieces into a clean jar and layer them with onions and spices. Pour the hot pickling liquid over the herring until fully submerged. Allow the mixture to cool before sealing the jar. Refrigerate for at least 24 hours to allow the flavors to develop. Serve chilled once properly pickled.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 20g · fat 10g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Allow enough time for proper pickling flavor.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · sour cream · chives","trivia":"A staple dish during Swedish festive seasons.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-pytt-i-panna","name":"Pytt i Panna","nameAlt":"Swedish Hash with Meat and Potatoes","aliases":["Pyttipanna","Pytt i panna"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"everyday meal","ingredients":"150g potatoes · 100g beef · 50g onion · 10ml oil · 5g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g potatoes · 1200g beef · 600g onion · 120ml oil · 60g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Peel and dice the potatoes into small cubes and boil them briefly until just tender, then drain and cool. Cut the beef into small bite-sized pieces and finely chop the onion. Heat oil in a large frying pan over medium heat and cook the potatoes until golden and crisp on the edges. Add the beef and cook until browned and cooked through, stirring frequently. Add the chopped onion and continue cooking until softened and slightly caramelized. Season with salt and black pepper, mixing everything evenly. Cook until all components are well combined and heated through. Serve hot directly from the pan.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 40g · fat 25g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days and reheat in a pan.","chefNotes":"Use leftover meats for authentic flavor.","pairsWith":"fried eggs · pickled beetroot · mustard sauce","trivia":"Originally a way to use up leftovers in Swedish homes.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-lussekatter","name":"Lussekatter","nameAlt":"Saffron Sweet Buns","aliases":["Lucia buns","Lussekatt"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"St Lucia Day","ingredients":"200g flour · 100ml milk · 50g butter · 30g sugar · 5g yeast · 1g saffron","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1200ml milk · 600g butter · 360g sugar · 60g yeast · 12g saffron","method":"Warm the milk gently and dissolve the saffron into it to release its color and aroma. Add yeast to the milk and allow it to activate until slightly foamy. Mix in flour, sugar, and softened butter to form a soft dough. Knead the dough until smooth and elastic, then let it rise until doubled in size. Shape the dough into traditional S-shaped buns and place them on a baking tray. Allow the buns to rise again until light and puffy. Bake in a preheated oven until golden and cooked through. Let them cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 55g · fat 15g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use high-quality saffron for best color and flavor.","pairsWith":"ginger cookies · fruit compote · vanilla custard","trivia":"Traditionally eaten during the Lucia celebrations in December.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-knackebrod","name":"Knackebrod","nameAlt":"Swedish Crispbread","aliases":["Knäckebröd","Crispbread"],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g rye flour · 100ml water · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g rye flour · 1200ml water · 60g salt","method":"Combine the rye flour, water, and salt in a bowl and mix until a firm dough forms. Knead the dough briefly until smooth and cohesive. Roll the dough out very thinly on a floured surface to achieve a crisp texture. Cut into flat rounds or rectangles and prick the surface with a fork to prevent bubbling. Place the pieces on a baking tray lined with parchment paper. Bake in a preheated oven until completely dry and crisp without browning too much. Allow the crispbread to cool fully so it hardens properly. Store once completely cooled.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 50g · fat 2g","storage":"Store in a dry airtight container for up to 2 weeks.","chefNotes":"Roll as thin as possible for maximum crispness.","pairsWith":"cheese · smoked salmon · pickled vegetables","trivia":"A staple Swedish bread with a long shelf life.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-artsoppa","name":"Ärtsoppa","nameAlt":"Swedish Yellow Pea Soup","aliases":["Artsoppa","Pea Soup Sweden"],"course":"main","type":"legume","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"Thursday meal","ingredients":"150g yellow peas · 100g pork · 50g onion · 500ml water · 5g salt · 2g thyme","ingredients12":"1800g yellow peas · 1200g pork · 600g onion · 6000ml water · 60g salt · 24g thyme","method":"Rinse the yellow peas thoroughly and soak them if necessary to reduce cooking time. Place the peas in a pot with water and bring to a gentle boil. Add chopped pork and onion to the pot and stir well. Reduce the heat and allow the soup to simmer slowly until the peas become soft and begin to break down. Stir occasionally to prevent sticking and ensure even cooking. Add salt and thyme for seasoning and continue simmering until the soup thickens to a hearty consistency. Taste and adjust seasoning if needed. Serve hot once fully cooked.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 40g · fat 15g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days or freeze for longer storage.","chefNotes":"Slow simmering improves texture and flavor.","pairsWith":"mustard · crispbread · pickled vegetables","trivia":"Traditionally served with pancakes on Thursdays.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-vasterbottensostpaj","name":"Vasterbottensostpaj","nameAlt":"Vasterbotten Cheese Pie","aliases":["Västerbottensostpaj","Swedish Cheese Pie"],"course":"side","type":"savory pie","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"festive","ingredients":"100g flour · 50g butter · 1 egg · 100g cheese · 100ml cream · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 600g butter · 12 eggs · 1200g cheese · 1200ml cream · 60g salt","method":"Prepare a pastry dough by mixing flour and butter until crumbly, then add egg to bind it together. Press the dough into a pie dish evenly, covering the base and sides. Chill the pastry briefly to prevent shrinking during baking. In a bowl, whisk together cream, egg, grated cheese, and salt until smooth. Pour the filling into the prepared crust evenly. Bake in a preheated oven until the filling is set and the top turns golden. Allow the pie to cool slightly so it firms up before slicing. Serve warm or at room temperature.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 15g · carbs 25g · fat 35g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use authentic Västerbotten cheese for best flavor.","pairsWith":"green salad · smoked salmon · pickled onions","trivia":"A popular dish at Swedish midsummer celebrations.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-ostkaka","name":"Ostkaka","nameAlt":"Swedish Baked Cheesecake","aliases":["Swedish Cheesecake","Ost kaka"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"200g curd cheese · 100ml cream · 50g sugar · 1 egg · 20g almonds","ingredients12":"2400g curd cheese · 1200ml cream · 600g sugar · 12 eggs · 240g almonds","method":"Preheat the oven and prepare a baking dish by greasing it lightly. In a bowl, mix the curd cheese with cream, sugar, and egg until smooth. Stir in chopped almonds to add texture and flavor. Pour the mixture into the prepared dish evenly. Bake in the oven until the surface is golden and the center is set but still slightly soft. Allow the cheesecake to cool before serving so it firms up properly. Slice into portions and serve slightly warm or chilled. Garnish as desired.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 30g · fat 28g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overbake to keep the texture creamy.","pairsWith":"berry jam · whipped cream · fresh fruit","trivia":"Differs from American cheesecake with a lighter texture.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"sweden-glogg","name":"Glögg","nameAlt":"Swedish Mulled Wine","aliases":["Glogg","Mulled Wine Sweden"],"course":"drink","type":"beverage","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Sweden","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"200ml red wine · 20g sugar · 5g cinnamon · 2g cloves · 10g raisins","ingredients12":"2400ml red wine · 240g sugar · 60g cinnamon · 24g cloves · 120g raisins","method":"Pour the red wine into a pot and heat it gently over low heat without boiling. Add sugar, cinnamon, and cloves, stirring until the sugar dissolves completely. Allow the mixture to warm slowly so the spices infuse into the wine. Add raisins toward the end of the heating process. Continue heating until the drink is aromatic and fully infused. Remove from heat and strain if desired to remove spices. Serve warm in heatproof glasses. Enjoy immediately while hot.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 1g · carbs 25g · fat 0g","storage":"Store refrigerated for up to 2 days and reheat gently.","chefNotes":"Do not boil to preserve alcohol content and flavor.","pairsWith":"ginger cookies · saffron buns · almond biscuits","trivia":"A traditional holiday drink served during Swedish winters.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-farikal","name":"Fårikål","nameAlt":"Norwegian Lamb and Cabbage Stew","aliases":["Farikal","Lamb Cabbage Stew"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"autumn","ingredients":"250g lamb · 200g cabbage · 300ml water · 5g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"3000g lamb · 2400g cabbage · 3600ml water · 60g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Cut the lamb into large pieces and season lightly with salt. Chop the cabbage into wedges of similar size. Layer the lamb and cabbage alternately in a heavy pot. Sprinkle whole black pepper and salt between the layers. Pour water into the pot to cover the base. Bring to a gentle boil and then reduce to a slow simmer. Cover and cook until the lamb is tender and easily pulls apart. Stir occasionally but gently to keep layers intact. Serve hot once fully cooked.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 10g · fat 35g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Slow cooking develops deep flavor.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · flatbread · lingonberry sauce","trivia":"Considered Norway's national dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-rakfisk","name":"Rakfisk","nameAlt":"Fermented Fish","aliases":["Norwegian Rakfisk"],"course":"starter","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"150g trout · 20g salt · 5g sugar","ingredients12":"1800g trout · 240g salt · 60g sugar","method":"Clean the trout thoroughly and remove all internal parts carefully. Rub the fish with salt and sugar evenly on all sides. Place the fish in a container and press it down firmly. Store in a cool place for several weeks to allow fermentation. Turn the fish occasionally to ensure even curing. Once fermented, remove the fish and slice into thin pieces. Serve raw in thin slices. Enjoy immediately after preparation.","cookTime":"20160 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 2g · fat 18g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and consume within a few days after opening.","chefNotes":"Ensure proper fermentation conditions for safety.","pairsWith":"flatbread · sour cream · onions","trivia":"A traditional fermented fish dish dating back centuries.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-krumkake","name":"Krumkake","nameAlt":"Norwegian Waffle Cookies","aliases":["Krumkaker"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"100g flour · 80g sugar · 50g butter · 1 egg · 5g cardamom","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 960g sugar · 600g butter · 12 eggs · 60g cardamom","method":"Mix the egg and sugar together until light and slightly fluffy. Add melted butter and mix until combined. Stir in flour and cardamom to create a smooth batter. Heat a krumkake iron and lightly grease it. Spoon a small amount of batter onto the iron and cook until golden. Quickly roll the cookie into a cone shape while still warm. Allow it to cool and harden. Repeat with remaining batter. Serve once cooled.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 45g · fat 15g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Roll immediately while warm to shape properly.","pairsWith":"whipped cream · berry compote · chocolate sauce","trivia":"A traditional holiday cookie in Norway.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-brunost-sandwich","name":"Brunost Sandwich","nameAlt":"Brown Cheese Open Sandwich","aliases":["Brown Cheese Bread","Brunost"],"course":"starter","type":"dairy","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"breakfast","ingredients":"100g bread · 50g brown cheese · 10g butter","ingredients12":"1200g bread · 600g brown cheese · 120g butter","method":"Slice the bread evenly and lay it flat on a clean surface. Spread a thin layer of butter over each slice for flavor. Cut the brown cheese into thin slices using a cheese slicer. Place the cheese slices evenly over the bread. Arrange neatly to cover the surface completely. Serve immediately while fresh. Enjoy as a simple breakfast or snack.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 30g · fat 15g","storage":"Best consumed fresh.","chefNotes":"Use a cheese slicer for thin slices.","pairsWith":"fruit slices · yogurt · jam","trivia":"Brown cheese is uniquely Norwegian.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-kj-ttkaker","name":"Kjøttkaker","nameAlt":"Norwegian Meat Cakes","aliases":["Kjottkaker","Norwegian Meat Patties"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"family dinner","ingredients":"150g ground beef · 50g onion · 30ml milk · 20g breadcrumbs · 1 egg · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"1800g ground beef · 600g onion · 360ml milk · 240g breadcrumbs · 12 eggs · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Finely chop the onion and mix it with ground beef, breadcrumbs, milk, egg, salt, and pepper. Combine thoroughly until smooth and slightly sticky. Shape the mixture into oval patties. Heat a pan over medium heat and cook the patties until browned on both sides. Reduce heat and continue cooking until fully done inside. Turn occasionally to ensure even cooking. Allow them to rest briefly before serving. Serve hot once ready.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 10g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Keep mixture moist for tender patties.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · gravy · peas","trivia":"A traditional Norwegian comfort dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-lefse","name":"Lefse","nameAlt":"Soft Norwegian Flatbread","aliases":["Potato Lefse","Norwegian Lefse"],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"holiday","ingredients":"200g potatoes · 80g flour · 20g butter · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g potatoes · 960g flour · 240g butter · 60g salt","method":"Boil the potatoes until tender, then mash them until smooth. Mix in butter, flour, and salt to form a soft dough. Divide the dough into small portions. Roll each portion into thin rounds on a floured surface. Cook each round on a hot griddle until lightly browned on both sides. Turn carefully to avoid tearing. Allow to cool slightly before serving. Serve warm or at room temperature.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 50g · fat 10g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Roll thin for best texture.","pairsWith":"butter · sugar · cinnamon","trivia":"A traditional Norwegian festive bread.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-r-mmegr-t","name":"Rømmegrøt","nameAlt":"Sour Cream Porridge","aliases":["Rommegrot","Norwegian Cream Porridge"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200ml sour cream · 50g flour · 200ml milk · 20g sugar · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400ml sour cream · 600g flour · 2400ml milk · 240g sugar · 60g salt","method":"Heat the sour cream in a pot until it begins to simmer gently. Add flour gradually while stirring continuously to prevent lumps. Cook the mixture until it thickens and releases butter. Remove excess butter if necessary. Slowly add milk while stirring to achieve a smooth consistency. Add sugar and salt to taste. Continue cooking until creamy and well combined. Serve warm once ready.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 35g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Stir constantly to avoid lumps.","pairsWith":"cinnamon sugar · cured meats · flatbread","trivia":"Often served at Norwegian festivals.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-pinnekj-tt","name":"Pinnekjøtt","nameAlt":"Salted Dried Lamb Ribs","aliases":["Pinnekjott","Norwegian Lamb Ribs"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"250g lamb ribs · 300ml water · 5g salt","ingredients12":"3000g lamb ribs · 3600ml water · 60g salt","method":"Soak the salted lamb ribs in cold water overnight to remove excess salt. Drain the ribs and place them on a rack or birch sticks inside a pot to keep them elevated above the water. Pour water into the bottom of the pot without submerging the meat. Cover the pot tightly and bring the water to a gentle simmer. Steam the ribs slowly until the meat becomes tender and begins to pull away from the bone. Check occasionally to ensure there is enough water for steaming. Once cooked, optionally brown the ribs briefly in the oven for added texture. Serve hot once fully prepared.","cookTime":"180 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 0g · fat 50g","storage":"Refrigerate leftovers for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not boil the meat; steaming preserves flavor and texture.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · mashed rutabaga · mustard sauce","trivia":"A traditional Norwegian Christmas dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-klippfisk","name":"Klippfisk","nameAlt":"Dried and Salted Cod","aliases":["Clipfish","Norwegian Salt Cod"],"course":"main","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"200g cod · 300ml water · 20g salt · 10ml oil","ingredients12":"2400g cod · 3600ml water · 240g salt · 120ml oil","method":"Soak the dried salted cod in cold water for at least 24 hours, changing the water several times to remove excess salt. Drain the fish and cut it into manageable portions. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat and lightly cook the fish pieces until they begin to firm up. Transfer the fish to a pot and add fresh water to cover it partially. Simmer gently until the fish becomes tender and flakes easily with a fork. Avoid vigorous boiling to maintain texture. Once cooked, remove from heat and allow it to rest briefly. Serve warm once ready.","cookTime":"90 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 0g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Proper soaking is essential to balance saltiness.","pairsWith":"potatoes · tomato sauce · olives","trivia":"Klippfisk was a major Norwegian export.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-fiskesuppe","name":"Fiskesuppe","nameAlt":"Norwegian Creamy Fish Soup","aliases":["Fiske suppe"],"course":"main","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"everyday meal","ingredients":"150g white fish · 50g carrot · 50g leek · 200ml fish stock · 100ml cream · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"1800g white fish · 600g carrot · 600g leek · 2400ml fish stock · 1200ml cream · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Cut the fish into bite-sized pieces and set aside. Slice the carrot and leek into thin pieces. Bring the fish stock to a gentle simmer in a pot. Add the vegetables and cook until they soften. Stir in the cream and reduce the heat. Add the fish and cook until it becomes opaque and flakes easily. Season with salt and pepper. Stir gently to avoid breaking the fish. Serve hot once ready.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 15g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overcook fish.","pairsWith":"flatbread · boiled potatoes · herb salad","trivia":"A coastal Norwegian staple.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-sodd","name":"Sodd","nameAlt":"Norwegian Meatball Soup","aliases":["Trøndersodd","Norwegian Sodd"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"150g meatballs · 50g carrot · 50g potato · 300ml broth · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"1800g meatballs · 600g carrot · 600g potato · 3600ml broth · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Prepare or use pre-made meatballs and set them aside. Peel and dice the carrots and potatoes into small uniform pieces. Bring the broth to a gentle boil in a pot. Add the vegetables and cook until they are tender but still hold their shape. Add the meatballs and allow them to heat through completely. Season with salt and pepper as needed. Let the soup simmer briefly to blend the flavors. Stir occasionally without breaking the meatballs. Serve hot once everything is cooked through.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 25g · fat 20g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use homemade broth for richer flavor.","pairsWith":"flatbread · boiled potatoes · pickled vegetables","trivia":"Sodd is often served at weddings and special occasions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-svele","name":"Svele","nameAlt":"Norwegian Sweet Pancakes","aliases":["Svele pancake","Norwegian griddle cakes"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"150g flour · 100ml milk · 30g sugar · 1 egg · 5g baking soda · 10g butter","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 1200ml milk · 360g sugar · 12 eggs · 60g baking soda · 120g butter","method":"Whisk together the egg and sugar until light and slightly frothy. Add milk and mix until well combined. Gradually incorporate the flour and baking soda to form a smooth batter. Allow the batter to rest briefly to develop texture. Heat a pan or griddle and melt a small amount of butter. Pour portions of batter onto the hot surface and cook until bubbles form on the surface. Flip the pancakes and cook until golden and cooked through. Repeat with remaining batter. Serve warm once ready.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 50g · fat 12g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overmix the batter to keep pancakes soft.","pairsWith":"butter · brown cheese · berry jam","trivia":"Traditionally served on ferries along Norway's west coast.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-riskrem","name":"Riskrem","nameAlt":"Rice Cream Dessert with Berry Sauce","aliases":["Norwegian Rice Cream","Riskrem dessert"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"150g rice pudding · 100ml cream · 30g sugar · 50g berry sauce","ingredients12":"1800g rice pudding · 1200ml cream · 360g sugar · 600g berry sauce","method":"Prepare rice pudding in advance and allow it to cool completely. Whip the cream with sugar until it forms soft peaks. Gently fold the whipped cream into the rice pudding until light and airy. Mix carefully to maintain the fluffy texture. Spoon the mixture into serving dishes evenly. Top with berry sauce just before serving. Chill briefly to enhance the texture and flavor. Serve cold once ready.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 50g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Fold gently to keep the dessert light.","pairsWith":"berry compote · almond cookies · vanilla sauce","trivia":"A hidden almond tradition brings luck to the finder.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-flatbr-d","name":"Flatbrød","nameAlt":"Traditional Norwegian Flatbread","aliases":["Flatbrod","Norwegian Flatbread"],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g whole grain flour · 120ml water · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g whole grain flour · 1440ml water · 60g salt","method":"Mix the flour, water, and salt together to form a firm dough. Knead the dough briefly until it becomes smooth and cohesive. Divide the dough into small portions for easier rolling. Roll each portion into very thin flat rounds on a floured surface. Heat a dry pan or griddle over medium heat. Cook each flatbread until it becomes dry and slightly crisp with light browning. Flip to cook both sides evenly. Allow the flatbread to cool completely so it becomes crisp. Store once fully cooled.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 50g · fat 2g","storage":"Store in a dry airtight container for up to 2 weeks.","chefNotes":"Thin rolling is key for authentic texture.","pairsWith":"cured meats · cheese · soups","trivia":"Flatbrød has been a staple in Norway for centuries.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-lutefisk","name":"Lutefisk","nameAlt":"Lye-Treated Dried Cod","aliases":["Lutefisk Norway","Lye Fish"],"course":"main","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"200g dried cod · 500ml water · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g dried cod · 6000ml water · 60g salt","method":"Soak the dried cod in cold water for several days, changing the water regularly to rehydrate it fully. After soaking, treat the fish with a lye solution following safe preparation methods, then rinse thoroughly to remove any residue. Place the fish in a baking dish and season lightly with salt. Bake in a preheated oven until the fish becomes gelatinous and flakes easily. Monitor the texture closely to avoid overcooking. Allow the fish to rest briefly after cooking. Serve hot once ready.","cookTime":"1440 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 0g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Ensure proper rinsing after lye treatment for safety.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · peas · bacon","trivia":"Lutefisk is a traditional Nordic dish dating back centuries.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-medisterkaker","name":"Medisterkaker","nameAlt":"Norwegian Pork Meat Patties","aliases":["Medisterkake","Christmas Pork Patties"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"150g ground pork · 30ml milk · 20g breadcrumbs · 1 egg · 5g salt · 2g pepper · 5g nutmeg","ingredients12":"1800g ground pork · 360ml milk · 240g breadcrumbs · 12 eggs · 60g salt · 24g pepper · 60g nutmeg","method":"Combine the ground pork with breadcrumbs, milk, egg, salt, pepper, and nutmeg in a bowl. Mix thoroughly until the mixture becomes smooth and slightly sticky. Shape the mixture into small round patties using damp hands. Heat a pan over medium heat and add a small amount of fat. Fry the patties until browned on both sides, turning carefully to maintain shape. Reduce the heat and continue cooking until fully cooked through. Allow the patties to rest briefly before serving. Serve warm once ready.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 24g · carbs 8g · fat 32g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overcook to keep the patties juicy.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · red cabbage · gravy","trivia":"A staple on Norwegian Christmas tables.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-tilsl-rte-bondepiker","name":"Tilslørte Bondepiker","nameAlt":"Layered Apple and Cream Dessert","aliases":["Hidden Farmer's Daughters","Apple Crumble Cream Dessert"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"150g apples · 50g breadcrumbs · 30g sugar · 50ml cream · 10g butter","ingredients12":"1800g apples · 600g breadcrumbs · 360g sugar · 600ml cream · 120g butter","method":"Peel and slice the apples, then cook them gently in a pan with a small amount of sugar until soft and slightly caramelized. In another pan, melt butter and toast the breadcrumbs until golden and crisp. Whip the cream until soft peaks form and it holds its shape. In serving glasses, layer the apple mixture, toasted breadcrumbs, and whipped cream. Repeat the layers until the glass is filled. Finish with a layer of cream on top. Chill briefly to allow the layers to settle. Serve cold once ready.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 50g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use tart apples for balanced flavor.","pairsWith":"vanilla custard · berry compote · almond biscuits","trivia":"The name humorously translates to 'veiled farm girls'.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-spekemat","name":"Spekemat","nameAlt":"Norwegian Cured Meats Platter","aliases":["Spekemat platter","Cured Meat Board"],"course":"starter","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"100g cured meats · 100g flatbread · 50g sour cream · 30g cheese","ingredients12":"1200g cured meats · 1200g flatbread · 600g sour cream · 360g cheese","method":"Slice the cured meats thinly and arrange them neatly on a serving platter. Break the flatbread into manageable pieces for serving. Place the sour cream into a small serving bowl and smooth the surface. Slice the cheese into thin pieces or cubes for easy serving. Arrange all components attractively on the platter. Ensure even distribution so each serving includes all elements. Serve immediately at room temperature. Allow guests to assemble their own combinations.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 25g · fat 28g","storage":"Store components separately in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use a variety of cured meats for best experience.","pairsWith":"potato salad · pickled vegetables · mustard sauce","trivia":"Popular during Norwegian summer gatherings.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-raspeballer","name":"Raspeballer","nameAlt":"Norwegian Potato Dumplings","aliases":["Komle","Klubb"],"course":"main","type":"starch","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"250g potatoes · 80g flour · 100g pork · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"3000g potatoes · 960g flour · 1200g pork · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Peel and grate the potatoes, then squeeze out excess liquid to improve texture. Mix the grated potatoes with flour, salt, and pepper to form a thick dough. Cut the pork into small cubes for filling. Shape portions of the dough into balls, placing pork pieces inside each one. Bring a large pot of salted water to a gentle boil. Carefully add the dumplings and cook until they float and become firm. Allow them to simmer until fully cooked through. Remove with a slotted spoon and serve hot.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 60g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Ensure dumplings are tightly sealed to prevent breaking.","pairsWith":"melted butter · bacon · mashed rutabaga","trivia":"Known by different names across Norway.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-makrell-i-tomat","name":"Makrell i Tomat","nameAlt":"Mackerel in Tomato Sauce","aliases":["Norwegian Mackerel Spread","Makrell"],"course":"starter","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"breakfast","ingredients":"120g mackerel · 80g tomato sauce · 50g bread · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1440g mackerel · 960g tomato sauce · 600g bread · 60g salt","method":"Cook the mackerel gently until it flakes easily, then remove any bones carefully. Mix the fish with tomato sauce until evenly combined. Season lightly with salt to enhance the flavor. Toast the bread slices until crisp if desired. Spoon the mackerel mixture generously over the bread. Spread evenly to cover the surface. Serve immediately while fresh. Enjoy as an open sandwich.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 20g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate mixture for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use fresh mackerel for best taste.","pairsWith":"boiled eggs · cucumber salad · crispbread","trivia":"A common Norwegian breakfast item.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"norway-eplekake","name":"Eplekake","nameAlt":"Norwegian Apple Cake","aliases":["Eple kake","Norwegian Apple Cake"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Norway","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"150g apples · 100g flour · 80g sugar · 50g butter · 1 egg · 5g cinnamon","ingredients12":"1800g apples · 1200g flour · 960g sugar · 600g butter · 12 eggs · 60g cinnamon","method":"Peel and slice the apples evenly and set them aside. In a bowl, mix butter and sugar until light and creamy. Add the egg and beat until well combined. Gradually add flour and cinnamon to form a smooth batter. Pour the batter into a greased baking dish and arrange the apple slices on top. Bake in a preheated oven until the cake is golden and a skewer inserted comes out clean. Allow the cake to cool slightly before slicing. Serve warm or at room temperature.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 55g · fat 18g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use tart apples for better flavor balance.","pairsWith":"vanilla sauce · whipped cream · berry compote","trivia":"A classic homemade dessert in Norway.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-smorrebrod","name":"Smorrebrod","nameAlt":"Danish Open-Faced Sandwich","aliases":["Smørrebrød","Danish Open Sandwich"],"course":"main","type":"mixed","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"lunch","ingredients":"100g rye bread · 80g smoked fish · 50g egg · 30g mayonnaise · 20g cucumber · 10g dill","ingredients12":"1200g rye bread · 960g smoked fish · 600g egg · 360g mayonnaise · 240g cucumber · 120g dill","method":"Slice the rye bread evenly and lay it flat on a clean surface. Spread a thin layer of mayonnaise across the bread to create a base. Arrange slices of smoked fish neatly over the bread. Slice the boiled egg and place it evenly on top of the fish layer. Add thin slices of cucumber for freshness and crunch. Sprinkle fresh dill over the sandwich for flavor and presentation. Ensure the toppings are balanced and evenly distributed. Serve immediately as an open-faced sandwich.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 30g · fat 20g","storage":"Best consumed fresh, store components separately if needed.","chefNotes":"Use dense rye bread for authentic texture.","pairsWith":"potato salad · pickled herring · boiled potatoes","trivia":"A cornerstone of Danish lunch culture.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-frikadeller","name":"Frikadeller","nameAlt":"Danish Pork Meatballs","aliases":["Frikadelle","Danish Meat Patties"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"family dinner","ingredients":"150g ground pork · 50g onion · 30ml milk · 20g breadcrumbs · 1 egg · 5g salt · 2g pepper · 10ml butter","ingredients12":"1800g ground pork · 600g onion · 360ml milk · 240g breadcrumbs · 12 eggs · 60g salt · 24g pepper · 120ml butter","method":"Finely chop the onion and sauté it gently in butter until soft and translucent. In a bowl, combine the ground pork with breadcrumbs, milk, egg, salt, and pepper. Add the cooked onion and mix thoroughly until smooth. Shape the mixture into oval patties using your hands. Heat butter in a pan over medium heat and fry the patties until golden brown on both sides. Reduce the heat and continue cooking until fully cooked through. Turn occasionally to ensure even cooking. Let the patties rest briefly before serving.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 10g · fat 30g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Keep patties moist by not overcooking.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · red cabbage · gravy","trivia":"A staple Danish comfort food dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-stegt-flaesk","name":"Stegt Flaesk","nameAlt":"Crispy Pork Belly with Parsley Sauce","aliases":["Stegt flæsk","Danish Pork Belly"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"200g pork belly · 150g potatoes · 100ml milk · 10g parsley · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"2400g pork belly · 1800g potatoes · 1200ml milk · 120g parsley · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Slice the pork belly into even strips and season lightly with salt. Place the strips in a pan or oven and cook until they become crispy and golden. Turn occasionally to ensure even crisping on all sides. Boil the potatoes until tender and set aside. In a saucepan, heat milk and add chopped parsley to create a simple sauce. Stir until the sauce is warm and slightly thickened. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Serve the crispy pork with boiled potatoes and parsley sauce.","cookTime":"50 min","kcal":650,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 35g · fat 45g","storage":"Refrigerate leftovers for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Cook pork slowly for best crisp texture.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · parsley sauce · pickled beetroot","trivia":"Considered Denmark's national dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-rugbrod","name":"Rugbrod","nameAlt":"Danish Rye Bread","aliases":["Rugbrød","Danish Dark Rye Bread"],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g rye flour · 100ml water · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g rye flour · 1200ml water · 60g salt","method":"Combine the rye flour, water, and salt in a bowl and mix until a thick dough forms. Knead briefly until the mixture is evenly combined. Transfer the dough into a greased loaf pan and smooth the top. Allow the dough to rest and rise slightly. Bake in a preheated oven until the bread is firm and fully cooked through. Check doneness by tapping the bottom for a hollow sound. Remove from the oven and let it cool completely before slicing. Slice thinly for serving.","cookTime":"90 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 50g · fat 2g","storage":"Store in a sealed container for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Allow full cooling before slicing for best texture.","pairsWith":"cheese · cured meats · smoked fish","trivia":"A staple bread in Danish cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-aebleskiver","name":"Aebleskiver","nameAlt":"Danish Pancake Balls","aliases":["Æbleskiver","Danish Pancake Puffs"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"150g flour · 100ml milk · 1 egg · 30g sugar · 10g butter · 5g baking powder","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 1200ml milk · 12 eggs · 360g sugar · 120g butter · 60g baking powder","method":"Whisk together the egg and sugar until light and slightly frothy. Add milk and melted butter and mix well. Gradually incorporate flour and baking powder to form a smooth batter. Heat a special æbleskiver pan and lightly grease each cavity. Pour batter into each cavity and cook until bubbles form on the surface. Turn the balls carefully using a skewer to cook evenly on all sides. Continue cooking until golden and fully cooked through. Remove from the pan and allow to cool slightly. Serve warm.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 50g · fat 15g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Turn frequently for even round shape.","pairsWith":"powdered sugar · fruit jam · chocolate sauce","trivia":"Traditionally served during Christmas markets.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-risalamande","name":"Risalamande","nameAlt":"Rice Pudding Dessert with Almonds","aliases":["Ris a la mande","Danish Rice Dessert"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"150g rice pudding · 100ml cream · 30g sugar · 30g almonds · 50g cherry sauce","ingredients12":"1800g rice pudding · 1200ml cream · 360g sugar · 360g almonds · 600g cherry sauce","method":"Prepare rice pudding ahead of time and allow it to cool completely. Whip the cream with sugar until soft peaks form. Fold the whipped cream gently into the rice pudding to create a light texture. Stir in chopped almonds evenly throughout the mixture. Transfer the dessert into serving bowls. Chill until ready to serve. Spoon cherry sauce over the top just before serving. Serve cold once fully prepared.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 55g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Fold gently to keep it airy.","pairsWith":"cherry sauce · almond biscuits · vanilla cream","trivia":"A hidden almond tradition awards a prize.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-polser","name":"Polser","nameAlt":"Danish Hot Dogs","aliases":["Pølser","Danish Hotdog"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"street food","ingredients":"150g sausage · 100g bun · 30g pickles · 20g mustard · 20g ketchup · 10g onions","ingredients12":"1800g sausage · 1200g bun · 360g pickles · 240g mustard · 240g ketchup · 120g onions","method":"Heat the sausage in hot water or grill until fully cooked and heated through. Warm the bun slightly to improve texture. Place the sausage inside the bun carefully. Add mustard and ketchup evenly along the sausage. Top with chopped onions and sliced pickles. Arrange toppings neatly for balanced flavor. Serve immediately while hot. Enjoy fresh for best taste.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 40g · fat 30g","storage":"Best consumed fresh.","chefNotes":"Use crispy onions for authentic texture.","pairsWith":"potato salad · coleslaw · fries","trivia":"A popular street food across Denmark.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-stjerneskud","name":"Stjerneskud","nameAlt":"Danish Fish Fillet Open Sandwich","aliases":["Shooting Star Sandwich"],"course":"main","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"lunch","ingredients":"100g white fish fillet · 80g shrimp · 100g rye bread · 30g mayonnaise · 20g lemon · 10g dill","ingredients12":"1200g white fish fillet · 960g shrimp · 1200g rye bread · 360g mayonnaise · 240g lemon · 120g dill","method":"Season the fish fillet lightly and cook it in a pan until golden and cooked through. Toast the rye bread lightly for a firm base. Place the cooked fish fillet on top of the bread. Arrange shrimp evenly over the fish. Add small spoonfuls of mayonnaise across the top. Squeeze lemon juice over the dish. Garnish with dill for freshness. Serve immediately while fresh.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 30g · fat 20g","storage":"Best consumed fresh.","chefNotes":"Use fresh fish for best results.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · cucumber salad · pickled vegetables","trivia":"Named 'shooting star' for its layered look.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-boller-i-karry","name":"Boller i Karry","nameAlt":"Meatballs in Curry Sauce","aliases":["Danish Curry Meatballs"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"family meal","ingredients":"150g ground pork · 30g onion · 30ml milk · 20g breadcrumbs · 1 egg · 5g curry powder · 200ml broth · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g ground pork · 360g onion · 360ml milk · 240g breadcrumbs · 12 eggs · 60g curry powder · 2400ml broth · 60g salt","method":"Mix ground pork with onion, milk, breadcrumbs, egg, and salt until smooth. Shape into small meatballs. Bring broth to a simmer and cook the meatballs until done. In another pan, heat curry powder gently to release flavor. Add broth gradually to create a sauce. Combine meatballs with sauce and simmer gently. Stir to coat evenly. Cook until slightly thickened. Serve hot.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 20g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use mild curry for authentic flavor.","pairsWith":"rice · vegetables · pickled cucumber","trivia":"A Danish adaptation of curry flavors.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-leverpostej","name":"Leverpostej","nameAlt":"Danish Liver Pâté","aliases":["Danish Liver Spread"],"course":"starter","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"lunch","ingredients":"150g pork liver · 50g onion · 30ml milk · 20g flour · 1 egg · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"1800g pork liver · 600g onion · 360ml milk · 240g flour · 12 eggs · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Blend the pork liver with onion, milk, flour, egg, salt, and pepper until smooth. Pour into a greased dish evenly. Place in a water bath for gentle cooking. Bake until set and firm. Check doneness with a skewer. Allow to cool slightly before slicing. Slice into portions and serve warm or cold. Store properly after cooling.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 15g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Water bath prevents drying.","pairsWith":"rye bread · pickles · crispy onions","trivia":"A classic Danish sandwich topping.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-kartoffelsalat","name":"Kartoffelsalat","nameAlt":"Danish Potato Salad","aliases":["Kartoffel salat","Danish Potato Salad"],"course":"side","type":"vegetable","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"200g potatoes · 50g yogurt · 20g mustard · 20g onion · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"2400g potatoes · 600g yogurt · 240g mustard · 240g onion · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Boil the potatoes until tender, then allow them to cool before slicing into even pieces. In a bowl, mix yogurt with mustard, salt, and pepper to create a smooth dressing. Finely chop the onion and add it to the dressing for flavor. Combine the sliced potatoes with the dressing gently to avoid breaking them apart. Mix until all the potatoes are evenly coated. Taste and adjust seasoning if needed. Chill the salad in the refrigerator before serving. Serve cold once ready.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 40g · fat 12g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use waxy potatoes for best texture.","pairsWith":"grilled sausages · roast chicken · pickled vegetables","trivia":"Popular at Danish summer gatherings.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-wienerbrod","name":"Wienerbrod","nameAlt":"Danish Pastry","aliases":["Wienerbrød","Danish Pastry"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"breakfast","ingredients":"200g flour · 100g butter · 50ml milk · 30g sugar · 5g yeast · 1 egg","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1200g butter · 600ml milk · 360g sugar · 60g yeast · 12 eggs","method":"Prepare a dough by mixing flour, milk, yeast, sugar, and egg until smooth. Knead lightly and allow it to rise until doubled. Roll the dough out and fold in layers of butter to create a laminated structure. Chill the dough between folds to maintain layers. Roll out again and cut into desired shapes. Place on a baking tray and allow to rise again. Bake in a preheated oven until golden and flaky. Allow to cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 50g · fat 25g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Keep butter cold for proper lamination.","pairsWith":"fruit jam · custard · chocolate spread","trivia":"Inspired by Austrian baking traditions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-koldskal","name":"Koldskal","nameAlt":"Cold Buttermilk Soup","aliases":["Koldskål","Danish Cold Soup"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"200ml buttermilk · 50g yogurt · 30g sugar · 5g lemon juice · 20g biscuits","ingredients12":"2400ml buttermilk · 600g yogurt · 360g sugar · 60g lemon juice · 240g biscuits","method":"In a bowl, combine buttermilk, yogurt, sugar, and lemon juice. Whisk until smooth and slightly frothy. Taste and adjust sweetness or acidity if needed. Chill the mixture in the refrigerator until cold. Crush the biscuits lightly for topping. Pour the cold soup into serving bowls. Sprinkle the crushed biscuits over the top. Serve immediately while chilled.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 40g · fat 6g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Serve very cold for best taste.","pairsWith":"strawberries · oat biscuits · fruit compote","trivia":"A refreshing Danish summer dessert.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-roedgroed","name":"Roedgroed","nameAlt":"Red Berry Pudding","aliases":["Rødgrød med fløde","Danish Berry Dessert"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"150g mixed berries · 300ml water · 30g sugar · 5g starch · 50ml cream","ingredients12":"1800g mixed berries · 3600ml water · 360g sugar · 60g starch · 600ml cream","method":"Combine the berries and water in a pot and bring to a gentle boil. Allow the berries to soften and release their juices. Add sugar and stir until dissolved. In a separate bowl, mix starch with cold water to form a slurry. Pour the slurry into the berry mixture while stirring continuously. Cook until the mixture thickens into a pudding-like consistency. Remove from heat and allow it to cool slightly. Serve with cream poured over the top.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 3g · carbs 50g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Adjust sugar depending on berry tartness.","pairsWith":"cream · vanilla custard · biscuits","trivia":"Famously difficult Danish phrase to pronounce.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-hakkebof","name":"Hakkebof","nameAlt":"Danish Beef Patty with Onions","aliases":["Hakkebøf","Hamburger Steak"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"family dinner","ingredients":"180g ground beef · 50g onion · 10ml oil · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"2160g ground beef · 600g onion · 120ml oil · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Shape the ground beef into a thick patty and season with salt and pepper. Slice the onion into rings. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat and cook the beef patty until browned on both sides. Continue cooking until fully cooked through. In the same pan, cook the onion rings until soft and caramelized. Stir occasionally to prevent burning. Place the onions on top of the patty. Let rest briefly before serving.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 10g · fat 35g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Cook on medium heat for juiciness.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · gravy · pickled beetroot","trivia":"A traditional Danish home-style dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-braendende-kaerlighed","name":"Braendende Kaerlighed","nameAlt":"Mashed Potatoes with Bacon and Onions","aliases":["Brændende kærlighed","Burning Love"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"comfort food","ingredients":"250g potatoes · 100g bacon · 50g onion · 30ml milk · 10g butter · 5g salt","ingredients12":"3000g potatoes · 1200g bacon · 600g onion · 360ml milk · 120g butter · 60g salt","method":"Peel and boil the potatoes until tender, then mash with milk and butter until smooth. Season with salt to taste. Cut the bacon into pieces and fry until crisp. Remove bacon and cook chopped onion in the same pan until soft. Combine bacon and onion together. Spoon mashed potatoes onto a plate and top with the bacon mixture. Mix lightly before serving. Serve hot.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 50g · fat 35g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use starchy potatoes for best mash.","pairsWith":"pickled beetroot · green salad · mustard","trivia":"The name translates to 'burning love'.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-flaeskesteg","name":"Flaeskesteg","nameAlt":"Roast Pork with Crackling","aliases":["Flæskesteg","Danish Roast Pork"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"250g pork roast · 5g salt · 2g pepper · 300ml water","ingredients12":"3000g pork roast · 60g salt · 24g pepper · 3600ml water","method":"Score the pork skin carefully without cutting too deep into the meat. Rub salt into the skin and season the meat with pepper. Place the pork in a roasting dish with water at the bottom. Roast in a preheated oven until the skin becomes crisp and golden. Increase heat toward the end for crackling. Check that meat is fully cooked and tender. Let rest before slicing. Serve hot.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":650,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 0g · fat 55g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Dry skin ensures crispy crackling.","pairsWith":"potatoes · red cabbage · gravy","trivia":"A Danish Christmas classic.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-tarteletter","name":"Tarteletter","nameAlt":"Chicken and Asparagus Tartlets","aliases":["Tarteletter med høns i asparges"],"course":"starter","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"festive","ingredients":"100g chicken · 50g asparagus · 100ml cream · 20g flour · 50g tart shells · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g chicken · 600g asparagus · 1200ml cream · 240g flour · 600g tart shells · 60g salt","method":"Cook the chicken until tender and shred into pieces. Cut asparagus into small pieces and cook until tender. Prepare a sauce by heating cream and adding flour to thicken. Stir until smooth. Add chicken and asparagus into the sauce and mix well. Season with salt. Warm tart shells in the oven. Fill shells with the mixture evenly. Serve immediately while warm.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 25g · fat 25g","storage":"Store filling separately for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Avoid overcooking asparagus.","pairsWith":"green salad · pickled vegetables · potatoes","trivia":"A classic Danish party dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-gammeldags-kylling","name":"Gammeldags Kylling","nameAlt":"Old-Fashioned Chicken Stew","aliases":["Danish Chicken Stew"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"family meal","ingredients":"200g chicken · 50g carrot · 50g leek · 200ml broth · 100ml cream · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"2400g chicken · 600g carrot · 600g leek · 2400ml broth · 1200ml cream · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Cut chicken into pieces and cook in broth until tender. Slice vegetables and add to the broth. Cook until vegetables soften. Stir in cream and simmer gently. Season with salt and pepper. Continue cooking until flavors combine and sauce thickens slightly. Stir occasionally. Serve hot.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 20g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Simmer gently for tender chicken.","pairsWith":"potatoes · parsley · bread","trivia":"A comforting Danish home dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-pebernodder","name":"Pebernodder","nameAlt":"Danish Spiced Cookies","aliases":["Pebernødder","Pepper Nuts"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"150g flour · 80g sugar · 50g butter · 1 egg · 5g spices","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 960g sugar · 600g butter · 12 eggs · 60g spices","method":"Cream butter and sugar until light. Add egg and mix well. Gradually add flour and spices to form dough. Roll dough into small balls. Place on baking tray. Bake until golden. Allow to cool completely. Store once cooled. Serve as snack.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 45g · fat 15g","storage":"Store in airtight container for up to 2 weeks.","chefNotes":"Keep cookies small for best texture.","pairsWith":"fruit compote · cream · biscuits","trivia":"A Danish Christmas tradition.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"denmark-citronfromage","name":"Citronfromage","nameAlt":"Lemon Mousse Dessert","aliases":["Lemon Fromage"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Denmark","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"100ml cream · 50g sugar · 10ml lemon juice · 1 egg · 5g gelatin","ingredients12":"1200ml cream · 600g sugar · 120ml lemon juice · 12 eggs · 60g gelatin","method":"Whisk egg and sugar until pale. Heat lemon juice and dissolve gelatin into it. Add to egg mixture while stirring. Whip cream to soft peaks. Fold cream into mixture gently. Pour into serving dishes. Chill until set. Serve cold.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 35g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overheat gelatin.","pairsWith":"berry sauce · biscuits · fruit","trivia":"A classic light Danish dessert.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-karjalanpiirakka","name":"Karjalanpiirakka","nameAlt":"Karelian Rice Pie","aliases":["Karjalan piirakka","Karelian Pasty"],"course":"side","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g rye flour · 50g wheat flour · 100ml water · 5g salt · 150g rice · 300ml milk","ingredients12":"1200g rye flour · 600g wheat flour · 1200ml water · 60g salt · 1800g rice · 3600ml milk","method":"Prepare a dough by mixing rye flour, wheat flour, water, and salt until firm. Roll the dough into thin oval shapes. Cook rice in milk until it becomes a thick porridge. Allow the filling to cool slightly before use. Spoon the rice mixture onto the center of each dough piece. Fold and crimp the edges to create the traditional shape. Bake in a preheated oven until the crust is firm and slightly crisp. Brush lightly with butter after baking. Serve warm.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 60g · fat 8g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Keep crust thin for authentic texture.","pairsWith":"egg butter · smoked fish · cucumber salad","trivia":"A traditional dish from the Karelia region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-poronkaristys","name":"Poronkäristys","nameAlt":"Sauteed Reindeer","aliases":["Poronkaristys","Reindeer Stew"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"200g reindeer meat · 150g potatoes · 50g onion · 10ml oil · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"2400g reindeer meat · 1800g potatoes · 600g onion · 120ml oil · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Slice the reindeer meat thinly and set aside. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat and sauté chopped onion until soft. Add the meat and cook until browned on all sides. Season with salt and pepper. Lower the heat and allow the meat to simmer gently until tender. Boil potatoes separately until soft. Stir occasionally to ensure even cooking. Serve the meat hot alongside the potatoes.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 35g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Cook slowly to keep meat tender.","pairsWith":"lingonberry jam · pickled cucumber · mashed potatoes","trivia":"A staple dish of the Sami people.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-hernekeitto","name":"Hernekeitto","nameAlt":"Finnish Pea Soup","aliases":["Herne keitto","Pea Soup Finland"],"course":"main","type":"legume","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"Thursday meal","ingredients":"150g dried peas · 100g pork · 50g onion · 500ml water · 5g salt · 2g mustard","ingredients12":"1800g dried peas · 1200g pork · 600g onion · 6000ml water · 60g salt · 24g mustard","method":"Rinse the dried peas thoroughly and soak them if needed. Place the peas in a pot with water and bring to a boil. Add chopped pork and onion. Reduce heat and simmer slowly until peas soften and break down. Stir occasionally to prevent sticking. Add salt and mustard for flavor. Continue cooking until thick and hearty. Taste and adjust seasoning. Serve hot.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 40g · fat 15g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Slow simmering improves texture.","pairsWith":"mustard · rye bread · pancakes","trivia":"Traditionally eaten on Thursdays in Finland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-kalakukko","name":"Kalakukko","nameAlt":"Fish and Pork Rye Pie","aliases":["Kalakukko pie","Fish bread Finland"],"course":"main","type":"seafood","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"200g fish · 100g pork · 200g rye dough · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g fish · 1200g pork · 2400g rye dough · 60g salt","method":"Prepare a rye dough and roll it into a large flat shape. Place fish and pork pieces in the center of the dough. Season lightly with salt. Fold the dough over the filling and seal tightly. Place the pie into a baking dish. Bake in a preheated oven for several hours until fully cooked. Ensure the crust is firm and the filling is tender. Allow to cool slightly before slicing. Serve warm.","cookTime":"180 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 40g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Seal dough well to retain moisture.","pairsWith":"butter · milk · pickled vegetables","trivia":"A traditional dish from Eastern Finland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-lohikeitto","name":"Lohikeitto","nameAlt":"Finnish Salmon Soup","aliases":["Salmon Soup Finland","Lohi keitto"],"course":"main","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"everyday meal","ingredients":"150g salmon · 100g potatoes · 50g carrot · 200ml broth · 100ml cream · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"1800g salmon · 1200g potatoes · 600g carrot · 2400ml broth · 1200ml cream · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Peel and dice the potatoes and carrots into small pieces. Bring broth to a simmer and add vegetables. Cook until they begin to soften. Add salmon pieces and cook gently until fish flakes easily. Stir in cream and reduce heat. Season with salt and pepper. Simmer briefly to combine flavors. Serve hot once ready.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 25g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Avoid overcooking fish.","pairsWith":"rye bread · butter · dill","trivia":"A classic Finnish comfort soup.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-mustikkapiirakka","name":"Mustikkapiirakka","nameAlt":"Finnish Blueberry Pie","aliases":["Blueberry Pie Finland","Mustikka piirakka"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"150g blueberries · 100g flour · 50g butter · 50g sugar · 1 egg","ingredients12":"1800g blueberries · 1200g flour · 600g butter · 600g sugar · 12 eggs","method":"Prepare a dough by mixing flour, butter, sugar, and egg until smooth. Press the dough into a baking dish evenly. Spread blueberries over the surface. Bake in a preheated oven until the crust is golden and filling is set. Allow to cool slightly before serving. Slice into portions. Serve warm or cold.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 50g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use fresh berries for best flavor.","pairsWith":"vanilla sauce · cream · yogurt","trivia":"Wild blueberries are widely used in Finland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-ruisleipa","name":"Ruisleipa","nameAlt":"Finnish Rye Bread","aliases":["Ruisleipä","Finnish Rye Bread"],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g rye flour · 120ml water · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g rye flour · 1440ml water · 60g salt","method":"Mix rye flour, water, and salt into a firm dough. Knead briefly until smooth. Shape into flat rounds or loaves. Place onto a baking tray. Bake in a preheated oven until firm and cooked through. Check for a hollow sound when tapped. Allow to cool completely before slicing. Store once cooled.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 50g · fat 2g","storage":"Store in a dry container for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Dense texture is traditional.","pairsWith":"butter · cheese · smoked fish","trivia":"A staple bread in Finnish cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-graavilohi","name":"Graavilohi","nameAlt":"Finnish Cured Salmon","aliases":["Graavilohi Finland","Gravlax Finnish Style"],"course":"starter","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"holiday","ingredients":"150g salmon · 20g salt · 15g sugar · 5g dill · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g salmon · 240g salt · 180g sugar · 60g dill · 24g black pepper","method":"Check the salmon for bones and remove them carefully. Mix salt, sugar, and black pepper in a bowl until evenly combined. Rub the mixture thoroughly over the salmon fillet. Place fresh dill over the fish and wrap tightly. Place the wrapped fish in a dish and weigh it down slightly. Refrigerate for 24 to 48 hours, turning occasionally. Once cured, scrape off excess seasoning. Slice thinly before serving and present chilled.","cookTime":"2880 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 5g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate and consume within 3 days.","chefNotes":"Slice thinly for best texture.","pairsWith":"mustard dill sauce · boiled potatoes · rye bread","trivia":"A Nordic preservation method shared across countries.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-kaalilaatikko","name":"Kaalilaatikko","nameAlt":"Finnish Cabbage Casserole","aliases":["Cabbage Box","Kaalilaatikko casserole"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"home cooking","ingredients":"200g cabbage · 100g ground beef · 50g rice · 100ml broth · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"2400g cabbage · 1200g ground beef · 600g rice · 1200ml broth · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Chop the cabbage into thin strips and cook it lightly until softened. Cook the rice separately until tender. In a bowl, combine the cabbage, cooked rice, and ground beef. Add broth and season with salt and pepper. Transfer the mixture into a baking dish evenly. Bake in a preheated oven until the top is golden and the mixture is fully cooked. Stir occasionally during baking if needed. Allow it to rest before serving. Serve warm once ready.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 35g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"A touch of sweetness can enhance flavor.","pairsWith":"lingonberry jam · boiled potatoes · cucumber salad","trivia":"A classic Finnish comfort dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-lihapiirakka","name":"Lihapiirakka","nameAlt":"Finnish Meat Pie","aliases":["Finnish Meat Pastry","Lihapiirakka pie"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"street food","ingredients":"150g dough · 100g ground beef · 50g rice · 10ml oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g dough · 1200g ground beef · 600g rice · 120ml oil · 60g salt","method":"Prepare a simple dough and allow it to rest briefly. Cook the rice until tender and set aside. Brown the ground beef in a pan and season with salt. Mix the beef with the cooked rice to form the filling. Roll out the dough and place portions of filling in the center. Fold and seal the dough into oval shapes. Fry or bake until golden and cooked through. Allow to cool slightly before serving. Serve warm as a snack or meal.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 50g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Seal edges well to prevent leaks.","pairsWith":"pickled cucumber · mustard · coleslaw","trivia":"A popular Finnish street food item.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-pannukakku","name":"Pannukakku","nameAlt":"Finnish Oven Pancake","aliases":["Finnish Pancake","Oven Pancake Finland"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"150g flour · 200ml milk · 1 egg · 30g sugar · 10g butter","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 2400ml milk · 12 eggs · 360g sugar · 120g butter","method":"Whisk together flour, milk, egg, and sugar to form a smooth batter. Grease a baking dish with butter and pour in the batter evenly. Place the dish in a preheated oven. Bake until the pancake is golden and set in the center. Check doneness by lightly pressing the surface. Allow it to cool slightly before cutting into pieces. Serve warm or at room temperature. Enjoy once ready.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 55g · fat 12g","storage":"Store in the refrigerator for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overbake to keep it soft.","pairsWith":"berry jam · whipped cream · fresh fruit","trivia":"A simple and popular Finnish dessert.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-siskonmakkarakeitto","name":"Siskonmakkarakeitto","nameAlt":"Finnish Sausage Soup","aliases":["Sausage Soup Finland","Siskonmakkara soup"],"course":"main","type":"meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"everyday meal","ingredients":"150g sausage · 100g potatoes · 50g carrot · 300ml broth · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"1800g sausage · 1200g potatoes · 600g carrot · 3600ml broth · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Peel and dice the potatoes and carrots into small pieces. Bring the broth to a gentle boil in a pot. Add the vegetables and cook until they begin to soften. Remove the sausage from its casing and form small pieces directly into the soup. Allow the sausage to cook until fully done. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Simmer briefly to combine flavors. Serve hot once ready.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 30g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Add sausage gently to maintain shape.","pairsWith":"rye bread · butter · pickled vegetables","trivia":"A comforting Finnish home-style soup.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-leipajuusto","name":"Leipäjuusto","nameAlt":"Finnish Squeaky Cheese Dessert","aliases":["Bread Cheese","Finnish Cheese Curds"],"course":"dessert","type":"dairy","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"dessert","ingredients":"150g cheese · 50g cloudberry jam","ingredients12":"1800g cheese · 600g cloudberry jam","method":"Slice the cheese into thick pieces and place them in a baking dish. Warm the cheese gently in the oven until it softens but does not melt completely. Remove from the oven once heated through. Spoon cloudberry jam over the warm cheese evenly. Allow the flavors to combine slightly. Serve immediately while warm. Enjoy the contrast of textures. Finish once ready.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 20g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overheat to maintain texture.","pairsWith":"berry compote · cream · oat biscuits","trivia":"Known for its squeaky texture when eaten.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-runebergintorttu","name":"Runebergintorttu","nameAlt":"Runeberg Torte","aliases":["Runeberg Cake","Runebergin torttu"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"Runeberg Day","ingredients":"100g flour · 80g sugar · 50g butter · 1 egg · 20g jam · 10g icing","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 960g sugar · 600g butter · 12 eggs · 240g jam · 120g icing","method":"Cream the butter and sugar together until light and fluffy. Add the egg and mix until fully incorporated. Gradually add flour to form a smooth batter. Spoon the batter into small molds evenly. Bake in a preheated oven until golden and cooked through. Allow the cakes to cool completely. Top each cake with a small amount of jam and a ring of icing. Let the decoration set before serving. Serve once ready.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 50g · fat 18g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use raspberry jam for authentic flavor.","pairsWith":"coffee cake · berry sauce · whipped cream","trivia":"Named after Finnish poet Johan Ludvig Runeberg.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-rosolli","name":"Rosolli","nameAlt":"Finnish Beetroot Salad","aliases":["Rosolli salad","Beetroot Salad Finland"],"course":"side","type":"vegetable","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"150g beetroot · 100g potatoes · 50g carrot · 30g pickles · 50ml cream · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g beetroot · 1200g potatoes · 600g carrot · 360g pickles · 600ml cream · 60g salt","method":"Boil the beetroot, potatoes, and carrots separately until tender, then allow them to cool completely. Peel and dice all the vegetables into small uniform cubes. Chop the pickles into similar-sized pieces for even texture. In a bowl, combine all the diced ingredients gently. Add cream and season with salt to taste. Mix carefully to avoid breaking the vegetables. Chill the salad in the refrigerator before serving. Serve cold once flavors have melded.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 40g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Dice evenly for balanced texture.","pairsWith":"roast meats · boiled eggs · rye bread","trivia":"A traditional Finnish Christmas side dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-paistetut-muikut","name":"Paistetut Muikut","nameAlt":"Fried Vendace Fish","aliases":["Muikku fry","Finnish Fried Fish"],"course":"main","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"200g vendace fish · 50g flour · 10ml oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g vendace fish · 600g flour · 120ml oil · 60g salt","method":"Clean the small fish and pat them dry thoroughly. Toss the fish lightly in flour and salt until evenly coated. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat until hot. Add the fish in batches and fry until golden and crisp. Turn carefully to cook both sides evenly. Continue frying until the fish are fully cooked and crunchy. Remove and drain excess oil on paper. Serve immediately while hot.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 20g · fat 18g","storage":"Best consumed fresh, can refrigerate for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Do not overcrowd the pan for crispiness.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · dill sauce · lemon wedges","trivia":"A popular street and market food in Finland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-kanttarellikastike","name":"Kanttarellikastike","nameAlt":"Chanterelle Mushroom Sauce","aliases":["Chanterelle Sauce","Kanttarelli kastike"],"course":"side","type":"sauce","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"autumn","ingredients":"150g chanterelle mushrooms · 50g onion · 100ml cream · 10g butter · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"1800g chanterelle mushrooms · 600g onion · 1200ml cream · 120g butter · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Clean the mushrooms thoroughly and chop them into bite-sized pieces. Finely chop the onion and sauté it in butter until soft. Add the mushrooms and cook until they release moisture and begin to brown. Stir occasionally to ensure even cooking. Pour in the cream and reduce the heat to a gentle simmer. Allow the sauce to thicken slightly. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Serve warm once ready.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 12g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not wash mushrooms excessively to retain flavor.","pairsWith":"boiled potatoes · grilled meat · pasta","trivia":"Chanterelles are widely foraged in Finnish forests.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-riisipuuro","name":"Riisipuuro","nameAlt":"Finnish Rice Porridge","aliases":["Rice Porridge Finland","Riisi puuro"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"100g rice · 300ml milk · 20g sugar · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g rice · 3600ml milk · 240g sugar · 24g salt","method":"Combine the rice and a small amount of water in a pot and bring to a gentle boil. Once the water is absorbed, add the milk gradually while stirring. Cook the mixture over low heat, stirring frequently to prevent sticking. Allow the rice to soften completely and absorb the milk. Add sugar and salt to balance the flavor. Continue cooking until the porridge reaches a creamy consistency. Stir occasionally to maintain smooth texture. Serve warm once ready.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 50g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Stir frequently to prevent burning.","pairsWith":"cinnamon sugar · berry compote · milk","trivia":"An almond is hidden in the porridge for luck.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-graavilohi-sandwich","name":"Graavilohi Sandwich","nameAlt":"Cured Salmon Open Sandwich","aliases":["Finnish Salmon Sandwich","Graavilohi leipä"],"course":"starter","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"lunch","ingredients":"100g rye bread · 80g cured salmon · 30g cream cheese · 10g dill · 10g lemon","ingredients12":"1200g rye bread · 960g cured salmon · 360g cream cheese · 120g dill · 120g lemon","method":"Slice the rye bread evenly and lay it flat. Spread cream cheese over the bread as a base layer. Arrange thin slices of cured salmon evenly on top. Squeeze a small amount of lemon juice over the salmon. Sprinkle fresh dill for flavor and presentation. Assemble carefully to keep layers intact. Serve immediately while fresh. Enjoy as a light meal or starter.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 25g · fat 18g","storage":"Best consumed fresh.","chefNotes":"Use thin salmon slices for best texture.","pairsWith":"cucumber salad · boiled eggs · pickled vegetables","trivia":"A common Finnish café offering.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-mammi","name":"Mämmi","nameAlt":"Finnish Rye Malt Dessert","aliases":["Mammi","Rye Malt Pudding"],"course":"dessert","type":"sweet","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"Easter","ingredients":"150g rye flour · 50g malt · 300ml water · 20g sugar · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g rye flour · 600g malt · 3600ml water · 240g sugar · 24g salt","method":"Mix rye flour and malt with warm water to form a thick mixture. Allow the mixture to rest to develop sweetness naturally. Heat the mixture slowly while stirring to prevent burning. Add sugar and salt to enhance flavor. Transfer the mixture to a baking dish. Bake slowly in the oven until thickened and darkened. Allow it to cool completely to set. Serve chilled once ready.","cookTime":"120 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 55g · fat 2g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 5 days.","chefNotes":"Resting enhances natural sweetness.","pairsWith":"cream · milk · sugar","trivia":"A traditional Finnish Easter dessert with a unique flavor.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"finland-silakkapihvit","name":"Silakkapihvit","nameAlt":"Baltic Herring Patties","aliases":["Herring Patties Finland","Silakka pihvit"],"course":"main","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"northern-europe","country":"Finland","occasion":"everyday meal","ingredients":"150g herring · 50g flour · 1 egg · 10ml oil · 5g salt · 2g pepper","ingredients12":"1800g herring · 600g flour · 12 eggs · 120ml oil · 60g salt · 24g pepper","method":"Clean the herring and remove bones carefully. Dip the fish in beaten egg and coat lightly with flour. Season with salt and pepper. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat. Fry the patties until golden and crisp on both sides. Turn carefully to maintain shape. Continue cooking until fully cooked through. Remove and drain excess oil. Serve hot once ready.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":360,"nutrition":"protein 24g · carbs 20g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use fresh fish for best flavor.","pairsWith":"mashed potatoes · dill sauce · pickled cucumber","trivia":"A traditional coastal Finnish dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-pierogi-ruskie","name":"Pierogi ruskie","nameAlt":"Potato and Cheese Dumplings","aliases":["pierogi z ziemniakami i twarogiem"],"course":"main","type":"dumpling","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g wheat flour · 100ml water · 1 egg · 5g salt · 150g potatoes · 100g twarog cheese · 50g onion · 20g butter · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g wheat flour · 1200ml water · 12 eggs · 60g salt · 1800g potatoes · 1200g twarog cheese · 600g onion · 240g butter · 24g black pepper","method":"Mix flour, water, egg and salt to form a soft dough and rest it for 20 minutes. Boil potatoes until tender then mash smoothly. Fry chopped onion in butter on medium for about 5 minutes until golden. Combine potatoes, cheese, onion, salt and pepper into a filling. Roll dough thinly and cut circles, then fill and seal the edges. Boil dumplings in salted water until they float, about 3 minutes. Remove and lightly fry in butter on medium for 4 minutes until golden.","cookTime":"40-50 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 70g · fat 15g","storage":"Store refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Resting the dough improves elasticity and makes sealing easier.","pairsWith":"sour cream · fried bacon · dill","trivia":"Despite the name, ruskie pierogi are a classic Polish dish not from Russia.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-bigos","name":"Bigos","nameAlt":"Hunter’s Stew","aliases":["kapusta z miesem"],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"150g sauerkraut · 100g white cabbage · 100g pork · 50g smoked sausage · 50g onion · 20g dried mushrooms · 200ml water · 5g garlic · 2g black pepper · 2g bay leaf","ingredients12":"1800g sauerkraut · 1200g white cabbage · 1200g pork · 600g smoked sausage · 600g onion · 240g dried mushrooms · 2400ml water · 60g garlic · 24g black pepper · 24g bay leaf","method":"Soak dried mushrooms in warm water for 20 minutes. Fry chopped onion and pork on medium heat for about 6 minutes until browned. Add sausage slices and cook another 4 minutes. Stir in sauerkraut, chopped cabbage and soaked mushrooms with their liquid. Add garlic, pepper and bay leaf and simmer on low heat for 60 minutes. Stir occasionally to prevent sticking and blend flavors. Taste and adjust seasoning before serving hot.","cookTime":"70-80 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 20g · fat 35g","storage":"Keeps well refrigerated for up to 4 days and improves in flavor.","chefNotes":"Reheating over several days deepens the taste significantly.","pairsWith":"rye bread · mustard · pickles","trivia":"Bigos was traditionally cooked over days by hunters in forests.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-zurek","name":"Żurek","nameAlt":"Sour Rye Soup","aliases":["zurek"],"course":"starter","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"Easter","ingredients":"300ml sour rye starter · 100g sausage · 50g bacon · 50g onion · 1 egg · 5g garlic · 2g marjoram · 500ml water · 3g salt","ingredients12":"3600ml sour rye starter · 1200g sausage · 600g bacon · 600g onion · 12 eggs · 60g garlic · 24g marjoram · 6000ml water · 36g salt","method":"Fry chopped bacon and onion on medium heat for about 5 minutes until crisp. Add sliced sausage and cook for another 4 minutes. Pour in water and bring to a gentle boil. Stir in sour rye starter and simmer on low heat for 20 minutes. Add garlic, marjoram and salt and cook briefly. Boil egg separately for 8 minutes and slice. Serve soup hot with egg pieces added just before serving.","cookTime":"35-40 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 25g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days and reheat gently.","chefNotes":"Use good quality fermented rye starter for authentic tang.","pairsWith":"rye bread · horseradish · boiled potatoes","trivia":"Żurek is a staple Easter soup in Poland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-kotlet-schabowy","name":"Kotlet schabowy","nameAlt":"Breaded Pork Cutlet","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"cutlet","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g pork loin · 50g breadcrumbs · 1 egg · 30g flour · 50ml oil · 3g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g pork loin · 600g breadcrumbs · 12 eggs · 360g flour · 600ml oil · 36g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Pound pork loin to even thickness. Season with salt and pepper on both sides. Coat in flour, dip in beaten egg, then cover in breadcrumbs. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat. Fry the cutlet for about 4 minutes per side until golden brown. Ensure the meat is cooked through before serving. Rest briefly on paper towel to remove excess oil.","cookTime":"15-20 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 30g · fat 30g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use fresh breadcrumbs for a crispier crust.","pairsWith":"mashed potatoes · cabbage salad · lemon","trivia":"This dish is Poland’s version of schnitzel.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-golabki","name":"Gołąbki","nameAlt":"Stuffed Cabbage Rolls","aliases":["golabki"],"course":"main","type":"stuffed","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"family","ingredients":"2 cabbage leaves · 150g minced pork · 50g rice · 50g onion · 200ml tomato sauce · 5g garlic · 3g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"24 cabbage leaves · 1800g minced pork · 600g rice · 600g onion · 2400ml tomato sauce · 60g garlic · 36g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Boil cabbage leaves briefly until soft. Cook rice until just tender, about 10 minutes. Fry onion and garlic on medium heat for 5 minutes until fragrant. Mix minced pork, rice, onion, garlic, salt and pepper. Place filling in cabbage leaves and roll tightly. Arrange rolls in a pot and cover with tomato sauce. Simmer on low heat for 50 minutes until cooked through. Serve warm with extra sauce.","cookTime":"60-70 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 40g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days in sauce.","chefNotes":"Do not overfill the leaves to avoid tearing.","pairsWith":"potatoes · sour cream · dill","trivia":"The name means “little pigeons” in Polish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-barszcz-czerwony","name":"Barszcz czerwony","nameAlt":"Beetroot Soup","aliases":["borscht polski"],"course":"starter","type":"soup","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"200g beetroot · 500ml water · 50g onion · 5g garlic · 10ml vinegar · 3g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g beetroot · 6000ml water · 600g onion · 60g garlic · 120ml vinegar · 36g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Peel and slice beetroot and place in a pot with water. Add chopped onion and garlic. Bring to a boil then simmer on low heat for 40 minutes. Add vinegar, salt and pepper. Strain the soup for a clear broth. Heat gently before serving. Serve hot as a light starter.","cookTime":"45-50 min","kcal":120,"nutrition":"protein 3g · carbs 25g · fat 1g","storage":"Store refrigerated for up to 4 days.","chefNotes":"A splash of vinegar keeps the color vibrant.","pairsWith":"dumplings · rye bread · sour cream","trivia":"Often served on Christmas Eve in Poland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-placki-ziemniaczane","name":"Placki ziemniaczane","nameAlt":"Potato Pancakes","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"pancake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g potatoes · 1 egg · 30g flour · 50ml oil · 3g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g potatoes · 12 eggs · 360g flour · 600ml oil · 36g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Grate potatoes and squeeze out excess liquid. Mix with egg, flour, salt and pepper. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat. Spoon batter into the pan and flatten. Fry each pancake for about 3 minutes per side until golden. Drain on paper towel before serving. Serve hot for best texture.","cookTime":"20-25 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 45g · fat 15g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days and reheat in a pan.","chefNotes":"Squeezing potatoes well prevents soggy pancakes.","pairsWith":"sour cream · applesauce · sugar","trivia":"Can be served sweet or savory depending on toppings.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-kielbasa-grill","name":"Kiełbasa z grilla","nameAlt":"Grilled Sausage","aliases":["kielbasa"],"course":"main","type":"grill","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"bbq","ingredients":"200g kielbasa sausage · 50g onion · 10g mustard · 5g garlic · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g kielbasa sausage · 600g onion · 120g mustard · 60g garlic · 24g black pepper","method":"Preheat grill to medium heat. Score sausage lightly to prevent bursting. Grill for about 10 minutes turning occasionally until browned. Add sliced onion to grill and cook until soft, about 6 minutes. Season with garlic and pepper. Serve hot with mustard on the side. Ensure sausage is heated through before serving.","cookTime":"15-20 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 5g · fat 50g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Avoid high heat to prevent splitting the casing.","pairsWith":"bread · mustard · pickles","trivia":"Kiełbasa refers broadly to Polish sausages of many kinds.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-sernik","name":"Sernik","nameAlt":"Polish Cheesecake","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"holiday","ingredients":"200g twarog cheese · 100g sugar · 2 eggs · 50g butter · 30g flour · 5g vanilla extract","ingredients12":"2400g twarog cheese · 1200g sugar · 24 eggs · 600g butter · 360g flour · 60g vanilla extract","method":"Preheat oven to 180°C. Mix cheese, sugar and butter until smooth. Add eggs one at a time and blend well. Stir in flour and vanilla extract. Pour batter into a greased baking tin. Bake for about 45 minutes until set. Allow to cool before slicing. Serve chilled or at room temperature.","cookTime":"50-60 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 15g · carbs 35g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 4 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overbake to keep the texture creamy.","pairsWith":"coffee · berries · cream","trivia":"Polish cheesecake often uses twaróg instead of cream cheese.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-makowiec","name":"Makowiec","nameAlt":"Poppy Seed Roll","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"200g flour · 100ml milk · 1 egg · 50g butter · 150g poppy seeds · 80g sugar · 5g yeast","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1200ml milk · 12 eggs · 600g butter · 1800g poppy seeds · 960g sugar · 60g yeast","method":"Activate yeast in warm milk for 10 minutes. Mix flour, egg, butter and yeast mixture into a dough. Knead until smooth and let rise for 60 minutes. Grind poppy seeds and mix with sugar. Roll dough flat and spread filling evenly. Roll into a log and place on a baking tray. Bake at 180°C for 35 minutes until golden. Cool before slicing.","cookTime":"50-60 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 60g · fat 22g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let the dough rise fully for a soft texture.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee · dried fruit","trivia":"Makowiec is a traditional Christmas dessert in Poland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-kompot","name":"Kompot","nameAlt":"Fruit Drink","aliases":[],"course":"drink","type":"beverage","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g apples · 50g sugar · 500ml water · 2g cinnamon","ingredients12":"2400g apples · 600g sugar · 6000ml water · 24g cinnamon","method":"Chop apples into pieces without peeling. Add to a pot with water and bring to a boil. Reduce heat and simmer for 20 minutes until fruit softens. Add sugar and cinnamon and stir well. Let cool slightly before serving. Serve warm or chilled depending on preference. Strain if a clear drink is desired.","cookTime":"25-30 min","kcal":120,"nutrition":"protein 1g · carbs 30g · fat 0g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use a mix of fruits for richer flavor.","pairsWith":"cakes · pastries · biscuits","trivia":"Kompot is commonly served at family meals in Poland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-krokiety","name":"Krokiety","nameAlt":"Stuffed Crepes","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"crepe","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"holiday","ingredients":"100g flour · 200ml milk · 1 egg · 100g cabbage · 50g mushrooms · 50g breadcrumbs · 50ml oil · 3g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 2400ml milk · 12 eggs · 1200g cabbage · 600g mushrooms · 600g breadcrumbs · 600ml oil · 36g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Mix flour, milk and egg into a smooth batter. Fry thin crepes on medium heat for about 2 minutes per side. Cook cabbage and mushrooms in a pan for 10 minutes until soft. Season filling with salt and pepper. Place filling on crepes and roll tightly. Coat rolls in breadcrumbs. Fry on medium heat for 5 minutes until golden. Serve hot and crisp.","cookTime":"35-45 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 15g · carbs 55g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days and reheat in a pan.","chefNotes":"Make crepes thin for easier rolling.","pairsWith":"barszcz · sour cream · pickles","trivia":"Krokiety are often served with beetroot soup.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-zapiekanka","name":"Zapiekanka","nameAlt":"Open-Faced Baguette Pizza","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"sandwich","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"1 baguette · 100g mushrooms · 50g cheese · 20g butter · 10g ketchup · 3g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"12 baguettes · 1200g mushrooms · 600g cheese · 240g butter · 120g ketchup · 36g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Slice the baguette lengthwise and lightly butter the cut sides. Chop mushrooms and sauté in butter on medium heat for about 6 minutes until soft. Spread mushrooms over the bread evenly. Top with grated cheese and season with salt and pepper. Bake at 200°C for 10 minutes until cheese melts and bread crisps. Drizzle ketchup on top before serving. Serve hot immediately.","cookTime":"15-20 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 14g · carbs 50g · fat 18g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Use a crusty baguette for best texture.","pairsWith":"cola · pickles · salad","trivia":"Zapiekanka became popular in Poland during the 1970s as fast food.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-fasolka-po-bretonsku","name":"Fasolka po bretońsku","nameAlt":"Baked Beans with Sausage","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g white beans · 100g sausage · 50g bacon · 50g onion · 200ml tomato sauce · 5g garlic · 3g paprika · 3g salt","ingredients12":"2400g white beans · 1200g sausage · 600g bacon · 600g onion · 2400ml tomato sauce · 60g garlic · 36g paprika · 36g salt","method":"Soak beans overnight then boil until tender for about 60 minutes. Fry chopped bacon and onion on medium heat for 6 minutes until golden. Add sausage slices and cook for 4 minutes. Stir in tomato sauce, garlic and paprika. Add cooked beans and mix well. Simmer on low heat for 20 minutes to combine flavors. Serve hot.","cookTime":"80-90 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 45g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Soaking beans reduces cooking time and improves texture.","pairsWith":"bread · pickles · mustard","trivia":"Despite its name, the dish is uniquely Polish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-kluski-slaskie","name":"Kluski śląskie","nameAlt":"Silesian Potato Dumplings","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"dumpling","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"family","ingredients":"200g potatoes · 50g potato starch · 1 egg · 3g salt","ingredients12":"2400g potatoes · 600g potato starch · 12 eggs · 36g salt","method":"Boil potatoes until soft and mash smoothly. Mix with potato starch, egg and salt to form a dough. Shape into small balls and press a dimple in the center. Boil in salted water until they float, about 3 minutes. Remove with a slotted spoon and drain well. Serve warm with sauce or gravy.","cookTime":"30-35 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 60g · fat 3g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"The dimple helps hold sauce when serving.","pairsWith":"gravy · roast meat · cabbage","trivia":"These dumplings originate from the Silesia region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-kapusta-z-grochem","name":"Kapusta z grochem","nameAlt":"Cabbage with Split Peas","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"stew","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"150g sauerkraut · 100g split peas · 50g onion · 20g butter · 3g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g sauerkraut · 1200g split peas · 600g onion · 240g butter · 36g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Soak split peas for 30 minutes then boil until tender for about 40 minutes. Cook sauerkraut in a separate pot with a little water for 30 minutes. Fry chopped onion in butter on medium heat for 5 minutes until golden. Combine peas, sauerkraut and onion. Season with salt and pepper. Simmer together for 10 minutes to blend flavors. Serve warm.","cookTime":"60-70 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 15g · carbs 45g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Rinse sauerkraut if too sour before cooking.","pairsWith":"bread · mushrooms · potatoes","trivia":"This dish is traditional during Polish Christmas Eve.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-rosol","name":"Rosół","nameAlt":"Clear Chicken Soup","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"Sunday","ingredients":"200g chicken · 50g carrot · 50g celery · 50g onion · 800ml water · 3g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g chicken · 600g carrot · 600g celery · 600g onion · 9600ml water · 36g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Place chicken in a pot with water and bring to a gentle boil. Skim off foam that forms on the surface. Add chopped carrot, celery and onion. Simmer on very low heat for 90 minutes to develop flavor. Season with salt and pepper. Strain for a clear broth before serving. Serve hot as a comforting soup.","cookTime":"90-100 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 5g · fat 15g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 4 days.","chefNotes":"Slow simmering keeps the broth clear and rich.","pairsWith":"noodles · parsley · bread","trivia":"Rosół is traditionally served on Sundays in Polish homes.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-paczki","name":"Pączki","nameAlt":"Polish Doughnuts","aliases":["paczki"],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g flour · 100ml milk · 1 egg · 50g sugar · 30g butter · 5g yeast · 200ml oil · 50g jam","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1200ml milk · 12 eggs · 600g sugar · 360g butter · 60g yeast · 2400ml oil · 600g jam","method":"Activate yeast in warm milk for 10 minutes. Mix flour, egg, sugar and butter with yeast mixture into a dough. Knead until smooth and let rise for 60 minutes. Shape into balls and rest briefly. Fry in hot oil at medium heat for about 4 minutes per side until golden. Fill with jam and dust lightly if desired. Serve warm.","cookTime":"70-80 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 55g · fat 20g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but keeps 1 day.","chefNotes":"Do not overcrowd the oil when frying.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · milk","trivia":"Pączki are especially popular on Fat Thursday in Poland.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-mazurek","name":"Mazurek","nameAlt":"Polish Easter Cake","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"Easter","ingredients":"200g flour · 100g butter · 80g sugar · 1 egg · 100g jam · 50g nuts","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1200g butter · 960g sugar · 12 eggs · 1200g jam · 600g nuts","method":"Mix flour, butter, sugar and egg into a dough. Press into a baking tin evenly. Bake at 180°C for 20 minutes until lightly golden. Spread jam over the cooled base. Decorate with nuts on top. Return to oven for 10 minutes to set. Cool completely before slicing. Serve as a festive dessert.","cookTime":"30-35 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 50g · fat 28g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 4 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overbake the base to keep it tender.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · dried fruit","trivia":"Mazurek is traditionally decorated elaborately for Easter.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-kasza-gryczana","name":"Kasza gryczana","nameAlt":"Buckwheat Groats","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"grain","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g buckwheat groats · 300ml water · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1200g buckwheat groats · 3600ml water · 36g salt","method":"Rinse buckwheat groats under cold water. Bring water to a boil with salt. Add groats and reduce heat to low. Cook covered for about 15 minutes until water is absorbed. Fluff with a fork before serving. Serve warm as a side dish. Ensure grains remain separate.","cookTime":"15-20 min","kcal":180,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 35g · fat 2g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not stir too much to avoid mushy texture.","pairsWith":"mushrooms · vegetables · meat","trivia":"Buckwheat is widely used in Polish traditional cooking.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-ogorki-kiszone","name":"Ogórki kiszone","nameAlt":"Fermented Pickled Cucumbers","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"pickle","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g cucumbers · 500ml water · 10g salt · 5g garlic · 5g dill","ingredients12":"2400g cucumbers · 6000ml water · 120g salt · 60g garlic · 60g dill","method":"Dissolve salt in water to make a brine. Place cucumbers, garlic and dill in a jar. Pour brine over to fully cover. Leave at room temperature for 24 hours to start fermentation. Transfer to a cool place and ferment further. Taste after a few days for desired sourness. Serve chilled as a side.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":40,"nutrition":"protein 2g · carbs 8g · fat 0g","storage":"Store refrigerated after fermentation for several weeks.","chefNotes":"Fermenting for several days deepens the flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · meat · potatoes","trivia":"Fermented cucumbers are a staple in Polish cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"poland-salatka-jarzynowa","name":"Sałatka jarzynowa","nameAlt":"Vegetable Salad with Mayonnaise","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"salad","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Poland","occasion":"holiday","ingredients":"100g potatoes · 50g carrot · 50g peas · 1 egg · 50g mayonnaise · 30g pickles · 3g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1200g potatoes · 600g carrot · 600g peas · 12 eggs · 600g mayonnaise · 360g pickles · 36g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Boil potatoes and carrot until tender, about 20 minutes, then cool. Boil egg for 8 minutes and peel. Dice vegetables and egg into small pieces. Combine with peas and chopped pickles. Mix in mayonnaise thoroughly. Season with salt and pepper. Chill before serving for best flavor.","cookTime":"30-35 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 30g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Dice ingredients evenly for better texture.","pairsWith":"bread · ham · cheese","trivia":"This salad is a staple at Polish celebrations.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-borshch","name":"Борщ","nameAlt":"Beetroot Soup","aliases":["Borscht","Borsch"],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g beetroot · 80g cabbage · 60g potato · 50g carrot · 50g onion · 100g beef · 10g tomato paste · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g garlic · 5g dill · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g beetroot · 960g cabbage · 720g potato · 600g carrot · 600g onion · 1200g beef · 120g tomato paste · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g garlic · 60g dill · 60g salt","method":"Heat oil in a pot on medium and sauté chopped onion and carrot for about 5 minutes. Add diced beef and cook until browned for about 6 minutes. Stir in grated beetroot and tomato paste and cook for 5 minutes. Add chopped cabbage and potato and pour in water to cover. Bring to a boil then simmer on low heat for 30 minutes. Add minced garlic and salt and cook for another 5 minutes. Turn off heat and stir in chopped dill. Let the soup rest for 10 minutes before serving.","cookTime":"50-60 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 28g · fat 12g","storage":"Store in the fridge for up to 3 days in a sealed container.","chefNotes":"The flavor improves the next day after resting overnight.","pairsWith":"sour cream · rye bread · garlic bread","trivia":"Borshch is considered a national symbol of Ukrainian cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-varenyky","name":"Вареники","nameAlt":"Stuffed Dumplings","aliases":["Pierogi Ukrainian"],"course":"main","type":"dumpling","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"150g flour · 80ml water · 1 egg · 100g potato · 50g onion · 10g butter · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 960ml water · 12 eggs · 1200g potato · 600g onion · 120g butter · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour, egg, water, and salt into a soft dough and knead for 8 minutes. Let the dough rest for 20 minutes. Boil potatoes until tender for about 15 minutes and mash them. Fry chopped onion in butter on medium heat for 5 minutes and mix into potatoes. Roll out dough and cut circles then fill with potato mixture. Seal edges firmly and boil dumplings in salted water for 5 minutes until they float. Remove and toss lightly with butter. Serve warm.","cookTime":"40-50 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 65g · fat 10g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 2 days and reheat gently.","chefNotes":"Seal edges well to prevent filling from leaking during boiling.","pairsWith":"sour cream · fried onions · dill","trivia":"Varenyky are a staple at Ukrainian celebrations.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-holubtsi","name":"Голубці","nameAlt":"Stuffed Cabbage Rolls","aliases":["Holubtsy"],"course":"main","type":"stuffed","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"family","ingredients":"120g cabbage · 100g minced pork · 50g rice · 50g onion · 20g tomato paste · 10ml oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1440g cabbage · 1200g minced pork · 600g rice · 600g onion · 240g tomato paste · 120ml oil · 60g salt","method":"Boil cabbage leaves in water for 5 minutes to soften. Cook rice in boiling water for 10 minutes until half done. Fry chopped onion in oil on medium heat for 5 minutes. Mix rice, minced pork, onion, and salt. Place filling in cabbage leaves and roll tightly. Arrange rolls in a pot and spread tomato paste over them. Add water to cover and simmer on low heat for 40 minutes. Let rest for 10 minutes before serving.","cookTime":"60-70 min","kcal":390,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 35g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days in a sealed container.","chefNotes":"Use slightly undercooked rice to avoid mushy texture.","pairsWith":"sour cream · rye bread · pickles","trivia":"Holubtsi are common at Ukrainian weddings and holidays.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-deruny","name":"Деруни","nameAlt":"Potato Pancakes","aliases":["Draniki"],"course":"side","type":"pancake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g potato · 30g onion · 1 egg · 20g flour · 20ml oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g potato · 360g onion · 12 eggs · 240g flour · 240ml oil · 60g salt","method":"Grate potatoes and onion finely and squeeze out excess liquid. Mix with egg, flour, and salt until combined. Heat oil in a pan on medium heat. Spoon batter into the pan and flatten slightly. Fry each side until golden brown for about 4 minutes per side. Remove and drain on paper towels. Serve immediately while hot. Optionally add a dollop of sour cream.","cookTime":"20-25 min","kcal":310,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 40g · fat 12g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Squeeze moisture well for crispier pancakes.","pairsWith":"sour cream · applesauce · dill","trivia":"Deruny are especially popular in western Ukraine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-salo","name":"Сало","nameAlt":"Cured Pork Fat","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"cured","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"100g pork fat · 10g salt · 5g garlic · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1200g pork fat · 120g salt · 60g garlic · 24g black pepper","method":"Rub pork fat thoroughly with salt, minced garlic, and pepper. Place in a container and cover tightly. Store in the fridge for 2 days to cure. Slice thinly before serving. Serve chilled or at room temperature. Optionally add extra garlic on top. Enjoy with bread. This dish requires no cooking.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":800,"nutrition":"protein 2g · carbs 0g · fat 88g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Let cure overnight for best flavor development.","pairsWith":"rye bread · pickles · vodka","trivia":"Salo is a beloved traditional Ukrainian delicacy.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-kholodets","name":"Холодець","nameAlt":"Meat Aspic","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"aspic","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"holiday","ingredients":"200g pork knuckle · 50g carrot · 30g onion · 5g garlic · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g pork knuckle · 600g carrot · 360g onion · 60g garlic · 60g salt","method":"Place pork knuckle in a pot and cover with water. Bring to a boil and simmer on low heat for 2 hours. Add carrot and onion and cook for another 1 hour. Add garlic and salt in the final 10 minutes. Remove meat and shred it finely. Pour broth over the meat in a dish. Let cool and refrigerate until set for several hours. Serve chilled.","cookTime":"180 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 5g · fat 25g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and consume within 3 days.","chefNotes":"Skim impurities during cooking for a clear broth.","pairsWith":"mustard · horseradish · bread","trivia":"Kholodets is a staple at festive Ukrainian tables.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-pampushky","name":"Пампушки","nameAlt":"Garlic Bread Rolls","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g flour · 80ml milk · 5g yeast · 10g sugar · 20ml oil · 5g garlic · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 960ml milk · 60g yeast · 120g sugar · 240ml oil · 60g garlic · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour, yeast, milk, sugar, and salt into a dough and knead for 10 minutes. Let it rise in a warm place for 1 hour. Shape into small balls and place on a tray. Bake at 180°C for 20 minutes until golden. Mix oil and minced garlic together. Brush garlic oil over hot rolls. Let cool slightly before serving. Serve warm.","cookTime":"90-100 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 35g · fat 9g","storage":"Store in a sealed container for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Brush garlic oil immediately after baking for best absorption.","pairsWith":"borshch · butter · herbs","trivia":"Pampushky are often served with borshch.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-kutia","name":"Кутя","nameAlt":"Sweet Wheat Porridge","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"porridge","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"100g wheat berries · 20g honey · 20g poppy seeds · 30g walnuts · 20g raisins","ingredients12":"1200g wheat berries · 240g honey · 240g poppy seeds · 360g walnuts · 240g raisins","method":"Soak wheat berries overnight in water. Boil them until tender for about 40 minutes. Grind poppy seeds lightly. Mix cooked wheat with honey, poppy seeds, walnuts, and raisins. Stir well until combined. Let sit for 10 minutes to absorb flavors. Serve at room temperature. This dish requires no further cooking.","cookTime":"50-60 min","kcal":330,"nutrition":"protein 9g · carbs 55g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Soaking wheat overnight improves texture significantly.","pairsWith":"tea · dried fruit · nuts","trivia":"Kutia is traditionally eaten on Christmas Eve in Ukraine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-syrnyky","name":"Сирники","nameAlt":"Cottage Cheese Pancakes","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pancake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"breakfast","ingredients":"150g cottage cheese · 1 egg · 30g flour · 20g sugar · 20ml oil","ingredients12":"1800g cottage cheese · 12 eggs · 360g flour · 240g sugar · 240ml oil","method":"Mix cottage cheese, egg, flour, and sugar into a thick batter. Shape into small patties. Heat oil in a pan on medium heat. Fry patties until golden on both sides for about 4 minutes per side. Remove and drain excess oil. Serve warm. Optionally add toppings like sour cream or jam.","cookTime":"15-20 min","kcal":290,"nutrition":"protein 14g · carbs 25g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use dry cottage cheese to avoid soggy batter.","pairsWith":"jam · sour cream · honey","trivia":"Syrnyky are a popular Ukrainian breakfast dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-kapusniak","name":"Капусняк","nameAlt":"Sauerkraut Soup","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g sauerkraut · 100g pork · 50g potato · 50g carrot · 30g onion · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g sauerkraut · 1200g pork · 600g potato · 600g carrot · 360g onion · 60g salt","method":"Cook pork in water on low heat for 30 minutes. Add chopped carrot and onion and cook for 10 minutes. Add sauerkraut and diced potato. Simmer for another 30 minutes until vegetables are tender. Season with salt. Let rest for 10 minutes. Serve hot. Stir before serving.","cookTime":"70-80 min","kcal":340,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 20g · fat 18g","storage":"Store in the fridge for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Rinse sauerkraut lightly if too sour.","pairsWith":"bread · sour cream · herbs","trivia":"Kapusniak has been eaten in Ukraine for centuries.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-uzvar","name":"Узвар","nameAlt":"Dried Fruit Drink","aliases":[],"course":"drink","type":"beverage","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"30g dried apples · 20g dried pears · 20g prunes · 10g honey · 300ml water","ingredients12":"360g dried apples · 240g dried pears · 240g prunes · 120g honey · 3600ml water","method":"Bring water to a boil in a pot. Add dried fruits and simmer on low heat for 20 minutes. Turn off heat and let steep for 15 minutes. Add honey and stir until dissolved. Strain if desired. Serve warm or chilled. This drink requires minimal cooking.","cookTime":"30-35 min","kcal":120,"nutrition":"protein 1g · carbs 30g · fat 0g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let it steep longer for deeper flavor.","pairsWith":"desserts · pastries · nuts","trivia":"Uzvar is traditionally served at Christmas Eve dinner.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-nalysnyky","name":"Налисники","nameAlt":"Thin Crepes with Filling","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"crepe","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g flour · 150ml milk · 1 egg · 20g sugar · 100g cottage cheese · 10ml oil","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 1800ml milk · 12 eggs · 240g sugar · 1200g cottage cheese · 120ml oil","method":"Mix flour, milk, egg, and sugar into a smooth batter. Heat a pan on medium and lightly oil it. Pour a thin layer and cook crepes for about 2 minutes per side. Mix cottage cheese with a little sugar. Place filling on each crepe and roll tightly. Arrange in a dish and warm at 160°C for 10 minutes. Serve warm. Optionally add sour cream.","cookTime":"30-40 min","kcal":360,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 45g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Keep crepes thin for best texture.","pairsWith":"sour cream · jam · honey","trivia":"Nalysnyky are popular during Ukrainian celebrations.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-banosh","name":"Банош","nameAlt":"Creamy Cornmeal with Cheese and Pork","aliases":["Banush"],"course":"main","type":"porridge","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"80g cornmeal · 150ml cream · 50g bryndza cheese · 50g pork belly · 5g salt","ingredients12":"960g cornmeal · 1800ml cream · 600g bryndza cheese · 600g pork belly · 60g salt","method":"Bring cream to a gentle simmer on low heat. Slowly add cornmeal while stirring constantly. Cook while stirring for about 10 minutes until thick and smooth. Fry diced pork belly on medium heat until crispy for about 8 minutes. Spoon cornmeal into a bowl and top with cheese and pork. Sprinkle with salt if needed. Serve immediately while hot.","cookTime":"20-25 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 16g · carbs 35g · fat 35g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Stir constantly to prevent lumps forming.","pairsWith":"pickles · sour cream · herbs","trivia":"Banosh originates from the Carpathian mountain region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-kruchenyky","name":"Крученики","nameAlt":"Stuffed Meat Rolls","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"rolled","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"family","ingredients":"150g pork · 50g mushrooms · 30g onion · 20g breadcrumbs · 20ml oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g pork · 600g mushrooms · 360g onion · 240g breadcrumbs · 240ml oil · 60g salt","method":"Slice pork thinly and flatten with a mallet. Chop mushrooms and onion finely. Fry mushrooms and onion in oil on medium heat for 6 minutes. Mix with breadcrumbs and salt. Place filling on pork slices and roll tightly. Secure with toothpicks and brown in a pan for 5 minutes. Add a little water and simmer on low heat for 30 minutes. Remove picks and serve hot.","cookTime":"45-55 min","kcal":410,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 12g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Secure rolls tightly to keep filling inside.","pairsWith":"mashed potatoes · gravy · pickles","trivia":"Kruchenyky are often served at festive gatherings.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-zrazy","name":"Зрази","nameAlt":"Stuffed Meat Patties","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"patty","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g minced beef · 50g onion · 1 egg · 30g breadcrumbs · 20ml oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g minced beef · 600g onion · 12 eggs · 360g breadcrumbs · 240ml oil · 60g salt","method":"Mix minced beef with egg, breadcrumbs, and salt. Chop onion finely and sauté in oil for 5 minutes. Form meat mixture into patties and place onion filling inside. Seal and shape into ovals. Fry in oil on medium heat for about 5 minutes per side. Reduce heat and cook for another 10 minutes. Serve hot. Let rest briefly before serving.","cookTime":"25-30 min","kcal":430,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 15g · fat 30g","storage":"Store in fridge for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Keep patties sealed to prevent filling from leaking.","pairsWith":"potatoes · sour cream · salad","trivia":"Zrazy have roots in noble Eastern European cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-kasha","name":"Каша","nameAlt":"Buckwheat Porridge","aliases":["Grechka"],"course":"side","type":"porridge","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g buckwheat · 200ml water · 10ml oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g buckwheat · 2400ml water · 120ml oil · 60g salt","method":"Rinse buckwheat under cold water. Bring water to a boil in a pot. Add buckwheat and salt and reduce heat to low. Cover and simmer for 15 minutes until water is absorbed. Turn off heat and let sit for 5 minutes. Fluff with a fork and add oil. Serve warm. Stir before serving.","cookTime":"20-25 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 40g · fat 4g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not stir while cooking to keep grains fluffy.","pairsWith":"vegetables · meat · mushrooms","trivia":"Buckwheat is a staple grain in Ukrainian cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-paska","name":"Паска","nameAlt":"Easter Bread","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"bread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"Easter","ingredients":"200g flour · 100ml milk · 50g sugar · 1 egg · 50g butter · 5g yeast · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1200ml milk · 600g sugar · 12 eggs · 600g butter · 60g yeast · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour, yeast, warm milk, sugar, and egg into a dough. Knead for 10 minutes until smooth. Add butter and knead again. Let rise in a warm place for 1 hour. Shape into a round loaf and place in a tin. Bake at 180°C for 35 minutes until golden. Let cool before slicing. Serve at room temperature.","cookTime":"100-110 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 55g · fat 15g","storage":"Store in a sealed container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Decorate the top before baking for a traditional look.","pairsWith":"tea · jam · butter","trivia":"Paska is blessed in church during Easter celebrations.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-varenukha","name":"Варенуха","nameAlt":"Spiced Fruit Drink","aliases":[],"course":"drink","type":"beverage","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"50g dried apples · 20g raisins · 10g honey · 300ml water · 2g cinnamon","ingredients12":"600g dried apples · 240g raisins · 120g honey · 3600ml water · 24g cinnamon","method":"Bring water to a boil in a pot. Add dried apples and raisins and simmer for 20 minutes. Add cinnamon and continue cooking for 5 minutes. Remove from heat and stir in honey. Let steep for 10 minutes. Strain if desired. Serve warm. This drink is aromatic and comforting.","cookTime":"30-35 min","kcal":140,"nutrition":"protein 1g · carbs 35g · fat 0g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Adjust honey to taste for sweetness.","pairsWith":"desserts · pastries · nuts","trivia":"Varenukha dates back to Cossack traditions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-olivye","name":"Олів'є","nameAlt":"Potato Salad with Mayonnaise","aliases":["Russian Salad"],"course":"side","type":"salad","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"holiday","ingredients":"100g potato · 50g carrot · 50g peas · 50g cooked chicken · 30g mayonnaise · 1 egg · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g potato · 600g carrot · 600g peas · 600g cooked chicken · 360g mayonnaise · 12 eggs · 60g salt","method":"Boil potatoes and carrots until tender for about 20 minutes. Boil egg for 10 minutes and cool. Dice vegetables, egg, and chicken into small cubes. Combine in a bowl with peas. Add mayonnaise and salt and mix well. Chill in the fridge for 30 minutes before serving. Stir before serving. Serve cold.","cookTime":"30-35 min","kcal":360,"nutrition":"protein 15g · carbs 30g · fat 20g","storage":"Keep refrigerated and consume within 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use chilled ingredients for best texture.","pairsWith":"bread · pickles · meat","trivia":"Olivye salad is a must-have at New Year celebrations.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-kyiv-cake","name":"Київський торт","nameAlt":"Kyiv Meringue Cake","aliases":["Kyiv Cake"],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"3 egg whites · 80g sugar · 50g hazelnuts · 50g butter · 50g condensed milk","ingredients12":"36 egg whites · 960g sugar · 600g hazelnuts · 600g butter · 600g condensed milk","method":"Whisk egg whites with sugar until stiff peaks form. Fold in chopped hazelnuts gently. Spread mixture into layers and bake at 150°C for 1 hour until dry. Beat butter with condensed milk to make cream. Layer baked meringue with cream. Chill in the fridge for 2 hours. Slice and serve. Keep refrigerated until serving.","cookTime":"120-130 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 40g · fat 32g","storage":"Store in fridge for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Bake at low temperature to keep meringue crisp.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · berries","trivia":"Kyiv Cake is one of Ukraine’s most famous desserts.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-hrechanyky","name":"Гречаники","nameAlt":"Buckwheat Meat Patties","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"patty","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g buckwheat · 100g minced pork · 30g onion · 1 egg · 20ml oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g buckwheat · 1200g minced pork · 360g onion · 12 eggs · 240ml oil · 60g salt","method":"Cook buckwheat in water for 15 minutes until soft. Fry chopped onion in oil on medium heat for 5 minutes. Mix buckwheat with minced pork, onion, egg, and salt. Shape into patties. Fry in oil for about 5 minutes per side until golden. Reduce heat and cook for another 10 minutes. Serve hot. Let rest briefly before serving.","cookTime":"30-35 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 30g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Mix well to bind patties properly.","pairsWith":"sour cream · vegetables · salad","trivia":"Hrechanyky combine two Ukrainian staples: pork and buckwheat.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"ukraine-plachynda","name":"Плацинда","nameAlt":"Stuffed Flatbread","aliases":["Placinda"],"course":"main","type":"flatbread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Ukraine","occasion":"traditional","ingredients":"150g flour · 80ml water · 100g potato · 50g onion · 20ml oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 960ml water · 1200g potato · 600g onion · 240ml oil · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour, water, and salt into a dough and knead for 8 minutes. Let rest for 20 minutes. Boil potatoes until tender for 15 minutes and mash them. Fry chopped onion in oil for 5 minutes and mix into potatoes. Roll dough thin and add filling. Fold and seal into flat rounds. Fry in a pan on medium heat for about 4 minutes per side until golden. Serve warm.","cookTime":"40-50 min","kcal":370,"nutrition":"protein 9g · carbs 55g · fat 12g","storage":"Store in fridge for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Roll dough thin for better texture.","pairsWith":"sour cream · herbs · tea","trivia":"Plachynda is popular in southern Ukraine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-borscht","name":"Борщ","nameAlt":"Beetroot Soup","aliases":["Borsch","Borshch"],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g beef · 100g beetroot · 80g cabbage · 50g potato · 30g carrot · 30g onion · 10g tomato paste · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g garlic · 5g salt · 2g black pepper · 5g dill · 10g sour cream · 500ml water","ingredients12":"1800g beef · 1200g beetroot · 960g cabbage · 600g potato · 360g carrot · 360g onion · 120g tomato paste · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g garlic · 60g salt · 24g black pepper · 60g dill · 120g sour cream · 6000ml water","method":"Cut the beef into small chunks and simmer in water on low heat for about 40 minutes until tender. Peel and slice the beetroot and cook separately in a little oil on medium heat for about 10 minutes. Chop cabbage, potato, carrot, and onion into even pieces. Add potato and cabbage to the broth and cook for 15 minutes at a gentle boil. Fry onion and carrot in oil on medium until soft, about 6 minutes, then stir in tomato paste. Combine all vegetables and beetroot into the pot and simmer on low for another 20 minutes. Season with salt, pepper, and crushed garlic, then cook for 5 more minutes. Serve hot with chopped dill and a spoon of sour cream.","cookTime":"90 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 28g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days in a sealed container.","chefNotes":"Resting overnight deepens the flavor significantly.","pairsWith":"rye bread · sour cream · pickles","trivia":"Borscht varies widely across Eastern Europe but beetroot is always central.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-pelmeni","name":"Пельмени","nameAlt":"Meat Dumplings","aliases":["Pel'meni"],"course":"main","type":"dumpling","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g flour · 1 egg · 50ml water · 150g minced beef · 50g minced pork · 30g onion · 5g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 12 egg · 600ml water · 1800g minced beef · 600g minced pork · 360g onion · 60g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Mix flour, egg, and water to form a firm dough and knead for about 10 minutes. Let the dough rest for 20 minutes at room temperature. Finely chop onion and mix with minced meats, salt, and pepper. Roll the dough thin and cut into small circles. Place a small amount of filling in each circle and fold into dumplings. Bring salted water to a boil and cook dumplings for 6 to 8 minutes until they float. Stir occasionally to prevent sticking. Serve hot with butter or sour cream.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 40g · fat 18g","storage":"Freeze uncooked dumplings for up to 2 months.","chefNotes":"Do not overfill or they may burst during cooking.","pairsWith":"sour cream · vinegar · dill","trivia":"Pelmeni originated in Siberia as a convenient winter food.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-blini","name":"Блины","nameAlt":"Thin Pancakes","aliases":["Blintz","Blini"],"course":"dessert","type":"pancake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g flour · 1 egg · 200ml milk · 10g sugar · 5g salt · 10ml sunflower oil","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 12 egg · 2400ml milk · 120g sugar · 60g salt · 120ml sunflower oil","method":"Whisk flour, egg, milk, sugar, and salt into a smooth batter. Let the batter rest for 15 minutes at room temperature. Heat a lightly oiled pan over medium heat. Pour a thin layer of batter and swirl to cover the pan evenly. Cook for about 1 to 2 minutes until golden, then flip and cook another minute. Repeat with remaining batter. Stack pancakes and keep warm. Serve with sweet or savory fillings.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 30g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days wrapped well.","chefNotes":"Use a nonstick pan for best thin texture.","pairsWith":"honey · sour cream · jam","trivia":"Blini are traditionally served during Maslenitsa festival.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-beef-stroganoff","name":"Бефстроганов","nameAlt":"Beef Stroganoff","aliases":["Stroganov"],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g beef · 50g mushroom · 30g onion · 100ml sour cream · 10g flour · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"1800g beef · 600g mushroom · 360g onion · 1200ml sour cream · 120g flour · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Slice beef into thin strips and season with salt and pepper. Heat oil in a pan and sear beef on high heat for about 3 minutes. Remove and set aside. In the same pan cook sliced onion and mushrooms on medium heat for 8 minutes. Stir in flour and cook briefly for 1 minute. Add sour cream and mix until smooth. Return beef to the pan and simmer on low heat for 10 minutes. Stir gently and adjust seasoning. Serve hot.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 12g · fat 34g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not boil after adding sour cream to prevent curdling.","pairsWith":"rice · pasta · potatoes","trivia":"Named after the Stroganov family of Russian nobility.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-olivier-salad","name":"Салат Оливье","nameAlt":"Russian Potato Salad","aliases":["Olivier Salad"],"course":"side","type":"salad","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g potato · 50g carrot · 50g peas · 1 egg · 50g cooked chicken · 50g mayonnaise · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g potato · 600g carrot · 600g peas · 12 egg · 600g cooked chicken · 600g mayonnaise · 60g salt","method":"Boil potato and carrot until tender, about 20 minutes, then cool. Cook the egg for 10 minutes in boiling water and cool. Dice potato, carrot, egg, and chicken into small cubes. Combine all ingredients in a bowl with peas. Add mayonnaise and salt and mix gently. Chill for at least 30 minutes before serving. Taste and adjust seasoning if needed. Serve cold as a side dish.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 28g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Chilling improves texture and flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · pickles · roast meat","trivia":"A staple dish on New Year's tables in Russia.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-shchi","name":"Щи","nameAlt":"Cabbage Soup","aliases":["Shchi soup"],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g cabbage · 100g beef · 50g potato · 30g carrot · 30g onion · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt · 2g black pepper · 500ml water","ingredients12":"1800g cabbage · 1200g beef · 600g potato · 360g carrot · 360g onion · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt · 24g black pepper · 6000ml water","method":"Cut beef into pieces and simmer in water on low heat for 40 minutes. Chop cabbage, potato, carrot, and onion. Add potato and cabbage to the broth and cook for 15 minutes. Fry onion and carrot in oil on medium heat for about 6 minutes. Add fried vegetables to the soup and stir. Season with salt and pepper. Simmer for another 15 minutes on low heat. Serve hot.","cookTime":"80 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 20g · fat 12g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Sour cabbage can be used for a tangy version.","pairsWith":"rye bread · sour cream · garlic","trivia":"Shchi has been a staple of Russian cuisine for centuries.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-kvass","name":"Квас","nameAlt":"Fermented Bread Drink","aliases":["Kvass"],"course":"drink","type":"fermented","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g rye bread · 10g sugar · 2g yeast · 500ml water","ingredients12":"1200g rye bread · 120g sugar · 24g yeast · 6000ml water","method":"Toast rye bread until dark and crisp at 180°C for about 10 minutes. Place bread in warm water and let steep for 2 hours. Strain the liquid into a clean container. Add sugar and yeast and stir well. Cover loosely and ferment at room temperature for about 24 hours. Strain again and chill in the refrigerator. Serve cold.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":90,"nutrition":"protein 2g · carbs 18g · fat 0g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Fermentation time can vary depending on temperature.","pairsWith":"bread · soup · pickles","trivia":"Kvass has very low alcohol content despite fermentation.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-syrniki","name":"Сырники","nameAlt":"Cheese Pancakes","aliases":["Tvorozhniki"],"course":"dessert","type":"pancake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"breakfast","ingredients":"150g cottage cheese · 50g flour · 1 egg · 10g sugar · 10ml sunflower oil","ingredients12":"1800g cottage cheese · 600g flour · 12 egg · 120g sugar · 120ml sunflower oil","method":"Mix cottage cheese, egg, sugar, and flour into a soft dough. Form small patties with your hands. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat. Fry patties for about 4 minutes on each side until golden. Adjust heat to avoid burning. Remove and drain excess oil. Serve warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 22g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use dry cottage cheese for best texture.","pairsWith":"sour cream · jam · honey","trivia":"Syrniki are popular for breakfast across Russia.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-kholodets","name":"Холодец","nameAlt":"Meat Aspic","aliases":["Kholodets"],"course":"starter","type":"aspic","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g pork · 100g beef · 50g carrot · 30g onion · 5g garlic · 5g salt · 2g black pepper · 500ml water","ingredients12":"2400g pork · 1200g beef · 600g carrot · 360g onion · 60g garlic · 60g salt · 24g black pepper · 6000ml water","method":"Simmer pork and beef in water on low heat for 3 hours until very tender. Skim any foam that rises. Add carrot and onion and cook for another 30 minutes. Remove meat and shred into pieces. Strain the broth and season with salt, pepper, and garlic. Place meat into molds and pour over broth. Chill in the refrigerator until set, about overnight. Serve cold.","cookTime":"210 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 6g · fat 24g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Natural gelatin from bones helps it set without additives.","pairsWith":"mustard · horseradish · bread","trivia":"Kholodets is a traditional New Year dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-rasstegai","name":"Расстегай","nameAlt":"Open Fish Pie","aliases":["Rasstegai"],"course":"main","type":"pie","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"120g flour · 1 egg · 50ml milk · 100g fish · 30g onion · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 12 egg · 600ml milk · 1200g fish · 360g onion · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt","method":"Prepare dough by mixing flour, egg, and milk and knead until smooth. Let rest for 20 minutes. Cook fish and onion in oil on medium heat for 8 minutes. Roll dough and cut into circles. Fill with fish mixture and shape with an open top. Place on a tray and bake at 180°C for 25 minutes. Allow to cool slightly before serving. Serve warm.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 38g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Brush with egg wash for a golden crust.","pairsWith":"broth · tea · salad","trivia":"The opening in the pie lets broth be added before serving.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-vinegret","name":"Винегрет","nameAlt":"Beetroot Salad","aliases":["Vinegret salad"],"course":"side","type":"salad","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g beetroot · 50g potato · 50g carrot · 50g pickled cucumber · 30g onion · 20ml sunflower oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g beetroot · 600g potato · 600g carrot · 600g pickled cucumber · 360g onion · 240ml sunflower oil · 60g salt","method":"Boil beetroot, potato, and carrot until tender, about 25 minutes. Let cool completely. Dice all vegetables into small cubes. Add chopped pickled cucumber and onion. Mix everything in a bowl. Add oil and salt and toss gently. Chill before serving for 20 minutes. Serve cold.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":180,"nutrition":"protein 4g · carbs 26g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use uniform cuts for better texture.","pairsWith":"bread · pickles · fish","trivia":"The name comes from French vinaigrette but the dish is distinctly Russian.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-ukha","name":"Уха","nameAlt":"Fish Soup","aliases":["Ukha soup"],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g fish · 50g potato · 30g carrot · 30g onion · 5g salt · 2g black pepper · 500ml water","ingredients12":"1800g fish · 600g potato · 360g carrot · 360g onion · 60g salt · 24g black pepper · 6000ml water","method":"Cut fish into chunks and place in water. Bring to a gentle boil and cook for 15 minutes. Add chopped potato, carrot, and onion. Simmer on low heat for another 20 minutes. Skim foam if needed. Season with salt and pepper. Cook until vegetables are tender. Serve hot.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 24g · carbs 18g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Fresh fish gives the best flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · lemon · herbs","trivia":"Ukha is traditionally cooked outdoors by fishermen.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-vareniki","name":"Вареники","nameAlt":"Stuffed Dumplings","aliases":["Varenyky"],"course":"main","type":"dumpling","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g flour · 1 egg · 50ml water · 150g potato · 50g onion · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 12 egg · 600ml water · 1800g potato · 600g onion · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour, egg, and water into a dough and knead for 10 minutes. Let the dough rest for 20 minutes at room temperature. Boil potato until soft, about 20 minutes, then mash. Fry chopped onion in oil on medium heat for 6 minutes and mix into potato with salt. Roll dough thin and cut into circles. Fill with potato mixture and seal edges. Boil in salted water for 6 to 8 minutes until they float. Serve hot.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":360,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 55g · fat 10g","storage":"Freeze uncooked for up to 2 months.","chefNotes":"Seal edges tightly to prevent filling from leaking.","pairsWith":"sour cream · butter · dill","trivia":"Vareniki are often filled with sweet or savory fillings.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-okroshka","name":"Окрошка","nameAlt":"Cold Soup","aliases":["Okroshka soup"],"course":"starter","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"100g boiled potato · 50g cucumber · 50g cooked beef · 1 egg · 30g radish · 200ml kvass · 5g dill · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g boiled potato · 600g cucumber · 600g cooked beef · 12 egg · 360g radish · 2400ml kvass · 60g dill · 60g salt","method":"Dice boiled potato, cucumber, beef, egg, and radish into small pieces. Place all ingredients into a bowl. Pour chilled kvass over the mixture. Add chopped dill and salt. Stir gently to combine. Chill for 10 minutes before serving. Serve cold.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 14g · carbs 20g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 1 day.","chefNotes":"Keep kvass and solids separate until serving for freshness.","pairsWith":"bread · mustard · sour cream","trivia":"Okroshka is especially popular during hot Russian summers.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-kasha-buckwheat","name":"Гречневая каша","nameAlt":"Buckwheat Porridge","aliases":["Buckwheat kasha"],"course":"side","type":"porridge","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g buckwheat · 200ml water · 5g salt · 10ml sunflower oil","ingredients12":"1200g buckwheat · 2400ml water · 60g salt · 120ml sunflower oil","method":"Rinse buckwheat under cold water. Bring water to a boil and add salt. Stir in buckwheat and reduce heat to low. Cover and cook for about 15 minutes until water is absorbed. Turn off heat and let rest for 10 minutes. Fluff with a fork and add oil. Serve warm.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":190,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 32g · fat 5g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not stir during cooking for fluffy grains.","pairsWith":"meat · mushrooms · vegetables","trivia":"Buckwheat is a staple grain in Russian cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-ptichye-moloko","name":"Птичье молоко","nameAlt":"Souffle Cake","aliases":["Bird's Milk Cake"],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"100g sugar · 2 egg · 50g butter · 100ml milk · 10g gelatin · 50g flour","ingredients12":"1200g sugar · 24 egg · 600g butter · 1200ml milk · 120g gelatin · 600g flour","method":"Separate eggs and beat whites until stiff peaks form. Heat milk, sugar, and butter on low until dissolved. Dissolve gelatin in warm water and mix into milk mixture. Fold whipped egg whites into the mixture gently. Pour into a mold and chill until set, about several hours. Prepare a simple sponge base and place underneath. Chill again until firm. Slice and serve cold.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 50g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Allow proper chilling time for best structure.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee · berries","trivia":"The name means 'bird's milk', symbolizing rarity.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-pirozhki","name":"Пирожки","nameAlt":"Stuffed Buns","aliases":["Piroshki"],"course":"main","type":"bread","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g flour · 1 egg · 50ml milk · 100g minced beef · 30g onion · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 12 egg · 600ml milk · 1200g minced beef · 360g onion · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour, egg, and milk to form a dough and knead for 10 minutes. Let rest for 20 minutes. Cook minced beef with chopped onion on medium heat for 8 minutes. Roll dough into small portions and fill with meat. Shape into buns and seal well. Place on a tray and bake at 180°C for 25 minutes until golden. Cool slightly before serving. Serve warm.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":430,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 38g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Brush tops with egg wash for shine.","pairsWith":"tea · soup · salad","trivia":"Pirozhki are popular street food across Russia.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-solyanka","name":"Солянка","nameAlt":"Spicy Meat Soup","aliases":["Solyanka soup"],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g beef · 50g sausage · 50g pickled cucumber · 30g onion · 10g tomato paste · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt · 2g black pepper · 500ml water","ingredients12":"1200g beef · 600g sausage · 600g pickled cucumber · 360g onion · 120g tomato paste · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt · 24g black pepper · 6000ml water","method":"Cook beef in water on low heat for 40 minutes. Slice sausage and fry with onion on medium heat for 6 minutes. Add tomato paste and cook briefly for 2 minutes. Chop pickled cucumber and add to the pan. Combine everything into the broth. Simmer for 15 minutes on low heat. Season with salt and pepper. Serve hot.","cookTime":"70 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 24g · carbs 12g · fat 26g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"A slice of lemon is often added before serving.","pairsWith":"bread · sour cream · olives","trivia":"Solyanka is known for its rich and tangy flavor.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-medovik","name":"Медовик","nameAlt":"Honey Cake","aliases":["Medovik cake"],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"100g flour · 50g honey · 50g sugar · 1 egg · 50g butter · 100g sour cream","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 600g honey · 600g sugar · 12 egg · 600g butter · 1200g sour cream","method":"Heat honey, sugar, and butter gently until melted. Stir in egg and flour to form a dough. Divide into layers and roll thin. Bake each layer at 180°C for about 5 minutes until golden. Prepare cream with sour cream and sugar. Layer baked sheets with cream between each. Chill in the refrigerator for several hours. Slice and serve.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 55g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 4 days.","chefNotes":"Letting it rest overnight softens the layers.","pairsWith":"tea · berries · coffee","trivia":"Medovik is one of Russia’s most beloved cakes.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-golubtsy","name":"Голубцы","nameAlt":"Stuffed Cabbage Rolls","aliases":["Golubtsi"],"course":"main","type":"stuffed","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g cabbage · 100g minced beef · 50g rice · 30g onion · 10g tomato paste · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g cabbage · 1200g minced beef · 600g rice · 360g onion · 120g tomato paste · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt","method":"Boil cabbage leaves until soft, about 10 minutes. Cook rice until tender for 15 minutes. Mix rice with minced beef, chopped onion, and salt. Place filling into cabbage leaves and roll tightly. Arrange in a pot and cover with water and tomato paste. Simmer on low heat for 40 minutes. Check seasoning and serve hot. Serve warm.","cookTime":"70 min","kcal":360,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 30g · fat 16g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use large leaves for easier rolling.","pairsWith":"sour cream · bread · herbs","trivia":"Golubtsy are similar to cabbage rolls found across Eastern Europe.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-smetannik","name":"Сметанник","nameAlt":"Sour Cream Cake","aliases":["Smetana cake"],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"100g flour · 100g sour cream · 50g sugar · 1 egg · 5g baking powder","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 1200g sour cream · 600g sugar · 12 egg · 60g baking powder","method":"Mix flour, sugar, egg, sour cream, and baking powder into a smooth batter. Pour into a baking tin. Bake at 180°C for 30 minutes until set. Allow to cool completely. Slice and serve. Optionally add cream between layers. Serve at room temperature.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 45g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overmix to keep it light.","pairsWith":"tea · fruit · coffee","trivia":"Smetannik highlights the importance of sour cream in Russian desserts.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-pryaniki","name":"Пряники","nameAlt":"Spiced Honey Cookies","aliases":["Pryanik"],"course":"dessert","type":"cookie","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g flour · 50g honey · 30g sugar · 1 egg · 5g cinnamon · 5g baking powder","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 600g honey · 360g sugar · 12 egg · 60g cinnamon · 60g baking powder","method":"Mix honey, sugar, and egg until smooth. Add flour, cinnamon, and baking powder to form a dough. Roll dough and cut into shapes. Place on a tray and bake at 180°C for 15 minutes. Allow to cool before serving. Store in a dry place. Serve with tea.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 50g · fat 8g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Honey keeps them soft longer.","pairsWith":"tea · milk · jam","trivia":"Pryaniki have been made in Russia since medieval times.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"russia-mors","name":"Морс","nameAlt":"Berry Drink","aliases":["Mors drink"],"course":"drink","type":"juice","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Russia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g berries · 20g sugar · 300ml water","ingredients12":"1200g berries · 240g sugar · 3600ml water","method":"Crush berries and extract juice. Boil water and add sugar until dissolved. Combine berry juice with sweetened water. Stir well and cool. Chill before serving. Serve cold.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":120,"nutrition":"protein 1g · carbs 28g · fat 0g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use cranberries or lingonberries for authenticity.","pairsWith":"bread · pastries · desserts","trivia":"Mors is a traditional non-alcoholic fruit drink.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-gulyas","name":"Gulyás","nameAlt":"Beef and paprika soup","aliases":["Goulash"],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g beef chuck · 50g onion · 10g paprika · 5g garlic · 100g potato · 50g carrot · 5g caraway seeds · 500ml beef stock · 10ml sunflower oil · 3g salt","ingredients12":"2400g beef chuck · 600g onion · 120g paprika · 60g garlic · 1200g potato · 600g carrot · 60g caraway seeds · 6000ml beef stock · 120ml sunflower oil · 36g salt","method":"Heat oil in a pot over medium and sauté chopped onion until translucent, about 5 minutes. Add minced garlic and cook for 1 minute. Stir in paprika off the heat briefly to avoid burning, then return to heat. Add cubed beef and sear until browned, about 6 minutes. Pour in beef stock and add caraway seeds, then simmer gently for 60 minutes. Add diced potato and carrot and cook until tender, about 20 minutes. Season with salt and adjust consistency with water if needed. Serve hot.","cookTime":"90 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 35g · carbs 30g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate in a sealed container for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use Hungarian sweet paprika for authentic flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · sour cream · pickles","trivia":"Gulyás originated as a meal cooked by Hungarian shepherds.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-porkolt","name":"Pörkölt","nameAlt":"Paprika meat stew","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g pork shoulder · 60g onion · 10g paprika · 5g garlic · 200ml beef stock · 10ml sunflower oil · 3g salt","ingredients12":"2400g pork shoulder · 720g onion · 120g paprika · 60g garlic · 2400ml beef stock · 120ml sunflower oil · 36g salt","method":"Heat oil in a pot over medium and sauté chopped onion until golden, about 8 minutes. Add minced garlic and cook briefly. Stir in paprika off the heat, then add cubed pork. Brown the meat for about 6 minutes. Pour in stock and bring to a simmer. Cook covered on low heat for about 60 minutes until tender. Stir occasionally and add water if needed. Season with salt and serve thick and rich.","cookTime":"75 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 38g · carbs 8g · fat 45g","storage":"Store in the fridge for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Cook slowly to deepen the paprika flavor.","pairsWith":"nokedli · bread · pickles","trivia":"Pörkölt differs from gulyás by having less liquid.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-langos","name":"Lángos","nameAlt":"Fried flatbread","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"150g flour · 5g yeast · 100ml milk · 5g salt · 200ml sunflower oil · 30g sour cream · 20g cheese","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 60g yeast · 1200ml milk · 60g salt · 2400ml sunflower oil · 360g sour cream · 240g cheese","method":"Mix flour, yeast, warm milk, and salt into a dough and knead until smooth. Let rise in a warm place for about 60 minutes. Divide dough and flatten into rounds. Heat oil to 180°C and fry each piece until golden, about 3 minutes per side. Drain on paper towels. Spread with sour cream and sprinkle grated cheese. Serve immediately while hot.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":700,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 70g · fat 38g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Do not overcrowd the pan when frying.","pairsWith":"garlic · sour cream · cheese","trivia":"Lángos is a popular Hungarian street food.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-nokedli","name":"Nokedli","nameAlt":"Hungarian egg dumplings","aliases":["Galuska"],"course":"side","type":"dumpling","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g flour · 1 egg · 50ml water · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 12 egg · 600ml water · 36g salt","method":"Mix flour, egg, water, and salt into a sticky batter. Bring salted water to a boil at 100°C. Use a spoon or dumpling maker to drop small pieces into water. Cook until dumplings float, about 3 minutes. Remove with a slotted spoon. Toss lightly with oil or butter. Serve warm as a side.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 50g · fat 6g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Keep batter soft for tender dumplings.","pairsWith":"pörkölt · butter · herbs","trivia":"Nokedli is Hungary’s version of spaetzle.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-halaszle","name":"Halászlé","nameAlt":"Fisherman’s fish soup","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"soup","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g carp fish · 50g onion · 10g paprika · 500ml fish stock · 5g garlic · 3g salt","ingredients12":"2400g carp fish · 600g onion · 120g paprika · 6000ml fish stock · 60g garlic · 36g salt","method":"Sauté chopped onion in a pot over medium heat for 5 minutes. Add garlic and cook briefly. Stir in paprika off the heat. Add fish stock and bring to a boil. Add fish pieces and simmer gently for 20 minutes. Season with salt. Serve hot with bread.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 8g · fat 20g","storage":"Store refrigerated for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use fresh river fish for best taste.","pairsWith":"bread · chili · white wine","trivia":"Halászlé is traditionally made by river fishermen.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-toltott-kaposzta","name":"Töltött káposzta","nameAlt":"Stuffed cabbage rolls","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stuffed","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"150g cabbage leaves · 150g pork mince · 50g rice · 50g onion · 10g paprika · 300ml tomato juice · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1800g cabbage leaves · 1800g pork mince · 600g rice · 600g onion · 120g paprika · 3600ml tomato juice · 36g salt","method":"Boil cabbage leaves until soft, about 10 minutes. Mix pork mince with cooked rice, chopped onion, paprika, and salt. Place filling into leaves and roll tightly. Arrange in a pot and cover with tomato juice. Simmer on low heat for 90 minutes. Ensure rolls are tender and cooked through. Serve hot with sour cream.","cookTime":"110 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 32g · carbs 40g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let it rest overnight for deeper flavor.","pairsWith":"sour cream · bread · pickles","trivia":"This dish is a staple at Hungarian Christmas meals.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-rakott-krumpli","name":"Rakott krumpli","nameAlt":"Layered potato casserole","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"casserole","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g potato · 1 egg · 50g sausage · 50g sour cream · 5g paprika · 3g salt","ingredients12":"2400g potato · 12 egg · 600g sausage · 600g sour cream · 60g paprika · 36g salt","method":"Boil potatoes until tender, about 20 minutes, then slice. Hard boil eggs and slice. Layer potatoes, eggs, and sausage in a baking dish. Spread sour cream between layers and sprinkle paprika. Bake at 180°C for 40 minutes until golden. Let rest slightly before serving.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 50g · fat 35g","storage":"Store refrigerated for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use smoked sausage for deeper flavor.","pairsWith":"salad · pickles · bread","trivia":"Rakott krumpli is a beloved Hungarian comfort food.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-dobos-torta","name":"Dobos torta","nameAlt":"Layered sponge cake with caramel","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"celebration","ingredients":"100g flour · 100g sugar · 3 egg · 100g butter · 50g chocolate · 20g caramel","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 1200g sugar · 36 egg · 1200g butter · 600g chocolate · 240g caramel","method":"Whisk eggs and sugar until fluffy. Fold in flour and bake thin layers at 180°C for 8 minutes each. Prepare chocolate buttercream by mixing butter and melted chocolate. Layer sponge with buttercream. Top with caramel layer hardened until crisp. Slice carefully and serve.","cookTime":"60 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 45g · fat 28g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Cut caramel topping before it fully hardens.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea · cream","trivia":"Dobos torta was created in the 19th century.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-kurtoskalacs","name":"Kürtőskalács","nameAlt":"Chimney cake","aliases":["Chimney cake"],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"150g flour · 50g sugar · 5g yeast · 100ml milk · 30g butter · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 600g sugar · 60g yeast · 1200ml milk · 360g butter · 36g salt","method":"Mix flour, yeast, milk, sugar, butter, and salt into a dough. Let rise for 60 minutes. Roll into strips and wrap around a cylinder. Bake at 180°C for 20 minutes, turning occasionally. Brush with sugar while hot. Serve warm.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 60g · fat 15g","storage":"Best eaten fresh, store for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Rotate evenly for a uniform crust.","pairsWith":"cinnamon · nuts · chocolate","trivia":"Kürtőskalács is popular at markets and fairs.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-pogacsa","name":"Pogácsa","nameAlt":"Savory scones","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"150g flour · 50g butter · 50ml milk · 5g yeast · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 600g butter · 600ml milk · 60g yeast · 36g salt","method":"Mix flour, butter, milk, yeast, and salt into a dough. Knead until smooth and let rise for 45 minutes. Roll out and cut into small rounds. Bake at 180°C for 20 minutes until golden. Serve warm.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 35g · fat 18g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Brush tops with egg for shine.","pairsWith":"cheese · ham · tea","trivia":"Pogácsa is a traditional Hungarian snack.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-turos-csusza","name":"Túrós csusza","nameAlt":"Cottage cheese pasta","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"pasta","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g pasta · 100g cottage cheese · 50g sour cream · 20g butter · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1800g pasta · 1200g cottage cheese · 600g sour cream · 240g butter · 36g salt","method":"Cook pasta in salted boiling water for 10 minutes. Drain and mix with butter. Add cottage cheese and sour cream. Stir gently until combined. Heat briefly on low for 5 minutes. Serve warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 55g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Add crispy bacon if not vegetarian.","pairsWith":"salad · pickles · yogurt","trivia":"Túrós csusza is a simple comfort dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-lecso","name":"Lecsó","nameAlt":"Pepper and tomato stew","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"150g bell pepper · 100g tomato · 50g onion · 10g paprika · 10ml sunflower oil · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1800g bell pepper · 1200g tomato · 600g onion · 120g paprika · 120ml sunflower oil · 36g salt","method":"Heat oil in a pan over medium and sauté sliced onion for 5 minutes. Add chopped peppers and cook for 10 minutes. Stir in tomatoes and paprika. Simmer for 20 minutes until soft. Season with salt and serve warm.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 20g · fat 12g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use ripe tomatoes for best flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · eggs · sausage","trivia":"Lecsó is similar to French ratatouille.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-palacsinta","name":"Palacsinta","nameAlt":"Thin Hungarian pancakes","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pancake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g flour · 200ml milk · 1 egg · 10g sugar · 10ml sunflower oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 2400ml milk · 12 egg · 120g sugar · 120ml sunflower oil · 24g salt","method":"Whisk flour, milk, egg, sugar, oil, and salt into a smooth batter. Heat a pan over medium and lightly oil it. Pour a thin layer of batter and swirl to coat. Cook until edges lift, about 2 minutes, then flip and cook 1 minute more. Repeat with remaining batter. Fill with jam or sweet fillings and roll. Serve warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 35g · fat 9g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Let batter rest 10 minutes for smoother pancakes.","pairsWith":"jam · chocolate · fruit","trivia":"Palacsinta is thinner than American pancakes.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-hortobagyi-palacsinta","name":"Hortobágyi palacsinta","nameAlt":"Savory stuffed pancakes","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stuffed","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"2 pancake · 150g chicken · 50g onion · 10g paprika · 100ml sour cream · 5g garlic · 3g salt","ingredients12":"24 pancake · 1800g chicken · 600g onion · 120g paprika · 1200ml sour cream · 60g garlic · 36g salt","method":"Cook chopped onion in a pan over medium for 5 minutes. Add garlic and chicken pieces, cooking until browned, about 8 minutes. Stir in paprika and a little water, then simmer for 15 minutes. Fill pancakes with the mixture and roll. Place in a baking dish, cover with sour cream sauce, and bake at 180°C for 20 minutes. Serve hot.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 32g · carbs 30g · fat 32g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Blend sauce smooth for a refined finish.","pairsWith":"salad · pickles · paprika sauce","trivia":"Named after the Hortobágy region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-korozott","name":"Körözött","nameAlt":"Paprika cheese spread","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"spread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"150g cottage cheese · 30g butter · 10g paprika · 5g onion · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1800g cottage cheese · 360g butter · 120g paprika · 60g onion · 36g salt","method":"Mash cottage cheese and butter in a bowl until smooth. Finely chop onion and add to the mixture. Stir in paprika and salt. Mix thoroughly until well combined. Chill for 10 minutes before serving. Spread on bread or crackers.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 14g · carbs 6g · fat 22g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Add caraway seeds for extra flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · crackers · vegetables","trivia":"Körözött is popular as a beer snack.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-tojasleves","name":"Tojásleves","nameAlt":"Egg soup","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"soup","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"1 egg · 500ml vegetable stock · 10g paprika · 5g garlic · 5ml sunflower oil · 3g salt","ingredients12":"12 egg · 6000ml vegetable stock · 120g paprika · 60g garlic · 60ml sunflower oil · 36g salt","method":"Heat oil in a pot over medium and add minced garlic, cooking for 1 minute. Stir in paprika briefly off the heat. Pour in vegetable stock and bring to a simmer. Beat the egg and slowly pour into the soup while stirring. Cook for 3 minutes until egg strands form. Season with salt and serve hot.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":180,"nutrition":"protein 9g · carbs 5g · fat 12g","storage":"Store refrigerated for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Stir gently for fine egg ribbons.","pairsWith":"bread · herbs · pepper","trivia":"A simple Hungarian comfort soup.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-kapros-turos-lepeny","name":"Kapros túrós lepény","nameAlt":"Dill cottage cheese pie","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pie","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"120g flour · 100g cottage cheese · 30g sugar · 20g butter · 5g dill · 1 egg","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 1200g cottage cheese · 360g sugar · 240g butter · 60g dill · 12 egg","method":"Mix flour, butter, and egg into a dough and press into a baking dish. Combine cottage cheese, sugar, and chopped dill. Spread filling over dough evenly. Bake at 180°C for 35 minutes until set. Let cool slightly before slicing. Serve warm or at room temperature.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 14g · carbs 40g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Balance sweetness with fresh dill.","pairsWith":"tea · fruit · yogurt","trivia":"Combines sweet and savory flavors.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-krumplis-teszta","name":"Krumplis tészta","nameAlt":"Potato pasta","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"pasta","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g pasta · 150g potato · 50g onion · 10g paprika · 10ml sunflower oil · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1800g pasta · 1800g potato · 600g onion · 120g paprika · 120ml sunflower oil · 36g salt","method":"Boil potatoes until tender, about 20 minutes, then mash. Cook pasta in salted water for 10 minutes and drain. Sauté chopped onion in oil over medium for 5 minutes. Stir in paprika and mashed potatoes. Add pasta and mix thoroughly. Heat for 5 minutes and season with salt. Serve warm.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 70g · fat 16g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Fry lightly for crispy edges.","pairsWith":"pickles · salad · sour cream","trivia":"A budget-friendly traditional meal.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-meggyleves","name":"Meggyleves","nameAlt":"Sour cherry soup","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"soup","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"200g sour cherries · 300ml water · 30g sugar · 50ml sour cream · 5g cinnamon","ingredients12":"2400g sour cherries · 3600ml water · 360g sugar · 600ml sour cream · 60g cinnamon","method":"Bring water and cherries to a boil over medium heat. Add sugar and cinnamon and simmer for 15 minutes. Stir in sour cream and mix until smooth. Cook gently for 5 more minutes without boiling. Chill before serving. Serve cold.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 4g · carbs 35g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not boil after adding sour cream.","pairsWith":"pastry · cake · cream","trivia":"Often served cold in summer.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-turos-retes","name":"Túrós rétes","nameAlt":"Cottage cheese strudel","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g filo pastry · 150g cottage cheese · 30g sugar · 20g butter · 1 egg","ingredients12":"1200g filo pastry · 1800g cottage cheese · 360g sugar · 240g butter · 12 egg","method":"Mix cottage cheese, sugar, and egg into a filling. Lay out filo sheets and brush with melted butter. Spread filling evenly and roll tightly. Place on a baking tray and brush with butter. Bake at 180°C for 30 minutes until golden. Cool slightly and slice before serving.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 14g · carbs 40g · fat 18g","storage":"Store in a cool place for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Keep filo covered to prevent drying.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee · fruit","trivia":"Rétes is the Hungarian version of strudel.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-marhaporkolt","name":"Marhapörkölt","nameAlt":"Beef paprika stew","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g beef · 60g onion · 10g paprika · 5g garlic · 200ml beef stock · 10ml sunflower oil · 3g salt","ingredients12":"2400g beef · 720g onion · 120g paprika · 60g garlic · 2400ml beef stock · 120ml sunflower oil · 36g salt","method":"Heat oil in a pot and sauté chopped onion over medium for 8 minutes. Add garlic and cook briefly. Stir in paprika off heat. Add beef cubes and brown for 6 minutes. Pour in stock and simmer for 90 minutes until tender. Season with salt and serve thick.","cookTime":"100 min","kcal":580,"nutrition":"protein 40g · carbs 8g · fat 42g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Low heat ensures tender meat.","pairsWith":"nokedli · bread · pickles","trivia":"A classic Hungarian beef dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-zoldborsfozelek","name":"Zöldborsófőzelék","nameAlt":"Creamed pea stew","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"stew","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g green peas · 50ml milk · 10g flour · 20g butter · 5g garlic · 3g salt","ingredients12":"2400g green peas · 600ml milk · 120g flour · 240g butter · 60g garlic · 36g salt","method":"Melt butter in a pan over medium and sauté garlic for 1 minute. Stir in flour to form a roux. Gradually add milk while stirring to avoid lumps. Add peas and cook for 10 minutes until tender. Season with salt and serve warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 30g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Add a pinch of sugar to enhance sweetness.","pairsWith":"meat · eggs · bread","trivia":"Főzelék is a unique Hungarian vegetable dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-gyumolcsleves","name":"Gyümölcsleves","nameAlt":"Cold fruit soup","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"soup","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"200g mixed fruit · 300ml water · 30g sugar · 50ml cream · 5g cinnamon","ingredients12":"2400g mixed fruit · 3600ml water · 360g sugar · 600ml cream · 60g cinnamon","method":"Bring water and fruit to a boil over medium heat. Add sugar and cinnamon and simmer for 15 minutes. Stir in cream and mix well. Cool completely and chill before serving. Serve cold.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":240,"nutrition":"protein 3g · carbs 40g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use seasonal fruits for best taste.","pairsWith":"cake · pastry · cream","trivia":"Fruit soups are popular in Central Europe.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"hungary-rakott-teszta","name":"Rakott tészta","nameAlt":"Layered baked pasta","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"casserole","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Hungary","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g pasta · 100g pork mince · 50g onion · 100ml tomato juice · 20g cheese · 3g salt","ingredients12":"1800g pasta · 1200g pork mince · 600g onion · 1200ml tomato juice · 240g cheese · 36g salt","method":"Cook pasta in salted water for 10 minutes and drain. Sauté onion in a pan over medium for 5 minutes. Add pork mince and cook until browned, about 8 minutes. Stir in tomato juice and simmer for 10 minutes. Layer pasta and meat sauce in a baking dish and top with cheese. Bake at 180°C for 30 minutes until golden. Serve hot.","cookTime":"50 min","kcal":620,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 65g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let it rest before slicing for clean layers.","pairsWith":"salad · bread · pickles","trivia":"Layered pasta dishes are common in Hungarian home cooking.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-kebap-adana","name":"Adana Kebap","nameAlt":"Spicy minced lamb skewers","aliases":["Adana kebabı"],"course":"main","type":"kebab","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g lamb mince · 10g red pepper flakes · 5g salt · 2g black pepper · 10g butter · 50g flatbread","ingredients12":"2400g lamb mince · 120g red pepper flakes · 60g salt · 24g black pepper · 120g butter · 600g flatbread","method":"Mix the lamb mince with red pepper flakes, salt, and black pepper until evenly combined. Knead the mixture for a few minutes to develop a sticky texture. Shape onto flat metal skewers, pressing firmly. Preheat a grill to medium-high heat. Grill the kebabs, turning occasionally, for about 10 minutes until cooked through. Melt butter and brush over the kebabs in the final minute. Serve hot with flatbread. Rest briefly before serving to retain juices.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 20g · fat 35g","storage":"Store cooked kebabs in the fridge for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use lamb with some fat for best flavor and texture.","pairsWith":"ayran · grilled tomato · onion salad","trivia":"Adana Kebap originates from the southern city of Adana and is known for its heat.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-manti","name":"Mantı","nameAlt":"Turkish dumplings with yogurt sauce","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"dumpling","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"family","ingredients":"150g flour · 1 egg · 50ml water · 100g beef mince · 50g yogurt · 10g garlic · 10g butter · 5g paprika","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 12 eggs · 600ml water · 1200g beef mince · 600g yogurt · 120g garlic · 120g butter · 60g paprika","method":"Mix flour, egg, and water into a dough and knead until smooth. Roll thin and cut into small squares. Place a small amount of beef mince in each square. Fold into tiny parcels and seal tightly. Boil in salted water for about 8 minutes until tender. Melt butter with paprika over low heat. Mix yogurt with crushed garlic. Serve dumplings topped with yogurt and drizzled butter. Finish immediately while hot.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 55g · fat 18g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 2 days and reheat gently.","chefNotes":"Roll dough very thin for authentic texture.","pairsWith":"mint tea · cucumber salad","trivia":"Mantı are sometimes called Turkish ravioli due to their shape.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-lahmacun","name":"Lahmacun","nameAlt":"Thin flatbread with minced topping","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"flatbread","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"100g flour · 50ml water · 2g yeast · 2g salt · 80g beef mince · 30g tomato · 10g parsley · 5g olive oil","ingredients12":"1200g flour · 600ml water · 24g yeast · 24g salt · 960g beef mince · 360g tomato · 120g parsley · 60g olive oil","method":"Mix flour, water, yeast, and salt to form a soft dough. Let it rest for 10 minutes. Roll very thin into a round. Mix beef mince with finely chopped tomato, parsley, and olive oil. Spread the mixture thinly over the dough. Bake in a hot oven at 220°C for about 8 minutes. Remove when edges are crisp. Serve immediately rolled or flat. Add fresh herbs if desired.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":430,"nutrition":"protein 20g · carbs 50g · fat 15g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Bake on a preheated tray for extra crispness.","pairsWith":"lemon wedges · ayran","trivia":"Lahmacun is often called Turkish pizza but is much thinner.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-imam-bayildi","name":"İmam Bayıldı","nameAlt":"Stuffed eggplant with olive oil","aliases":["Imam bayildi"],"course":"main","type":"vegetable","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"1 eggplant · 50g onion · 50g tomato · 20ml olive oil · 5g garlic · 3g sugar · 2g salt","ingredients12":"12 eggplants · 600g onion · 600g tomato · 240ml olive oil · 60g garlic · 36g sugar · 24g salt","method":"Slice eggplant lengthwise and scoop slightly. Fry gently in olive oil until softened. Remove and set aside. Cook onion and garlic in olive oil until translucent. Add chopped tomato, sugar, and salt, and simmer for 10 minutes. Fill eggplants with the mixture. Place in a baking dish and drizzle with olive oil. Bake at 180°C for 30 minutes. Cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 4g · carbs 25g · fat 22g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days and serve cold or warm.","chefNotes":"Use ripe tomatoes for sweetness.","pairsWith":"rice · yogurt","trivia":"The name means 'the imam fainted', possibly from delight.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-menemen","name":"Menemen","nameAlt":"Scrambled eggs with tomato and pepper","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"scramble","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"breakfast","ingredients":"2 eggs · 100g tomato · 50g green pepper · 10g butter · 2g salt","ingredients12":"24 eggs · 1200g tomato · 600g green pepper · 120g butter · 24g salt","method":"Melt butter in a pan over medium heat. Add chopped green pepper and cook for 3 minutes. Add diced tomato and simmer until softened. Crack eggs into the pan without beating. Stir gently to combine while cooking. Cook until eggs are softly set, about 4 minutes. Season with salt. Serve immediately while warm. Avoid overcooking to keep creamy texture.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 10g · fat 25g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Keep eggs slightly runny for authenticity.","pairsWith":"bread · tea","trivia":"Menemen is a staple Turkish breakfast dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-pide","name":"Pide","nameAlt":"Boat-shaped Turkish flatbread","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"bread","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g flour · 80ml water · 3g yeast · 2g salt · 100g cheese · 1 egg","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 960ml water · 36g yeast · 24g salt · 1200g cheese · 12 eggs","method":"Mix flour, water, yeast, and salt into a dough. Knead until smooth and let rest for 15 minutes. Roll into an oval shape. Add cheese in the center and fold edges to form a boat. Crack egg on top. Bake at 200°C for 15 minutes until golden. Remove when edges are crisp. Let cool slightly before serving. Slice and enjoy warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 55g · fat 20g","storage":"Store in fridge for up to 2 days and reheat in oven.","chefNotes":"Use melting cheese for best texture.","pairsWith":"tea · salad","trivia":"Pide is often compared to pizza but has a unique shape.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-baklava","name":"Baklava","nameAlt":"Layered pastry with nuts and syrup","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g phyllo dough · 80g walnuts · 50g butter · 50g sugar · 50ml water · 10g honey","ingredients12":"1200g phyllo dough · 960g walnuts · 600g butter · 600g sugar · 600ml water · 120g honey","method":"Layer phyllo sheets brushing each with melted butter. Sprinkle crushed walnuts between layers. Continue layering until all used. Cut into small pieces before baking. Bake at 180°C for 30 minutes until golden. Boil sugar, water, and honey for 5 minutes. Pour syrup over hot pastry. Let soak and cool completely. Serve at room temperature.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 60g · fat 30g","storage":"Keep covered at room temperature for 3 days.","chefNotes":"Pour syrup while pastry is hot for best absorption.","pairsWith":"coffee · tea","trivia":"Baklava is one of Turkey’s most famous desserts worldwide.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-mercimek-corbasi","name":"Mercimek Çorbası","nameAlt":"Red lentil soup","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"soup","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g red lentils · 50g onion · 30g carrot · 20ml olive oil · 5g paprika · 2g salt · 500ml water","ingredients12":"1200g red lentils · 600g onion · 360g carrot · 240ml olive oil · 60g paprika · 24g salt · 6000ml water","method":"Heat olive oil in a pot over medium heat. Add chopped onion and cook until soft. Add carrot and cook for 3 minutes. Stir in lentils, paprika, salt, and water. Bring to a boil then reduce heat. Simmer for 20 minutes until lentils are soft. Blend until smooth. Serve hot.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 15g · carbs 40g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Blend well for a creamy texture.","pairsWith":"lemon · bread","trivia":"This soup is a staple in Turkish homes.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-kofte","name":"Köfte","nameAlt":"Seasoned meatballs","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"meatball","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g beef mince · 20g onion · 5g garlic · 5g cumin · 2g salt · 10ml olive oil","ingredients12":"2400g beef mince · 240g onion · 60g garlic · 60g cumin · 24g salt · 120ml olive oil","method":"Mix beef mince with grated onion, garlic, cumin, and salt. Knead mixture thoroughly. Shape into small patties or balls. Heat olive oil in a pan over medium heat. Fry köfte for about 8 minutes turning until browned. Ensure fully cooked inside. Remove and rest briefly. Serve warm.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":450,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 5g · fat 35g","storage":"Store in fridge for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let mixture rest before shaping for better texture.","pairsWith":"rice · salad","trivia":"Köfte variations exist across Turkey.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-dolma","name":"Dolma","nameAlt":"Stuffed vegetables or leaves","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stuffed","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"family","ingredients":"100g rice · 50g grape leaves · 50g onion · 20ml olive oil · 5g dill · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g rice · 600g grape leaves · 600g onion · 240ml olive oil · 60g dill · 24g salt","method":"Rinse rice thoroughly. Cook onion in olive oil until soft. Add rice, dill, and salt and cook briefly. Place filling into grape leaves and roll tightly. Arrange in a pot. Add water to cover partially. Simmer on low heat for 30 minutes. Let rest before serving. Serve warm or at room temperature.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 45g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Roll tightly to prevent unraveling.","pairsWith":"yogurt · lemon","trivia":"Dolma comes from a word meaning 'to fill'.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-simit","name":"Simit","nameAlt":"Sesame-crusted bread ring","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"150g flour · 80ml water · 3g yeast · 20g sesame seeds · 5g sugar · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g flour · 960ml water · 36g yeast · 240g sesame seeds · 60g sugar · 24g salt","method":"Mix flour, water, yeast, sugar, and salt into a dough. Knead until smooth and let rest for 20 minutes. Shape into rings. Dip in water then coat with sesame seeds. Place on a tray. Bake at 200°C for 15 minutes until golden. Cool slightly before serving. Serve fresh.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 50g · fat 6g","storage":"Best eaten same day.","chefNotes":"Toast sesame seeds lightly before coating for extra flavor.","pairsWith":"tea · cheese","trivia":"Simit is a popular Turkish street snack.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-iskender-kebap","name":"İskender Kebap","nameAlt":"Sliced döner with yogurt and sauce","aliases":["Iskender kebabı"],"course":"main","type":"kebab","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"restaurant","ingredients":"150g lamb · 50g yogurt · 50g tomato sauce · 50g bread · 10g butter","ingredients12":"1800g lamb · 600g yogurt · 600g tomato sauce · 600g bread · 120g butter","method":"Cook lamb slices on a grill until browned. Warm bread pieces and place on a plate. Arrange lamb over bread. Heat tomato sauce gently. Melt butter separately. Pour yogurt over lamb then drizzle tomato sauce and butter. Serve immediately while hot. Ensure meat stays juicy.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 40g · fat 35g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Use freshly grilled meat for best flavor.","pairsWith":"ayran · salad","trivia":"İskender Kebap is named after its creator from Bursa.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-cig-kofte","name":"Çiğ Köfte","nameAlt":"Spiced bulgur patties","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"mezze","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g fine bulgur · 20g tomato paste · 10g red pepper paste · 20ml olive oil · 10g onion · 5g cumin · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g fine bulgur · 240g tomato paste · 120g red pepper paste · 240ml olive oil · 120g onion · 60g cumin · 24g salt","method":"Place bulgur in a bowl and add a small amount of warm water to soften for 10 minutes. Add tomato paste, red pepper paste, olive oil, finely grated onion, cumin, and salt. Knead the mixture thoroughly by hand for about 10 minutes until it binds. Shape into small oval patties by squeezing in your palm. Arrange on a plate. Serve immediately with fresh greens. Keep mixture moist while shaping.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 35g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Kneading well is key to achieving the right texture.","pairsWith":"lettuce · lemon · ayran","trivia":"Originally made with raw meat, modern versions are often vegan.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-tarhana-corbasi","name":"Tarhana Çorbası","nameAlt":"Fermented grain and yogurt soup","aliases":[],"course":"starter","type":"soup","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"50g tarhana powder · 20g butter · 5g paprika · 2g salt · 400ml water","ingredients12":"600g tarhana powder · 240g butter · 60g paprika · 24g salt · 4800ml water","method":"Melt butter in a pot over medium heat. Stir in paprika and cook briefly for 1 minute. Add tarhana powder and mix well. Gradually pour in water while stirring to avoid lumps. Bring to a gentle boil. Simmer for 15 minutes, stirring occasionally. Season with salt. Serve hot with bread.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 25g · fat 10g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Whisk continuously to keep the soup smooth.","pairsWith":"bread · lemon","trivia":"Tarhana is one of the oldest preserved foods in Anatolia.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-kumpir","name":"Kumpir","nameAlt":"Loaded baked potato","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"street-food","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"1 potato · 20g butter · 30g cheese · 30g corn · 30g sausage · 10g pickles","ingredients12":"12 potatoes · 240g butter · 360g cheese · 360g corn · 360g sausage · 120g pickles","method":"Bake the potato at 200°C for about 45 minutes until soft inside. Cut open and mash the interior with butter and cheese. Mix until creamy. Add corn, sausage slices, and chopped pickles. Stir gently to combine. Return briefly to oven for 5 minutes. Serve hot.","cookTime":"50 min","kcal":650,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 70g · fat 30g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Use a large potato for better filling ratio.","pairsWith":"ayran · salad","trivia":"Kumpir is popular in Istanbul street markets.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-gozleme","name":"Gözleme","nameAlt":"Stuffed flatbread","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"flatbread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"120g flour · 60ml water · 2g salt · 80g spinach · 50g cheese · 10ml olive oil","ingredients12":"1440g flour · 720ml water · 24g salt · 960g spinach · 600g cheese · 120ml olive oil","method":"Mix flour, water, and salt into a dough and knead until smooth. Let rest for 15 minutes. Roll into thin circles. Place spinach and cheese filling on one half. Fold over and seal edges. Cook on a hot pan with olive oil for about 4 minutes per side until golden. Remove and slice. Serve warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 15g · carbs 45g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Roll dough thin for a crisp finish.","pairsWith":"tea · yogurt","trivia":"Gözleme is traditionally cooked on a griddle called a sac.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-sutlac","name":"Sütlaç","nameAlt":"Rice pudding","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pudding","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"50g rice · 400ml milk · 40g sugar · 5g vanilla · 2g cinnamon","ingredients12":"600g rice · 4800ml milk · 480g sugar · 60g vanilla · 24g cinnamon","method":"Cook rice in water until soft. Add milk and bring to a simmer over medium heat. Stir frequently to prevent sticking. Add sugar and vanilla and cook for 15 minutes. Pour into bowls. Sprinkle cinnamon on top. Bake at 180°C for 10 minutes if a browned top is desired. Cool slightly before serving.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 50g · fat 6g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Stir constantly to avoid burning the milk.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee","trivia":"Sütlaç is often served chilled or lightly baked.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-ayran","name":"Ayran","nameAlt":"Yogurt drink","aliases":[],"course":"drink","type":"beverage","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g yogurt · 100ml water · 2g salt","ingredients12":"2400g yogurt · 1200ml water · 24g salt","method":"Place yogurt in a bowl. Add water and salt. Whisk thoroughly until smooth and slightly frothy. Chill briefly if desired. Serve cold in a glass. Stir before serving. Adjust salt to taste.","cookTime":"5 min","kcal":120,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 8g · fat 6g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 1 day.","chefNotes":"Use cold water for best refreshment.","pairsWith":"kebab · pide","trivia":"Ayran is a staple drink across Turkey.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-kunefe","name":"Künefe","nameAlt":"Cheese pastry with syrup","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"pastry","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g shredded phyllo · 80g cheese · 40g butter · 50g sugar · 50ml water","ingredients12":"1200g shredded phyllo · 960g cheese · 480g butter · 600g sugar · 600ml water","method":"Melt butter and mix with shredded phyllo. Press half into a pan. Add cheese in the center. Cover with remaining phyllo. Cook on stovetop over medium heat for 10 minutes until golden. Flip carefully and cook another 8 minutes. Prepare syrup by boiling sugar and water for 5 minutes. Pour over hot pastry. Serve warm.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 15g · carbs 65g · fat 30g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Use stretchy cheese for best results.","pairsWith":"tea · pistachios","trivia":"Künefe is especially popular in southern Turkey.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-pastirma","name":"Pastırma","nameAlt":"Cured spiced beef","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"cured-meat","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"snack","ingredients":"100g beef · 10g garlic · 5g paprika · 5g cumin · 10g salt","ingredients12":"1200g beef · 120g garlic · 60g paprika · 60g cumin · 120g salt","method":"Rub beef with salt and press to cure for several days. Rinse and dry the meat thoroughly. Coat with a paste of garlic, paprika, and cumin. Hang in a cool place to dry for several days until firm. Slice thinly before serving. Serve at room temperature. Store properly after slicing.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":250,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 2g · fat 12g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Drying time takes several days and should be done in a cool place.","pairsWith":"bread · cheese","trivia":"Pastırma is similar to other cured meats like pastrami.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-zeytinyagli-fasulye","name":"Zeytinyağlı Fasulye","nameAlt":"Green beans in olive oil","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"vegetable","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"150g green beans · 50g tomato · 30g onion · 20ml olive oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g green beans · 600g tomato · 360g onion · 240ml olive oil · 24g salt","method":"Heat olive oil in a pan over medium heat. Add sliced onion and cook until soft. Add green beans and stir for 5 minutes. Add chopped tomato and salt. Pour in a small amount of water. Cover and simmer for 25 minutes until beans are tender. Let cool slightly. Serve warm or at room temperature.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":220,"nutrition":"protein 4g · carbs 20g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Cook slowly for best flavor.","pairsWith":"rice · yogurt","trivia":"Olive oil dishes are often served cold in Turkey.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-borek","name":"Börek","nameAlt":"Savory filled pastry","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"pastry","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g phyllo dough · 80g cheese · 30g spinach · 20ml milk · 1 egg","ingredients12":"1200g phyllo dough · 960g cheese · 360g spinach · 240ml milk · 12 eggs","method":"Layer phyllo sheets brushing with milk and egg mixture. Add cheese and spinach filling between layers. Continue layering until used. Cut into portions. Bake at 180°C for 30 minutes until golden. Let cool slightly. Serve warm.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 45g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overfill to prevent sogginess.","pairsWith":"tea · salad","trivia":"Börek has many regional variations across Turkey.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-hamsi-tava","name":"Hamsi Tava","nameAlt":"Fried anchovies","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"seafood","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"winter","ingredients":"150g anchovies · 30g flour · 20ml sunflower oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g anchovies · 360g flour · 240ml sunflower oil · 24g salt","method":"Clean and rinse anchovies thoroughly. Pat dry and season with salt. Coat lightly in flour. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat. Fry anchovies for about 4 minutes per side until golden and crisp. Remove and drain on paper. Serve immediately with lemon if desired.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 10g · fat 22g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Use fresh anchovies for best taste.","pairsWith":"lemon · salad","trivia":"Hamsi is especially popular along the Black Sea coast.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-revani","name":"Revani","nameAlt":"Semolina sponge cake with syrup","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cake","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"80g semolina · 50g sugar · 2 eggs · 50g yogurt · 20g butter · 50ml water","ingredients12":"960g semolina · 600g sugar · 24 eggs · 600g yogurt · 240g butter · 600ml water","method":"Beat eggs and sugar until light. Add yogurt, melted butter, and semolina. Mix until smooth. Pour into a greased pan. Bake at 180°C for 30 minutes until golden. Boil sugar and water for syrup. Pour syrup over hot cake. Let absorb and cool. Slice and serve.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 55g · fat 18g","storage":"Keep covered at room temperature for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Pour syrup evenly for consistent sweetness.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee","trivia":"Revani is popular across the former Ottoman regions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-sac-kavurma","name":"Sac Kavurma","nameAlt":"Pan-fried diced lamb","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"stir-fry","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g lamb · 50g onion · 30g green pepper · 20ml sunflower oil · 2g salt · 2g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g lamb · 600g onion · 360g green pepper · 240ml sunflower oil · 24g salt · 24g black pepper","method":"Heat sunflower oil in a wide pan over high heat. Add diced lamb and cook for about 8 minutes until browned. Stir occasionally to avoid burning. Add sliced onion and green pepper. Cook on medium heat for 6 minutes until softened. Season with salt and black pepper. Continue cooking until meat is tender. Serve hot immediately.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 8g · fat 40g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Cook on high heat first to seal in juices.","pairsWith":"flatbread · ayran","trivia":"Traditionally cooked on a large metal pan called a sac.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-tantuni","name":"Tantuni","nameAlt":"Spiced beef wrap","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"wrap","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"street-food","ingredients":"150g beef · 50g flatbread · 30g tomato · 20g onion · 10ml sunflower oil · 2g paprika · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g beef · 600g flatbread · 360g tomato · 240g onion · 120ml sunflower oil · 24g paprika · 24g salt","method":"Cook finely chopped beef in sunflower oil over medium heat for about 8 minutes. Add paprika and salt and stir well. Warm the flatbread briefly. Place beef onto bread and add chopped tomato and onion. Roll tightly into a wrap. Heat briefly on the pan for 2 minutes to crisp. Serve hot.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 40g · fat 22g","storage":"Best eaten fresh.","chefNotes":"Use very finely chopped meat for authentic texture.","pairsWith":"ayran · pickles","trivia":"Tantuni originates from the city of Mersin.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-icli-kofte","name":"İçli Köfte","nameAlt":"Stuffed bulgur croquettes","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"croquette","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"special","ingredients":"100g bulgur · 100g beef mince · 30g onion · 10g walnuts · 5g cumin · 2g salt · 20ml sunflower oil","ingredients12":"1200g bulgur · 1200g beef mince · 360g onion · 120g walnuts · 60g cumin · 24g salt · 240ml sunflower oil","method":"Soak bulgur in warm water for 10 minutes until soft. Mix with a portion of beef mince and knead into a dough. Cook remaining mince with onion, walnuts, cumin, and salt for 8 minutes. Shape bulgur dough into shells. Fill with cooked mixture and seal. Fry in hot oil at medium heat for about 6 minutes until golden. Drain and serve hot.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 45g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Seal well to prevent filling from leaking.","pairsWith":"yogurt · salad","trivia":"İçli köfte is similar to kibbeh found in Middle Eastern cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-alinazik","name":"Ali Nazik","nameAlt":"Eggplant puree with minced meat","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"meat-vegetable","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"restaurant","ingredients":"1 eggplant · 100g beef mince · 50g yogurt · 10g garlic · 10ml olive oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"12 eggplants · 1200g beef mince · 600g yogurt · 120g garlic · 120ml olive oil · 24g salt","method":"Roast eggplant at 200°C for 25 minutes until soft. Scoop flesh and mash with yogurt and garlic. Cook beef mince in olive oil over medium heat for 8 minutes until browned. Season with salt. Spread eggplant mixture on a plate. Top with hot minced meat. Serve immediately.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 12g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Roast eggplant until smoky for best flavor.","pairsWith":"flatbread · salad","trivia":"Ali Nazik originates from Gaziantep.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-tavuk-sis","name":"Tavuk Şiş","nameAlt":"Grilled chicken skewers","aliases":[],"course":"main","type":"kebab","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"barbecue","ingredients":"200g chicken · 30g yogurt · 10ml olive oil · 5g paprika · 2g salt","ingredients12":"2400g chicken · 360g yogurt · 120ml olive oil · 60g paprika · 24g salt","method":"Cut chicken into cubes and mix with yogurt, olive oil, paprika, and salt. Marinate for at least 20 minutes. Thread onto skewers. Grill over medium heat for about 12 minutes, turning occasionally. Cook until fully done and slightly charred. Remove and rest briefly. Serve hot.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 5g · fat 28g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Marinate longer for deeper flavor.","pairsWith":"rice · salad · ayran","trivia":"Şiş refers to the skewers used for grilling.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-pilav","name":"Pilav","nameAlt":"Butter rice","aliases":["Pilaf"],"course":"side","type":"rice","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g rice · 20g butter · 5g salt · 300ml water","ingredients12":"1200g rice · 240g butter · 60g salt · 3600ml water","method":"Rinse rice until water runs clear. Melt butter in a pot over medium heat. Add rice and stir for 2 minutes. Pour in water and add salt. Bring to a boil then reduce heat. Cover and cook for 15 minutes until water is absorbed. Let rest for 5 minutes before fluffing. Serve warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 55g · fat 8g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let rice rest before serving for best texture.","pairsWith":"kebab · stew","trivia":"Pilav is a staple side dish in Turkish cuisine.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-kisir","name":"Kısır","nameAlt":"Bulgur salad with herbs","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"salad","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g fine bulgur · 30g tomato paste · 20ml olive oil · 20g parsley · 10g lemon juice · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1200g fine bulgur · 360g tomato paste · 240ml olive oil · 240g parsley · 120g lemon juice · 24g salt","method":"Soak bulgur in warm water for 10 minutes until softened. Add tomato paste and mix well. Stir in olive oil, chopped parsley, lemon juice, and salt. Mix thoroughly until evenly combined. Let rest for 5 minutes to absorb flavors. Serve at room temperature.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 40g · fat 10g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use fresh parsley for bright flavor.","pairsWith":"lettuce · ayran","trivia":"Kısır is often served as part of a mezze spread.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-tursu","name":"Turşu","nameAlt":"Pickled vegetables","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"pickle","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"100g cucumber · 100ml water · 20ml vinegar · 10g garlic · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g cucumber · 1200ml water · 240ml vinegar · 120g garlic · 60g salt","method":"Wash and cut cucumbers if needed. Place in a jar with garlic. Mix water, vinegar, and salt until dissolved. Pour over vegetables to cover completely. Seal jar tightly. Let sit in a cool place for several days to pickle. Open and serve when ready.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":60,"nutrition":"protein 2g · carbs 10g · fat 0g","storage":"Keep refrigerated after opening for up to 2 weeks.","chefNotes":"Pickling takes several days for full flavor development.","pairsWith":"kebab · sandwiches","trivia":"Turşu is a common accompaniment to many Turkish dishes.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-mucver","name":"Mücver","nameAlt":"Zucchini fritters","aliases":[],"course":"side","type":"fritter","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"summer","ingredients":"150g zucchini · 1 egg · 50g flour · 10g dill · 20ml sunflower oil · 2g salt","ingredients12":"1800g zucchini · 12 eggs · 600g flour · 120g dill · 240ml sunflower oil · 24g salt","method":"Grate zucchini and squeeze out excess moisture. Mix with egg, flour, dill, and salt. Heat oil in a pan over medium heat. Spoon mixture into the pan and flatten slightly. Fry for about 4 minutes per side until golden. Remove and drain on paper. Serve warm.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":280,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 30g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Remove as much moisture as possible for crisp fritters.","pairsWith":"yogurt · salad","trivia":"Mücver is commonly served as a meze or side dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"turkey-sekerpare","name":"Şekerpare","nameAlt":"Semolina cookies in syrup","aliases":[],"course":"dessert","type":"cookie","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Turkey","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"80g flour · 40g semolina · 50g butter · 40g sugar · 1 egg · 50ml water","ingredients12":"960g flour · 480g semolina · 600g butter · 480g sugar · 12 eggs · 600ml water","method":"Mix flour, semolina, butter, sugar, and egg into a dough. Shape into small oval cookies. Place on a tray and bake at 180°C for 25 minutes until lightly golden. Boil sugar and water into syrup. Pour syrup over hot cookies. Let absorb and cool. Serve at room temperature.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 7g · carbs 55g · fat 18g","storage":"Keep covered at room temperature for 3 days.","chefNotes":"Pour syrup while cookies are hot for best absorption.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee","trivia":"Şekerpare means 'piece of sugar' in Turkish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-khachapuri","name":"ხაჭაპური","nameAlt":"Cheese-Filled Bread","aliases":["Khachapuri"],"course":"main","type":"bread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g flour · 120ml milk · 1 egg · 100g sulguni cheese · 20g butter · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1440ml milk · 12 eggs · 1200g sulguni cheese · 240g butter · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour, salt, milk, and egg to form a soft dough. Knead until smooth, about 8 minutes. Let it rest for 20 minutes at room temperature. Grate the cheese and mix lightly. Roll the dough into a round and place cheese in the center. Fold edges to seal and flatten gently. Bake at 220°C until golden, about 15 minutes. Brush with butter and serve warm.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 18g · carbs 55g · fat 22g","storage":"Store refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use a mix of mozzarella and feta if sulguni is unavailable.","pairsWith":"yogurt · tomato salad · black tea","trivia":"Khachapuri is considered Georgia’s national dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-khinkali","name":"ხინკალი","nameAlt":"Juicy Meat Dumplings","aliases":["Khinkali"],"course":"main","type":"dumpling","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g flour · 120ml water · 150g ground beef · 50g onion · 5g black pepper · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1440ml water · 1800g ground beef · 600g onion · 60g black pepper · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour and water into a firm dough and knead well. Let it rest for 30 minutes. Finely chop onion and mix with beef, salt, and pepper. Roll dough thin and cut into circles. Place filling in the center and gather edges into a pouch. Boil in salted water on high heat until they float, about 10 minutes. Serve hot with black pepper.","cookTime":"50 min","kcal":480,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 45g · fat 18g","storage":"Refrigerate cooked dumplings for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overfill or dumplings may burst during boiling.","pairsWith":"beer · black pepper · fresh herbs","trivia":"Khinkali are eaten by hand, holding the top knot.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-lobio","name":"ლობიო","nameAlt":"Bean Stew","aliases":["Lobio"],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g red kidney beans · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 5g coriander · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g red kidney beans · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 60g coriander · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt","method":"Soak beans overnight and drain. Boil in fresh water on medium heat until tender, about 60 minutes. Chop onion and garlic finely. Fry onion in oil until soft, about 5 minutes. Add garlic and coriander, cooking briefly. Mix in beans and simmer for 10 minutes. Mash slightly for texture and serve warm.","cookTime":"75 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 15g · carbs 50g · fat 8g","storage":"Store in the fridge for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Add a splash of vinegar for brightness.","pairsWith":"cornbread · pickles · red wine","trivia":"Lobio varies widely across Georgian regions.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-badrijani-nigvzit","name":"ბადრიჯანი ნიგვზით","nameAlt":"Eggplant with Walnut Paste","aliases":["Badrijani Nigvzit"],"course":"starter","type":"vegetable","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g eggplant · 80g walnuts · 10g garlic · 5g coriander · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g eggplant · 960g walnuts · 120g garlic · 60g coriander · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt","method":"Slice eggplant lengthwise and sprinkle with salt. Let sit for 15 minutes, then pat dry. Fry slices in oil on medium heat until golden, about 4 minutes per side. Grind walnuts with garlic and coriander into a paste. Spread walnut mixture on eggplant slices. Roll each slice and arrange on a plate. Chill slightly before serving.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 20g · fat 32g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use fresh walnuts for best flavor.","pairsWith":"pomegranate seeds · bread · white wine","trivia":"Walnuts are central to many Georgian dishes.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-chakhokhbili","name":"ჩახოხბილი","nameAlt":"Chicken Tomato Stew","aliases":["Chakhokhbili"],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g chicken · 150g tomato · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 5g coriander · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g chicken · 1800g tomato · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 60g coriander · 60g salt","method":"Cut chicken into pieces and brown in a pan on medium heat, about 8 minutes. Chop onions and add to the pan. Cook until softened, about 5 minutes. Add chopped tomatoes and garlic. Simmer on low heat for 25 minutes until tender. Stir in coriander and season. Serve hot.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":430,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 12g · fat 30g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use ripe tomatoes for better flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · rice · red wine","trivia":"Originally made with pheasant, now chicken is common.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-pkhali","name":"ფხალი","nameAlt":"Vegetable Walnut Spread","aliases":["Pkhali"],"course":"starter","type":"spread","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"150g spinach · 80g walnuts · 10g garlic · 5g coriander · 5ml vinegar · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g spinach · 960g walnuts · 120g garlic · 60g coriander · 60ml vinegar · 60g salt","method":"Boil spinach in water on medium heat for 3 minutes. Drain and squeeze out excess water. Grind walnuts with garlic and coriander. Mix spinach with walnut paste. Add vinegar and salt, mixing well. Shape into small balls or serve as a spread. Chill slightly before serving.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 9g · carbs 10g · fat 25g","storage":"Keep refrigerated for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Try with beetroot or eggplant variations.","pairsWith":"bread · wine · herbs","trivia":"Pkhali is served in colorful assortments.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-mtsvadi","name":"მწვადი","nameAlt":"Grilled Meat Skewers","aliases":["Mtsvadi"],"course":"main","type":"grill","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g pork · 50g onion · 5g black pepper · 5g salt · 10ml sunflower oil","ingredients12":"2400g pork · 600g onion · 60g black pepper · 60g salt · 120ml sunflower oil","method":"Cut pork into chunks and season with salt and pepper. Slice onion and mix with meat. Let marinate for 30 minutes. Thread onto skewers. Grill over medium heat until browned, about 12 minutes. Turn occasionally for even cooking. Serve hot.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":550,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 5g · fat 45g","storage":"Refrigerate leftovers for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use charcoal for authentic smoky flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · onions · red wine","trivia":"Mtsvadi is a staple at Georgian feasts.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-satsivi","name":"საცივი","nameAlt":"Chicken in Walnut Sauce","aliases":["Satsivi"],"course":"main","type":"sauce","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"Christmas","ingredients":"200g chicken · 100g walnuts · 10g garlic · 5g coriander · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g chicken · 1200g walnuts · 120g garlic · 60g coriander · 60g salt","method":"Boil chicken in water on medium heat until cooked, about 25 minutes. Remove and cool slightly. Grind walnuts with garlic and coriander. Add some broth to make a smooth sauce. Cut chicken and mix with sauce. Simmer gently for 10 minutes. Serve cooled or at room temperature.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":500,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 10g · fat 40g","storage":"Keep refrigerated up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Serve chilled for authentic style.","pairsWith":"bread · wine · herbs","trivia":"Satsivi is a festive Georgian dish.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-acha-puri","name":"აჭარული ხაჭაპური","nameAlt":"Boat-Shaped Cheese Bread with Egg","aliases":["Adjaruli Khachapuri"],"course":"main","type":"bread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g flour · 120ml milk · 1 egg · 120g cheese · 20g butter · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1440ml milk · 12 eggs · 1440g cheese · 240g butter · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour, milk, and salt into dough. Knead until smooth and let rest 20 minutes. Roll into oval and shape into a boat. Fill with cheese and bake at 220°C for 15 minutes. Crack an egg into the center and bake 3 more minutes. Add butter on top before serving.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 55g · fat 30g","storage":"Best eaten fresh but can be refrigerated for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Mix the egg into the cheese before eating.","pairsWith":"tea · salad · yogurt","trivia":"This version comes from the Adjara region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-tkemali","name":"ტყემალი","nameAlt":"Sour Plum Sauce","aliases":["Tkemali"],"course":"side","type":"sauce","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g sour plums · 10g garlic · 5g coriander · 5g dill · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g sour plums · 120g garlic · 60g coriander · 60g dill · 60g salt","method":"Boil plums in water on medium heat until soft, about 10 minutes. Drain and mash to remove pits. Add crushed garlic, coriander, and dill. Simmer for 10 minutes until thickened. Season with salt. Cool before serving.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":120,"nutrition":"protein 2g · carbs 25g · fat 1g","storage":"Store refrigerated up to 1 week.","chefNotes":"Adjust sourness with a pinch of sugar if needed.","pairsWith":"grilled meat · bread · potatoes","trivia":"Tkemali is a staple Georgian condiment.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-elarji","name":"ელარჯი","nameAlt":"Cornmeal and Cheese Mash","aliases":["Elarji"],"course":"side","type":"porridge","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"150g cornmeal · 100g cheese · 300ml water · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g cornmeal · 1200g cheese · 3600ml water · 60g salt","method":"Boil water with salt on medium heat. Add cornmeal slowly, stirring constantly. Cook until thick, about 10 minutes. Add cheese and stir until melted and stretchy. Continue stirring until smooth. Serve hot.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":400,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 50g · fat 15g","storage":"Best eaten fresh; refrigerate up to 1 day.","chefNotes":"Stir constantly to prevent lumps.","pairsWith":"stew · herbs · wine","trivia":"Elarji is especially popular in western Georgia.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-churchkhela","name":"ჩურჩხელა","nameAlt":"Walnut Grape Candy","aliases":["Churchkhela"],"course":"dessert","type":"candy","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"150g walnuts · 300ml grape juice · 50g flour · 10g sugar","ingredients12":"1800g walnuts · 3600ml grape juice · 600g flour · 120g sugar","method":"Thread walnuts onto string. Heat grape juice with sugar on medium heat. Mix flour with a little juice and add to thicken. Cook until thick, about 10 minutes. Dip walnut strings into mixture. Hang to dry until firm, about several hours. Repeat dipping for thicker coating. Serve when set.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 8g · carbs 45g · fat 18g","storage":"Store in a cool dry place for up to 2 weeks.","chefNotes":"Drying time is several days for best texture.","pairsWith":"tea · coffee · wine","trivia":"Often called the Georgian Snickers.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-chakapuli","name":"ჩაქაფული","nameAlt":"Herbed Lamb and Tarragon Stew","aliases":["Chakapuli"],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g lamb · 50g onion · 20g tarragon · 100g green plums · 10g garlic · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g lamb · 600g onion · 240g tarragon · 1200g green plums · 120g garlic · 60g salt","method":"Cut lamb into chunks and place in a pot. Chop onion and garlic and add to the pot. Add plums and half the tarragon. Pour in a little water and simmer on low heat for 60 minutes. Stir occasionally until meat is tender. Add remaining tarragon and cook 10 more minutes. Season and serve hot.","cookTime":"75 min","kcal":460,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 10g · fat 35g","storage":"Refrigerate for up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use sour plums for authentic flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · white wine · herbs","trivia":"Chakapuli is popular during spring festivals.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-odjakhuri","name":"ოჯახური","nameAlt":"Family-Style Fried Meat and Potatoes","aliases":["Ojakhuri"],"course":"main","type":"fry","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g pork · 200g potatoes · 50g onion · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt · 5g black pepper","ingredients12":"2400g pork · 2400g potatoes · 600g onion · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt · 60g black pepper","method":"Cut pork and potatoes into chunks. Fry potatoes in oil on medium heat until golden, about 10 minutes. Remove and set aside. Fry pork in the same pan until browned, about 8 minutes. Add sliced onion and cook until soft. Return potatoes to the pan and mix well. Season and cook together for 5 minutes. Serve hot.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":600,"nutrition":"protein 25g · carbs 40g · fat 38g","storage":"Store refrigerated up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Cook in a clay pan for traditional presentation.","pairsWith":"pickles · bread · beer","trivia":"Ojakhuri means 'family-style' in Georgian.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-ajapsandali","name":"აჯაფსანდალი","nameAlt":"Georgian Vegetable Stew","aliases":["Ajapsandali"],"course":"main","type":"stew","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g eggplant · 100g tomato · 50g bell pepper · 50g onion · 10g garlic · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g eggplant · 1200g tomato · 600g bell pepper · 600g onion · 120g garlic · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt","method":"Chop all vegetables into chunks. Fry eggplant in oil on medium heat until softened, about 6 minutes. Remove and set aside. In the same pan, cook onion and bell pepper until soft. Add tomatoes and garlic and simmer for 10 minutes. Return eggplant and mix well. Cook together for another 10 minutes. Season and serve warm.","cookTime":"35 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 5g · carbs 30g · fat 14g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Let it rest before serving for deeper flavor.","pairsWith":"bread · herbs · red wine","trivia":"Ajapsandali is similar to ratatouille.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-gomi","name":"ღომი","nameAlt":"Cornmeal Porridge","aliases":["Gomi"],"course":"side","type":"porridge","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g cornmeal · 400ml water · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g cornmeal · 4800ml water · 60g salt","method":"Bring water and salt to a boil on medium heat. Add cornmeal gradually while stirring constantly. Cook until thick and smooth, about 15 minutes. Continue stirring to avoid lumps. Remove from heat and serve hot.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":300,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 60g · fat 2g","storage":"Best fresh; refrigerate for 1 day.","chefNotes":"Serve with cheese for richer taste.","pairsWith":"cheese · stew · herbs","trivia":"Gomi is a staple in western Georgia.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-kubdari","name":"კუბდარი","nameAlt":"Spiced Meat Bread","aliases":["Kubdari"],"course":"main","type":"bread","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g flour · 120ml water · 150g beef · 50g onion · 5g black pepper · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g flour · 1440ml water · 1800g beef · 600g onion · 60g black pepper · 60g salt","method":"Mix flour, water, and salt into dough and knead well. Let rest for 20 minutes. Chop beef and onion finely and season. Roll dough into a round and place filling inside. Seal edges and flatten gently. Bake at 200°C for 20 minutes until golden. Serve hot.","cookTime":"40 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 22g · carbs 50g · fat 20g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use fatty beef for juicier filling.","pairsWith":"yogurt · tea · herbs","trivia":"Kubdari comes from the Svaneti region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-nadugi","name":"ნადუღი","nameAlt":"Fresh Whey Cheese Spread","aliases":["Nadughi"],"course":"starter","type":"spread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g whey cheese · 10g mint · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g whey cheese · 120g mint · 60g salt","method":"Place whey cheese in a bowl. Finely chop mint and add to the cheese. Mix until smooth and creamy. Season with salt. Serve chilled or at room temperature.","cookTime":"10 min","kcal":180,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 5g · fat 12g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Wrap in thin cheese slices for traditional serving.","pairsWith":"bread · herbs · wine","trivia":"Nadugi is often served in rolled sulguni slices.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-shkmeruli","name":"შქმერული","nameAlt":"Garlic Chicken in Milk Sauce","aliases":["Shkmeruli"],"course":"main","type":"roast","diet":"omnivore","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"200g chicken · 150ml milk · 15g garlic · 20g butter · 5g salt","ingredients12":"2400g chicken · 1800ml milk · 180g garlic · 240g butter · 60g salt","method":"Roast chicken pieces at 200°C until golden, about 25 minutes. Melt butter in a pan on medium heat. Add crushed garlic and cook briefly. Pour in milk and simmer for 5 minutes. Add roasted chicken to the sauce. Simmer together for 10 minutes. Serve hot.","cookTime":"45 min","kcal":520,"nutrition":"protein 30g · carbs 8g · fat 40g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use plenty of garlic for authentic taste.","pairsWith":"bread · potatoes · white wine","trivia":"Shkmeruli originates from the Racha region.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-chvishtari","name":"ჭვიშტარი","nameAlt":"Cornbread with Cheese","aliases":["Chvishtari"],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g cornmeal · 100g cheese · 100ml water · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1800g cornmeal · 1200g cheese · 1200ml water · 60g salt","method":"Mix cornmeal, water, and salt into a thick batter. Add grated cheese and mix well. Shape into small patties. Fry in a pan on medium heat until golden, about 4 minutes per side. Serve warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":380,"nutrition":"protein 12g · carbs 45g · fat 18g","storage":"Store refrigerated for 2 days.","chefNotes":"Use sulguni cheese for best results.","pairsWith":"stew · yogurt · herbs","trivia":"Chvishtari is a western Georgian favorite.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-kalmakhi","name":"კალმახი","nameAlt":"Grilled Trout","aliases":["Kalmakhi"],"course":"main","type":"grill","diet":"pescatarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200g trout · 10ml sunflower oil · 5g salt · 5g black pepper · 10g lemon","ingredients12":"2400g trout · 120ml sunflower oil · 60g salt · 60g black pepper · 120g lemon","method":"Clean and pat dry the trout. Rub with oil, salt, and pepper. Grill on medium heat until cooked through, about 10 minutes per side. Squeeze lemon juice over before serving. Serve hot.","cookTime":"25 min","kcal":350,"nutrition":"protein 28g · carbs 2g · fat 25g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Do not overcook to keep fish moist.","pairsWith":"herbs · potatoes · white wine","trivia":"Trout is common in Georgian mountain rivers.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-bazhe","name":"ბაჟე","nameAlt":"Walnut Garlic Sauce","aliases":["Bazhe"],"course":"side","type":"sauce","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"festival","ingredients":"100g walnuts · 10g garlic · 5g coriander · 100ml water · 5g salt","ingredients12":"1200g walnuts · 120g garlic · 60g coriander · 1200ml water · 60g salt","method":"Grind walnuts into a fine paste. Crush garlic and mix into walnuts. Add coriander and salt. Gradually add water while stirring to create a smooth sauce. Serve at room temperature.","cookTime":"15 min","kcal":420,"nutrition":"protein 10g · carbs 12g · fat 38g","storage":"Refrigerate up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Adjust thickness with water as needed.","pairsWith":"chicken · vegetables · bread","trivia":"Bazhe is often served with poultry dishes.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-sulguni","name":"სულგუნი","nameAlt":"Georgian Brined Cheese","aliases":["Sulguni"],"course":"side","type":"cheese","diet":"vegetarian","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"200ml milk · 5g salt · 5ml vinegar","ingredients12":"2400ml milk · 60g salt · 60ml vinegar","method":"Heat milk on medium until warm but not boiling. Add vinegar and stir until curds form. Strain curds and press gently. Shape into a round and salt lightly. Let rest for 30 minutes before serving.","cookTime":"30 min","kcal":260,"nutrition":"protein 16g · carbs 5g · fat 20g","storage":"Keep refrigerated up to 3 days.","chefNotes":"Use full-fat milk for better texture.","pairsWith":"bread · wine · herbs","trivia":"Sulguni is known for its stretchy texture.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""},
{"id":"georgia-mchadi","name":"მჭადი","nameAlt":"Georgian Cornbread","aliases":["Mchadi"],"course":"side","type":"bread","diet":"vegan","cuisine":"eastern-europe","country":"Georgia","occasion":"everyday","ingredients":"150g cornmeal · 120ml water · 5g salt · 10ml sunflower oil","ingredients12":"1800g cornmeal · 1440ml water · 60g salt · 120ml sunflower oil","method":"Mix cornmeal, water, and salt into a firm dough. Shape into small flat rounds. Heat oil in a pan on medium heat. Fry rounds until golden, about 4 minutes per side. Serve warm.","cookTime":"20 min","kcal":320,"nutrition":"protein 6g · carbs 55g · fat 10g","storage":"Store in an airtight container for up to 2 days.","chefNotes":"Serve hot for best texture.","pairsWith":"beans · cheese · herbs","trivia":"Mchadi is a staple bread in Georgia.","howThisFeels":"","servings":1,"sharedWith":""}
